window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-chabashira-sae"]=[{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p29-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae class 1 d homeroom orientation   point system trap japanese history  class d homeroom for three years  class 1 d classroom  entrance day morning  the first bell rings  chabashira enters briskly  early thirties  hair pulled back into a ponytail  sharply dressed in a tailored business suit  exuding strict professionalism with zero warmth  distributes the official student handbook and guidelines without smiling   ahem  good morning to you  students  i m the instructor for class d  my name is chiyabashira sae  i usually teach japanese history  however  at this school  we do not change classrooms for each grade  for the next three years  i will be acting as your homeroom teacher  so i hope to get to know all of you  it s a pleasure to meet you   the entrance ceremony will be in the gymnasium one hour from now  but first  i will distribute written materials with information about this school s special rules  i will also hand out the admissions guide  institutional isolation  complete boarding school structure  students are required to live in campus dormitories and are strictly prohibited from leaving campus or contacting anyone in the outside world  including family and friends  without explicit administrative approval  s system economy  points as universal currency   i will now hand out your student id cards  by using your card  you can access any of the facilities on campus  purchase goods from the store  and so on  it acts like a credit card  however  it is imperative that you pay attention to the points that you spend  at this school  you can use your points to buy anything  anything located on the school premises is available for purchase   your student cards can be used simply by swiping them through the machine scanner  the method is simple  so you shouldn t get confused  points are automatically deposited into your account on the first of every month  you should all have received 100 000 points already  keep in mind that one point is worth one yen  no further explanation should be necessary  hands out campus student id cards that act as currency cards  s system  students confirm their initial balance of 100 000 points   shocked by the amount of points you ve been given  this school evaluates its students  talents  everyone here has passed the entrance examination  which itself speaks to your value and potential  the amount you ve received reflects the evaluation of your worth  you can use your points without restraint   after graduation  however  all of your points return to the school  because it s impossible to exchange your points for cash  there s no advantage to saving them  once points have been deposited into your account  it s up to you how to spend them  do as you like   in the event that you don t want to spend your points  you may transfer them to someone else  however  extorting money from your peers is not allowed  this school monitors bullying very carefully  immediately packs up her materials  delivers a perfunctory closing  and walks out the door  abandoning the class to celebrate their windfall  calculated omission  speaks with legalistic  literal truth while deliberately concealing the hidden trap never mentions class points  monthly evaluation deductions  absenteeism penalties  or the true meaning of class d  entices students into financial complacency  flat  dispassionate  strictly informative  formal school administrative tone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Class 1-D homeroom orientation &amp; point system trap<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.29–32<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom, entrance day morning. The first bell rings. Chabashira enters briskly. Early thirties, hair pulled back into a ponytail, sharply dressed in a tailored business suit, exuding strict professionalism with zero warmth.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ahem. Good morning to you, students. I’m the instructor for Class D. My name is Chiyabashira Sae. I usually teach Japanese history. However, at this school, we do not change classrooms for each grade. For the next three years, I…”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The entrance ceremony will be in the gymnasium one hour from now, but first, I will distribute written materials with information about this school’s special rules. I will also hand out the admissions guide.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I will now hand out your student ID cards. By using your card, you can access any of the facilities on campus, purchase goods from the store, and so on. It acts like a credit card. However, it is imperative that you pay…”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Japanese history; Class D homeroom for three years.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Distributes the official student handbook and guidelines without smiling.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ahem. Good morning to you, students. I’m the instructor for Class D. My name is Chiyabashira Sae. I usually teach Japanese history. However, at this school, we do not change classrooms for each grade. For the next three years, I will be acting as your homeroom teacher, so I hope to get to know all of you. It’s a pleasure to meet you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Institutional isolation: complete boarding school structure. Students are required to live in campus dormitories and are strictly prohibited from leaving campus or contacting anyone in the outside world (including family and friends) without explicit administrative approval.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> S-System economy: points as universal currency.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will now hand out your student ID cards. By using your card, you can access any of the facilities on campus, purchase goods from the store, and so on. It acts like a credit card. However, it is imperative that you pay attention to the points that you spend. At this school, you can use your points to buy anything. Anything located on the school premises is available for purchase.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your student cards can be used simply by swiping them through the machine scanner. The method is simple, so you shouldn’t get confused. Points are automatically deposited into your account on the first of every month. You should all have received 100,000 points already. Keep in mind that one point is worth one yen. No further explanation should be necessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands out campus student ID cards that act as currency cards (S-System); students confirm their initial balance of 100,000 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shocked by the amount of points you’ve been given? This school evaluates its students’ talents. Everyone here has passed the entrance examination, which itself speaks to your value and potential. The amount you’ve received reflects the evaluation of your worth. You can use your points without restraint.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After graduation, however, all of your points return to the school. Because it’s impossible to exchange your points for cash, there’s no advantage to saving them. Once points have been deposited into your account, it’s up to you how to spend them. Do as you like.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the event that you don’t want to spend your points, you may transfer them to someone else. However, extorting money from your peers is not allowed. This school monitors bullying very carefully.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Immediately packs up her materials, delivers a perfunctory closing, and walks out the door, abandoning the class to celebrate their windfall.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calculated omission: speaks with legalistic, literal truth while deliberately concealing the hidden trap—never mentions Class Points, monthly evaluation deductions, absenteeism penalties, or the true meaning of Class D. Entices students into financial complacency.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Flat, dispassionate, strictly informative, formal school administrative tone.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p104-1\">→ After: The deceptive April short test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p104-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the deceptive april short test classroom 1 d  late april  third period  japanese history  enters the rowdy classroom where students are chatting  calling her  sae chan sensei   quiet down a little  please  today s lesson will be a bit serious   it s the end of the month  so we re going to have a short test  please pass these to the back   don t say that  this test is just for future reference  it won t be reflected in your report cards  there is no risk involved  so don t worry  of course  cheating is prohibited  deceptive testing design  administers a 5 subject short diagnostic test  claims it has zero risk and does not impact report cards  yet the questions are split between elementary level basics and absurdly advanced university tier final problems  uses this unannounced test as a covert diagnostic of students  true academic baselines  master of institutional misdirection  allows students to take the exam casually while secretly logging their actual abilities","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p104-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The deceptive April short test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.104–106<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, late April (third period, Japanese History).<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Quiet down a little, please. Today’s lesson will be a bit serious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s the end of the month, so we’re going to have a short test. Please pass these to the back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t say that. This test is just for future reference. It won’t be reflected in your report cards. There is no risk involved, so don’t worry. Of course, cheating is prohibited.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Enters the rowdy classroom where students are chatting, calling her &quot;Sae-chan-sensei&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Deceptive testing design: administers a 5-subject short diagnostic test. Claims it has zero risk and does not impact report cards, yet the questions are split between elementary-level basics and absurdly advanced university-tier final problems. Uses this unannounced test as a covert diagnostic of students&#x27; true academic baselines.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Master of institutional misdirection; allows students to take the exam casually while secretly logging their actual abilities.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p29-1\">← Before: Class 1-D homeroom orientation &amp; point system trap<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p120-1\">→ After: May 1st homeroom: The 0-point revelation &amp; S-System truth<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p120-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae may 1st homeroom  the 0 point revelation   s system truth classroom 1 d  may 1st morning homeroom  strides into class holding a rolled up poster with a severe  cold expression  completely ignores ike s crude menopause joke   all right  your morning homeroom is about to begin  before we get started  does anyone have any questions  if so  now is the time to speak   hondou  i already explained this before  didn t i  points are deposited on the first day of the month  i ve confirmed that points were wired this month without any issues   are you kids really that dumb   sit down  hondou  i ll explain once more  points were deposited  that much i know for certain  there is absolutely no chance that we forgot about anyone in this class  to think so is ludicrous  understood  chuckles when koenji deduces that class d received zero points   while he certainly has an attitude problem  kouenji is exactly right  for crying out loud  barely anyone seems to have noticed the hint i gave you  how deplorable  delivers the devastating statistical breakdown of class d s april conduct   a total of ninety eight absences and late arrivals  three hundred ninety one incidences of talking or using a cell phone in class  that is quite a few infractions over one month  in this school  your class s results are reflected in the points that you receive  as a result  you wasted all of the 100 000 points that you should have received  that s what happened   i should have explained this all to you on the day of the entrance ceremony  this school measures its students  true abilities  this time  you were evaluated as being worth nothing  that s all  completely shreds hirata s objection that the rules were never explained beforehand   that is a rather bizarre argument  hirata  it is certainly true that i don t recall explaining the rules of point distribution  however  didn t you all learn in elementary school not to be late or talk in class  was that not taught throughout your elementary and junior high schools   i m sure that in nine years of compulsory education  you learned that being late and talking in class are bad things  and now you say that you can t understand this because i haven t explained it to you  i m afraid your reasoning is flimsy  if you had simply acted properly  then your points would not have dropped all the way to zero  this comes down to you taking personal responsibility   having just entered your first year of high school  did you honestly think you d receive 100 000 points every month with no strings attached  at a school established by the japanese government for the express purposes of training gifted people  that s unthinkable  try using some common sense  why would you leave it to chance   i cannot tell you  we cannot disclose the methods behind our student evaluation  it s the same as any other organization  when you enter a company  it is the company s choice whether or not to tell you how it evaluates its employees  however  i m not cruel  and i m not trying to be cold  in fact  this situation is so pathetic that i will give you one bit of guidance   let s say that you stop being late to class and have no more absences  even though zero points will be deducted from you this month  that doesn t mean that your points will increase  either  that means next month you will still receive zero points  from another perspective  you could say no matter how times you re late or absent to class  it doesn t matter  so  you re not really at a loss  are you  unfurls the class ranking poster on the blackboard  class a  940  class b  650  class c  490  class d  0   look here  morons  every other class got points  the amount of points we gave you for the first month should be plenty for you to live on   in this school  students are sorted by their level of excellence  the superior students are sorted into class a  the least capable in class d  it s the same system you d find in the major cram schools  in other words  class d is akin to the last bastion for failures  you are the worst of the worst  you re defective  this is just the result of you being defective  claps mockingly at their ruinous indulgence   however  i have to say  this year s class d was the first to ever spend all of their points in a single month  i am impressed by how much you indulged yourselves  wonderful  just wonderful   yes  you will remain at zero until you graduate  but don t worry  you can still have a room in the dorms and free meals  you won t die   what  you re still worried about your dignity  sudou  well then  work to make your class into the best one  your class s points aren t just linked to the amount of money that you receive each month  they re also indicative of your class rank  posts the short test score roster on the blackboard  exposes that 7 students would have been expelled had it been a formal exam   judging from these  i can see that we ve quite a few idiots in this class  these are the results of the short test you took a while ago  your sensei was so happy after your excellent performance  come on  what in the world did you all study when you were in junior high   i m so glad  if this were an actual test  then seven of you would ve had to drop out  red line expulsion rule  failing  scoring below the cutoff  on a midterm or final exam results in immediate expulsion from advanced nurturing high school  class a monopoly on privilege  the school s advertised 100  employment and college matriculation rate applies strictly and exclusively to graduates of  class a  classes b  c  and d receive zero guaranteed placement   oh  what  did i not explain this to you  if you fail on a midterm or final exam in this school  then you have to drop out  if we applied that rule to this test  anyone who scored below thirty two points would be out  you guys really are stupid  aren t you   however  nothing comes easy in this world  mediocre people such as yourselves would have to be naive to think that you could easily get into the college or workplace of your choice   you re wrong  to make your dreams of a bright future come true  your only option is to overtake class a  this school guarantees nothing for any other students   it looks like your bubbles have been burst  if you had simply understood the harsh reality of the situation from the start  then this long homeroom period might have meant something  your midterm exams are in three weeks  please think things over  and be careful not to drop out  ruthless institutional educator  uses cold psychological shock and mockery to shatter student illusions  revels in puncturing their sense of unearned privilege","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">May 1st homeroom: The 0-point revelation &amp; S-System truth<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.120–130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, May 1st morning homeroom.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“All right, your morning homeroom is about to begin. Before we get started, does anyone have any questions? If so, now is the time to speak.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hondou, I already explained this before, didn’t I? Points are deposited on the first day of the month. I’ve confirmed that points were wired this month without any issues.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you kids really that dumb?”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>30 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Strides into class holding a rolled-up poster with a severe, cold expression; completely ignores Ike’s crude menopause joke.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sit down, Hondou. I’ll explain once more… Points were deposited. That much I know for certain. There is absolutely no chance that we forgot about anyone in this class. To think so is ludicrous. Understood?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Chuckles when Kōenji deduces that Class D received zero points.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “While he certainly has an attitude problem, Kouenji is exactly right. For crying out loud, barely anyone seems to have noticed the hint I gave you. How deplorable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Delivers the devastating statistical breakdown of Class D&#x27;s April conduct.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A total of ninety-eight absences and late arrivals. Three hundred ninety-one incidences of talking or using a cell phone in class. That is quite a few infractions over one month. In this school, your class’s results are reflected in the points that you receive. As a result, you wasted all of the 100,000 points that you should have received. That’s what happened.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should have explained this all to you on the day of the entrance ceremony. This school measures its students’ true abilities. This time, you were evaluated as being worth nothing. That’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Completely shreds Hirata’s objection that the rules were never explained beforehand.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That is a rather bizarre argument, Hirata. It is certainly true that I don’t recall explaining the rules of point distribution. However, didn’t you all learn in elementary school not to be late or talk in class? Was that not taught throughout your elementary and junior high schools?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sure that in nine years of compulsory education, you learned that being late and talking in class are bad things. And now you say that you can’t understand this because I haven’t explained it to you? I’m afraid your reasoning is flimsy. If you had simply acted properly, then your points would not have dropped all the way to zero. This comes down to you taking personal responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Having just entered your first year of high school, did you honestly think you’d receive 100,000 points every month with no strings attached? At a school established by the Japanese government for the express purposes of training gifted people? That’s unthinkable. Try using some common sense. Why would you leave it to chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I cannot tell you. We cannot disclose the methods behind our student evaluation. It’s the same as any other organization. When you enter a company, it is the company’s choice whether or not to tell you how it evaluates its employees. However, I’m not cruel, and I’m not trying to be cold. In fact, this situation is so pathetic that I will give you one bit of guidance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s say that you stop being late to class and have no more absences… Even though zero points will be deducted from you this month, that doesn’t mean that your points will increase, either. That means next month you will still receive zero points. From another perspective, you could say no matter how times you’re late or absent to class, it doesn’t matter. So, you’re not really at a loss, are you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Unfurls the class ranking poster on the blackboard: Class A (940), Class B (650), Class C (490), Class D (0).<span class=\"pg\">p.125–126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Look here, morons. Every other class got points. The amount of points we gave you for the first month should be plenty for you to live on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this school, students are sorted by their level of excellence. The superior students are sorted into Class A, the least capable in Class D. It’s the same system you’d find in the major cram schools. In other words, Class D is akin to the last bastion for failures. You are the worst of the worst. You’re defective. This is just the result of you being defective.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Claps mockingly at their ruinous indulgence.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, I have to say, this year’s Class D was the first to ever spend all of their points in a single month. I am impressed by how much you indulged yourselves. Wonderful, just wonderful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. You will remain at zero until you graduate. But don’t worry, you can still have a room in the dorms and free meals. You won’t die.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? You’re still worried about your dignity, Sudou? Well then, work to make your class into the best one… Your class’s points aren’t just linked to the amount of money that you receive each month. They’re also indicative of your class rank.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Posts the short test score roster on the blackboard; exposes that 7 students would have been expelled had it been a formal exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Judging from these, I can see that we’ve quite a few idiots in this class… These are the results of the short test you took a while ago. Your sensei was so happy after your excellent performance. Come on, what in the world did you all study when you were in junior high?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127–128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m so glad. If this were an actual test, then seven of you would’ve had to drop out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Red-line expulsion rule: failing (scoring below the cutoff) on a midterm or final exam results in immediate expulsion from Advanced Nurturing High School.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Class A monopoly on privilege: the school&#x27;s advertised 100% employment and college matriculation rate applies strictly and exclusively to graduates of **Class A**. Classes B, C, and D receive zero guaranteed placement.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, what, did I not explain this to you? If you fail on a midterm or final exam in this school, then you have to drop out. If we applied that rule to this test, anyone who scored below thirty-two points would be out. You guys really are stupid, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, nothing comes easy in this world. Mediocre people such as yourselves would have to be naive to think that you could easily get into the college or workplace of your choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re wrong. To make your dreams of a bright future come true, your only option is to overtake Class A. This school guarantees nothing for any other students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It looks like your bubbles have been burst. If you had simply understood the harsh reality of the situation from the start, then this long homeroom period might have meant something. Your midterm exams are in three weeks. Please think things over, and be careful not to drop out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ruthless institutional educator; uses cold psychological shock and mockery to shatter student illusions; revels in puncturing their sense of unearned privilege.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p104-1\">← Before: The deceptive April short test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p140-1\">→ After: Guidance office trap &amp; exposing Ayanokōji&#x27;s 50s<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p140-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae guidance office trap   exposing ayanokoji s 50s hallway outside staff room  then guidance office  catches class 1 b homeroom teacher hoshinomiya chie flirting with ayanokoji  hits her firmly over the head and on the butt with her clipboard to chase her away   for getting involved with one of my students   it would have been better if you just left him alone  thanks for waiting  ayanokouji  let s go into the office  summons ayanokoji into the guidance office kitchen  turns on the kettle to make green tea  and orders him into hiding behind closed doors under penalty of expulsion  anticipating horikita s protest   don t make any unnecessary moves  shut up and get in here  understand  don t make a sound and stay until i tell you it s okay to come out  if you don t do as i say  you ll be expelled  receives horikita suzune  calmly confronts her academic arrogance with cutting social philosophy   i m an instructor  i understand the mind of a student  at least to some degree  horikita suzune  just as you said  you did well on the entrance examination  you had the third highest test score among the first year students and were close to the highest  and second highest scoring students  you did exceedingly well  and you re right  we found no particular problems in your interview  on the contrary  we evaluated you quite highly   incorrect evaluation  perhaps your self evaluation is far too high  i acknowledge that your academic ability is excellent  you re certainly very smart  however  who decided that smart people are categorically superior  we never said that   common sense  didn t common sense create our current  flawed society  before  japan relied solely on test scores to separate the superior and inferior  as a result  the incompetents at the top tried desperately to kick down the truly superior students  in the end  we settled on a system of hereditary succession   you re a capable student  i don t deny that  however  this school s goal is to produce superior people  if you believe academics alone place you into a higher class  you are mistaken  that was the very first thing we explained to you  besides  think rationally  would we have admitted someone like sudou if we decided superiority based solely on academic merit   there are some students who are happy to be incorrectly evaluated at a lower level  strange students who would happily be set at a low level   i m sorry  but you weren t sorted by mistake  you are definitely in class d  you are at that level  opens the kitchen door and presents ayanokoji to horikita along with his entrance exam answer sheets   you re an interesting student  ayanokouji   fifty points in japanese  fifty points in mathematics  fifty points in english  fifty points in social studies  fifty points in science  you even scored fifty points on the recent short test  do you know what this means   oh  you believe that getting 50s all across the board was a coincidence  he did it intentionally   you really do seem like an odious student  listen  only 3 percent of students solved the fifth math problem successfully  however  you solved it perfectly  and used a complex formula to do so  however  the tenth problem on the test had a completion rate of 76 percent  did you make a mistake on it  is that normal   for crying out loud  i respect your frank attitude  but it ll cause problems for you in the future   i wonder  he may be even more intelligent than you  horikita  teases ayanokoji about punishment if he throws a tantrum   if you did that  ayanokouji  i would demote you to e class  certainly  of course  the  e  stands for  expelled  as in  you d be kicked out of school  well  i suppose our conversation has ended  enjoy your lives  cunning puppetmaster  deliberately engineers encounters between high potential students  horikita and ayanokoji  to prod them into action while maintaining an aloof  sarcastic facade  keenly aware of his artificial score manipulation  calls him  odious  and  interesting  exploits horikita s pride to smoke him out into the open  punctures her narrow intellectual vanity  forces her to confront the reality of class d and introduces ayanokoji as a catalyst","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Guidance office trap &amp; exposing Ayanokōji&#x27;s 50s<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.140–148<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hallway outside staff room, then guidance office.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“For getting involved with one of my students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It would have been better if you just left him alone. Thanks for waiting, Ayanokouji. Let’s go into the office.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t make any unnecessary moves. Shut up and get in here. Understand? Don’t make a sound and stay until I tell you it’s okay to come out. If you don’t do as I say, you’ll be expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Catches Class 1-B homeroom teacher Hoshinomiya Chie flirting with Ayanokōji; hits her firmly over the head and on the butt with her clipboard to chase her away.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Summons Ayanokōji into the guidance office kitchen, turns on the kettle to make green tea, and orders him into hiding behind closed doors under penalty of expulsion, anticipating Horikita’s protest.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Receives Horikita Suzune; calmly confronts her academic arrogance with cutting social philosophy.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m an instructor. I understand the mind of a student, at least to some degree, Horikita Suzune. Just as you said, you did well on the entrance examination. You had the third-highest test score among the first-year students and were close to the highest- and second-highest-scoring students. You did exceedingly well. And you’re right: We found no particular problems in your interview. On the contrary, we evaluated you quite highly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Incorrect evaluation? Perhaps your self-evaluation is far too high… I acknowledge that your academic ability is excellent. You’re certainly very smart. However, who decided that smart people are categorically superior? We never said that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Common sense? Didn’t common sense create our current, flawed society? Before, Japan relied solely on test scores to separate the superior and inferior. As a result, the incompetents at the top tried desperately to kick down the truly superior students. In the end, we settled on a system of hereditary succession.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re a capable student. I don’t deny that. However, this school’s goal is to produce superior people. If you believe academics alone place you into a higher class, you are mistaken. That was the very first thing we explained to you. Besides, think rationally. Would we have admitted someone like Sudou if we decided superiority based solely on academic merit?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are some students who are happy to be incorrectly evaluated at a lower level… Strange students who would happily be set at a low level.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but you weren’t sorted by mistake. You are definitely in Class D. You are at that level.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens the kitchen door and presents Ayanokōji to Horikita along with his entrance exam answer sheets.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re an interesting student, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fifty points in Japanese. Fifty points in mathematics. Fifty points in English. Fifty points in social studies. Fifty points in science. You even scored Fifty points on the recent short test. Do you know what this means?”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? You believe that getting 50s all across the board was a coincidence? He did it intentionally.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You really do seem like an odious student. Listen. Only 3 percent of students solved the fifth math problem successfully. However, you solved it perfectly, and used a complex formula to do so. However, the tenth problem on the test had a completion rate of 76 percent. Did you make a mistake on it? Is that normal?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For crying out loud! I respect your frank attitude, but it’ll cause problems for you in the future.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder. He may be even more intelligent than you, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Teases Ayanokōji about punishment if he throws a tantrum.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you did that, Ayanokouji, I would demote you to E Class… Certainly. Of course, the ‘E’ stands for ‘expelled.’ As in, you’d be kicked out of school. Well, I suppose our conversation has ended. Enjoy your lives.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cunning puppetmaster; deliberately engineers encounters between high-potential students (Horikita and Ayanokōji) to prod them into action while maintaining an aloof, sarcastic facade.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Keenly aware of his artificial score manipulation; calls him &quot;odious&quot; and &quot;interesting&quot;; exploits Horikita&#x27;s pride to smoke him out into the open.<span class=\"pg\">p.142, 146–148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Punctures her narrow intellectual vanity; forces her to confront the reality of Class D and introduces Ayanokōji as a catalyst.<span class=\"pg\">p.143–147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p120-1\">← Before: May 1st homeroom: The 0-point revelation &amp; S-System truth<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p152-1\">→ After: Compass-stab wake-up &amp; discipline effects<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p152-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae compass stab wake up   discipline effects when ayanokoji cries out from horikita s compass stab  calmly needles him about starting a rebellious phase   the class  wary of point losses  suppresses its usual whispers   what s the matter  ayanokouji  you cried out  have you started your rebellious phase or something  reported by hirata in his study group speech  she has announced that the midterm is imminent and failing means expulsion  her opening week discipline warning has visibly reformed the class   far fewer late arrivals and far less talking in class than before  ayanokoji and horikita acknowledge the change","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Compass-stab wake-up &amp; discipline effects<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.152, 155<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What’s the matter, Ayanokouji? You cried out. Have you started your rebellious phase or something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji cries out from Horikita&#x27;s compass stab, calmly needles him about starting a rebellious phase — the class, wary of point losses, suppresses its usual whispers.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reported by Hirata in his study-group speech: she has announced that the midterm is imminent and failing means expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Her opening-week discipline warning has visibly reformed the class — far fewer late arrivals and far less talking in class than before (Ayanokōji and Horikita acknowledge the change).<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p140-1\">← Before: Guidance office trap &amp; exposing Ayanokōji&#x27;s 50s<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p224-1\">→ After: The &quot;forgotten&quot; test-material change<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p224-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the  forgotten  test material change previously told class d that age of discovery material would be on the midterm   one week later the class learns from class c that the test s material is different  when horikita confronts her in the faculty room  admits the change without a flicker of emotion  claims forgetfulness  and hands over handwritten textbook page numbers for the revised scope   that s right  the test s topics changed last friday  sorry  i must ve forgotten to inform you   thanks to you  horikita san  i was able to correct my mistake  i m grateful to all of you  that s all  thank you   i don t think so  you still have one week  if you use that study time wisely  it should be easy  right   shooing them out  total indifference to the gravity of the blunder   even if you stay  nothing will change  you understand that  don t you  doesn t apologize as they leave  the other teachers  except a smiling hoshinomiya  don t react at all   ayanokoji concludes it was no accident  ayanokoji s reading  her earlier unshakable certainty that  there was a way for us to pass this test  was the tell   the old test pipeline is the institutional escape hatch she hinted at  cold professional exchange  horikita withdraws the group rationally rather than escalating","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p224-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The &quot;forgotten&quot; test-material change<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.224–226<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s right. The test’s topics changed last Friday. Sorry, I must’ve forgotten to inform you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Thanks to you, Horikita-san, I was able to correct my mistake. I’m grateful to all of you. That’s all. Thank you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t think so. You still have one week. If you use that study time wisely, it should be easy. Right?” (shooing them out; total indifference to the gravity of the blunder)<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Previously told Class D that Age of Discovery material would be on the midterm — one week later the class learns from Class C that the test&#x27;s material is different.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Horikita confronts her in the faculty room, admits the change without a flicker of emotion, claims forgetfulness, and hands over handwritten textbook page numbers for the revised scope.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you stay, nothing will change. You understand that, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Doesn&#x27;t apologize as they leave; the other teachers (except a smiling Hoshinomiya) don&#x27;t react at all — Ayanokōji concludes it was no accident.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji&#x27;s reading: her earlier unshakable certainty that &quot;there was a way for us to pass this test&quot; was the tell — the old-test pipeline is the institutional escape hatch she hinted at.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Cold professional exchange; Horikita withdraws the group rationally rather than escalating.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p152-1\">← Before: Compass-stab wake-up &amp; discipline effects<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p240-1\">→ After: Exam-day opener &amp; the vacation reward<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p240-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae exam day opener   the vacation reward opens exam day with bold satisfaction at full attendance   there are no absences today  it appears everyone is present   that s the first hurdle for you leftovers  are there any questions  announces the institutional reward structure between papers   if anyone stumbles here  the other tests will be an uphill battle  quite frankly  you ll take this midterm and the final exam in july  if no one fails either test  you ll be rewarded with a vacation during your summer break   that s right  a dream vacation on an island surrounded by the brilliant blue sea","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Exam-day opener &amp; the vacation reward<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.240<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“There are no absences today. It appears everyone is present.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s the first hurdle for you leftovers. Are there any questions?”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If anyone stumbles here, the other tests will be an uphill battle, quite frankly. You’ll take this midterm and the final exam in July. If no one fails either test, you’ll be rewarded with a vacation during your summer break.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens exam day with bold satisfaction at full attendance.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Announces the institutional reward structure between papers.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. A dream vacation on an island surrounded by the brilliant blue sea.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p224-1\">← Before: The &quot;forgotten&quot; test-material change<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p246-1\">→ After: The red line, the rounding kill &amp; the hallway covenant<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p246-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the red line  the rounding kill   the hallway covenant posts the results sheet with genuine surprise at the class s performance   more than ten perfect scores across math  japanese  and social studies   honestly  i m impressed  i didn t think that you d score so well  many students tied with perfect scores in mathematics  japanese  and social studies  more than ten of you  actually  draws a red line directly above sudou s name the moment celebration starts   you failed  sudou   when did anyone say that thirty two points was a passing grade   say whatever you want  it won t matter  this is the undeniable truth  you had to score at least a forty to pass the midterm exam  in other words  you were just one point short  you were so close  writes the class pass grade formula on the board  79 6   2   39 8   we set a passing grade for each individual class  just as we did for the last test  we calculated that number by dividing the average score by two  that s how we arrived at our answer  runs expulsion processing without emotion  withdrawal form  legal guardian required   then hands sudou s english sheet to hirata on request  i was expecting that you d protest   he s being expelled  he got a failing grade     there are no mistakes   hirata s verification  faces horikita s decimal inconsistency challenge and closes it with the true rule   we didn t simply omit the decimal when we calculated the passing grade  we rounded the numbers up or down  on the last test  we rounded down to thirty two points  and on this  we rounded up to forty  there s your answer   you should have noticed that we rounded the numbers  but to hold on to that possibility  well  too bad  at any rate  first period will be starting soon  i ll be going  waits at the faculty room window  almost as if she were waiting for someone  engages ayanokoji s fairness inquiry   if you re asking for my personal opinion  then  no  of course not  the world isn t fair  not even the slightest bit   but it s an excellent example of how unfair the world is  in fact  you could call it a microcosm of our unfair society   that s unfortunate  what you ve said isn t wrong  but i can t allow you to do that  sudou will be expelled  that decision cannot be overturned at this stage  give up   the hedge ak pounces on   at this stage  reveals full knowledge of the old test operation   including that ak personally contacted the third year   and openly praises it   ayanokouji  i personally hold you in rather high regard  i ve thought so since assigning this test  obtaining the old test problems was certainly one correct solution  you distributed the old test problems to everyone in class and raised the average scores  i have to praise such a logical decision  honestly  you did very well  when ak proposes buying one test point  bursts out laughing   then names the price   ha ha ha ha ha  that s a rather interesting idea  you really are a different kind of student  i never imagined you d try to buy points   seeing as how this is a special occasion  i ll sell a test point for the exceptional price of 100 000 points  accepts ak s and horikita s id cards together  sells one point for a combined 100 000 points and cancels sudou s expulsion on the spot   fine  i accept your deal  i ll sell you one point to apply to sudou s test  taking a combined total of 100 000 points from you both  as for the matter of sudou s expulsion  you can inform the class that s no longer the case   do you understand how talented ayanokouji is  at least somewhat   to horikita   no one from class d has ever been promoted before  the school has already labeled you defective and will coldly toss you aside  how will you accomplish your goal   well  i look forward to seeing what you do next  as your homeroom teacher  i ll be sure to watch over you with great attention and care  rule shaped cruelty with deliberate seams  enforces expulsion without mercy  yet her hedges  waits  and praise are an invitation to exploit the system she just demonstrated  full mutual awareness  she knows his every move  prices his audacity at 100 000  and formally becomes his invested homeroom sponsor  defeats her counter trap  then rewards her defective vs trash answer with visible approval","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The red line, the rounding kill &amp; the hallway covenant<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.246–255<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Honestly, I’m impressed. I didn’t think that you’d score so well. Many students tied with perfect scores in mathematics, Japanese, and social studies. More than ten of you, actually.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You failed, Sudou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“When did anyone say that thirty-two points was a passing grade?”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Posts the results sheet with genuine surprise at the class&#x27;s performance — more than ten perfect scores across math, Japanese, and social studies.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Draws a red line directly above Sudou&#x27;s name the moment celebration starts.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Say whatever you want, it won’t matter. This is the undeniable truth. You had to score at least a forty to pass the midterm exam. In other words, you were just one point short. You were so close.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Writes the class pass-grade formula on the board: 79.6 ÷ 2 = 39.8.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We set a passing grade for each individual class, just as we did for the last test. We calculated that number by dividing the average score by two. That’s how we arrived at our answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Runs expulsion processing without emotion: withdrawal form, legal guardian required — then hands Sudou&#x27;s English sheet to Hirata on request (&quot;I was expecting that you&#x27;d protest&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s being expelled. He got a failing grade.” / “There…are no mistakes.” (Hirata&#x27;s verification)<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Faces Horikita&#x27;s decimal inconsistency challenge and closes it with the true rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.249–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We didn’t simply omit the decimal when we calculated the passing grade. We rounded the numbers up or down. On the last test, we rounded down to thirty-two points, and on this, we rounded up to forty. There’s your answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should have noticed that we rounded the numbers, but to hold on to that possibility… Well, too bad. At any rate, first period will be starting soon. I’ll be going.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Waits at the faculty-room window &quot;almost as if she were waiting for someone&quot;; engages Ayanokōji&#x27;s fairness inquiry.<span class=\"pg\">p.250–252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re asking for my personal opinion, then, no, of course not. The world isn’t fair, not even the slightest bit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But it’s an excellent example of how unfair the world is. In fact, you could call it a microcosm of our unfair society.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s unfortunate. What you’ve said isn’t wrong, but I can’t allow you to do that. Sudou will be expelled. That decision cannot be overturned at this stage. Give up.” (the hedge AK pounces on: &quot;at this stage&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reveals full knowledge of the old-test operation — including that AK personally contacted the third-year — and openly praises it.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji, I personally hold you in rather high regard. I’ve thought so since assigning this test. Obtaining the old test problems was certainly one correct solution… you distributed the old test problems to everyone in class and raised the average scores. I have to praise such a logical decision. Honestly, you did very well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When AK proposes buying one test point, bursts out laughing — then names the price.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha ha ha ha! That’s a rather interesting idea. You really are a different kind of student. I never imagined you’d try to buy points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Seeing as how this is a special occasion, I’ll sell a test point for the exceptional price of 100,000 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts AK&#x27;s and Horikita&#x27;s ID cards together: sells ONE point for a combined 100,000 points and cancels Sudou&#x27;s expulsion on the spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.253–254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine. I accept your deal. I’ll sell you one point to apply to Sudou’s test, taking a combined total of 100,000 points from you both. As for the matter of Sudou’s expulsion, you can inform the class that’s no longer the case.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you understand how talented Ayanokouji is? At least somewhat?” (to Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No one from Class D has ever been promoted before. The school has already labeled you defective and will coldly toss you aside. How will you accomplish your goal?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I look forward to seeing what you do next. As your homeroom teacher, I’ll be sure to watch over you with great attention and care.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rule-shaped cruelty with deliberate seams: enforces expulsion without mercy, yet her hedges, waits, and praise are an invitation to exploit the system she just demonstrated.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Full mutual awareness: she knows his every move, prices his audacity at 100,000, and formally becomes his invested homeroom sponsor.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Defeats her counter-trap, then rewards her defective-vs-trash answer with visible approval.<span class=\"pg\">p.249–255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v1-p240-1\">← Before: Exam-day opener &amp; the vacation reward<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p16-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 1  july 1  the point board  and a deposit with a rider she  strode into the classroom as the homeroom bell rang  to a class d more raucous than usual  the first payout day since enrollment   good morning  everyone  you all seem more restless than usual today   oh  so that s why you re all so restless   don t jump to conclusions  listen to what i have to say first  you re correct  ike  you have all worked harder than ever before  i recognize that  naturally  the school understands full well how you all feel  puts a paper listing the month s point totals on the board  class a at the top  rather than letting the class read the app s numbers unexplained   well then  without further ado  here are this month s point totals   well  this time there was a little trouble  the first year students  point distribution has been delayed  i m sorry  but you ll have to wait a bit longer   don t blame me  this was the school s decision  there s nothing i can do about it  once the trouble has been resolved  you ll receive your points  if there are still points left  that is  the same method as entrance day  now in maintenance mode  buy the room s acknowledgment first  you re correct  ike  then deliver the bad news  then assign it to the school and refuse responsibility   closing on a conditional no student asks her to unpack  ayanokoji is the only one who hears the rider as a warning   there was deeper meaning behind chabashira sensei s words  ak s memory of her entrance day line is what taught the class to spend  he  understood that our homeroom teacher  chabashira sensei  hadn t been kidding when she told us   at this school  you can buy anything with your points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): the point board, and a deposit with a rider<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.16–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She &quot;strode into the classroom as the homeroom bell rang&quot; to a Class D more raucous than usual, the first payout day since enrollment. Puts a paper listing the month&#x27;s point totals on the board, Class A at the top, rather than letting the class read the app&#x27;s numbers unexplained.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Good morning, everyone. You all seem more restless than usual today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, so that’s why you’re all so restless?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t jump to conclusions. Listen to what I have to say first. You’re correct, Ike. You have all worked harder than ever before. I recognize that. Naturally, the school understands full well how you all feel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then. Without further ado, here are this month’s point totals.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, this time there was a little trouble. The first-year students’ point distribution has been delayed. I’m sorry, but you’ll have to wait a bit longer,”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t blame me. This was the school’s decision, there’s nothing I can do about it. Once the trouble has been resolved, you’ll receive your points. If there are still points left, that is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The same method as entrance day, now in maintenance mode: buy the room&#x27;s acknowledgment first (&quot;You’re correct, Ike&quot;), then deliver the bad news, then assign it to the school and refuse responsibility — closing on a conditional no student asks her to unpack.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Ayanokōji is the only one who hears the rider as a warning: &quot;There was deeper meaning behind Chabashira-sensei’s words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s memory of her entrance-day line is what taught the class to spend: he &quot;understood that our homeroom teacher, Chabashira-sensei, hadn’t been kidding when she told us, &#x27;At this school, you can buy anything with your points.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: collecting Sudou for the faculty room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 3  collecting sudou for the faculty room  sudou  i have to talk to you about something  come to the faculty room   i ve already spoken with the advisor  you don t have to come with me if you don t want to  but you will face the consequences later   that all depends on you  the longer you stand there  the more time you waste  she removes the excuse before she makes the request   the club advisor has already been told  so his  i ve got basketball practice now  buys nothing  refuses to estimate how long it will take  that all depends on you  first direct contact since she cancelled his expulsion at the midterm  private summons  no audience in front of the class  and he  clicked his tongue  and followed  her out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: collecting Sudou for the faculty room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.22<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sudou. I have to talk to you about something. Come to the faculty room,”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve already spoken with the advisor. You don’t have to come with me if you don’t want to, but you will face the consequences later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That all depends on you. The longer you stand there, the more time you waste.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She removes the excuse before she makes the request — the club advisor has already been told, so his &quot;I’ve got basketball practice now&quot; buys nothing. Refuses to estimate how long it will take (&quot;That all depends on you&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> First direct contact since she cancelled his expulsion at the midterm: private summons, no audience in front of the class, and he &quot;clicked his tongue, and followed&quot; her out.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): the point board, and a deposit with a rider<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): she makes Sudou&#x27;s fight public<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3 open  july 2 homeroom  she makes sudou s fight public about to leave homeroom  she  assaulted us with one of her infamously brief and off hand announcements  naming sudou and class c in front of the whole class   i have an announcement for you all  there was a bit of trouble the other day  an incident between the student sitting there  sudou  and some students from class c  in short  there was a fight  ak s read of the delivery   her face was so devoid of emotion or interest when she spoke that there was a certain serene beauty to it  she inserted no personal bias whatsoever when she addressed the class  and explained the situation from a position of neutrality   the complaint came from class c  they claim that the fight was one sided  however  when we spoke to the accused  sudou said that their claims were false  he insists that the students class c called him over and started the fight   so in other words  we don t yet know the truth  therefore  we have put our decision on hold for now  our response  and the punishment  will come when we find out who was at fault   so speaks the accused  but i wouldn t say that you have a high level of credibility right now  if there is an eyewitness  as sudou seems to believe  then the situation may change  if anyone here witnessed the fight  please raise your hand   chabashira sensei continued talking in a robotic  flat voice  no students raised their hands in response to her question   too bad  sudou  it appears there are no witnesses in this class   in order to check for witnesses  every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident   anyway  that is all  we ll make our final judgment next tuesday  taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence  with that  let s end homeroom for the day  she destroys sudou s containment plan as a side effect of doing her job neutrally  no editorialising  no protection  and the school wide notification she volunteers is the step that turns a class matter into a cohort matter  ak   the school probably had no say in the matter  the disciplinary process stated on the page  accusation and defence both recorded  decision held pending eyewitness or evidence  judgment date fixed  next tuesday  and every class informed so witnesses can be found outside class d  she leaves and  sudou followed right after her    ak s read  he stayed out of the room rather than lose his temper at his classmates","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): she makes Sudou&#x27;s fight public<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–41<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">About to leave homeroom, she &quot;assaulted us with one of her infamously brief and off-hand announcements&quot;, naming Sudou and Class C in front of the whole class. &quot;Chabashira-sensei continued talking in a robotic, flat voice. No students raised their hands in response to her question.&quot; She leaves and &quot;Sudou followed right after her&quot; — AK&#x27;s read: he stayed out of the room rather than lose his temper at his classmates.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I have an announcement for you all. There was a bit of trouble the other day, an incident between the student sitting there, Sudou, and some students from Class C. In short, there was a fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The complaint came from Class C. They claim that the fight was one-sided. However, when we spoke to the accused, Sudou said that their claims were false. He insists that the students Class C called him over and started the…”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So in other words, we don’t yet know the truth. Therefore, we have put our decision on hold for now. Our response, and the punishment, will come when we find out who was at fault.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s read of the delivery: &quot;Her face was so devoid of emotion or interest when she spoke that there was a certain serene beauty to it. She inserted no personal bias whatsoever when she addressed the class, and explained the situation from a position of neutrality.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The complaint came from Class C. They claim that the fight was one-sided. However, when we spoke to the accused, Sudou said that their claims were false. He insists that the students Class C called him over and started the fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So speaks the accused, but I wouldn’t say that you have a high level of credibility right now. If there is an eyewitness, as Sudou seems to believe, then the situation may change. If anyone here witnessed the fight, please raise your hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Too bad, Sudou. It appears there are no witnesses in this class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In order to check for witnesses, every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, that is all. We’ll make our final judgment next Tuesday, taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence. With that, let’s end homeroom for the day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She destroys Sudou&#x27;s containment plan as a side effect of doing her job neutrally: no editorialising, no protection, and the school-wide notification she volunteers is the step that turns a class matter into a cohort matter. AK: &quot;The school probably had no say in the matter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The disciplinary process stated on the page: accusation and defence both recorded, decision held pending eyewitness or evidence, judgment date fixed (next Tuesday), and every class informed so witnesses can be found outside Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: collecting Sudou for the faculty room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the teacher who will not take the witness on trust<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 5 sec  5 2  the teacher who will not take the witness on trust the faculty room  after homeroom  at the class s request  ayanokoji hangs back   a witness  for sudou s case   i understand what you re said  however  i can t simply accept what you re telling me   sakura  why are you testifying now  when i reported the issue during homeroom  you didn t step forward  it s not as though you were absent that day  right   you re not good at talking with other people  and yet you ve decided to testify now  isn t that strange   i m speaking to sakura right now  her interrogation of a frightened witness reduces the girl physically   sakura hunched and shrank away  much like a frog cornered by a snake  the narrator adds that she  should have understood what kind of girl sakura was  and that speaking up at all  had made great progress    the method is exact and costly   i see  so  then you mustered up the courage to come forward   i see  well if you are a witness as you say  naturally i m obligated to relay that information to the school  however  while the school will listen to the whole story  sudou may not be declared innocent   are you really the witness  sakura  that s what i m getting at  i think that it may be a lie made up by class d because the students are afraid of receiving a negative evaluation   horrible  if you really had witnessed an event  you should have come forward on the first day  it s natural to feel suspicious when someone steps up just in the nick of time  considering that the witness is from class d  it s doubly suspicious  any reasonable person would have doubts  don t you think so  conveniently  a student from the same class happened to be in an infrequently visited building and happened to witness the entire event   however  a witness is a witness  i cannot determine if she s lying  so for the time being  i will accept her testimony  so  sakura  i will ask for you to join us on the day of deliberation  i understand that you do not like to associate with others  but can you do this   if you don t like it  you do have the option to withdraw  also  we ll tell sudou that he will be participating in the deliberation   if sudou himself consents  i will approve it  however  we cannot allow that many people  only a maximum of two may sit in on the deliberation  please think on that carefully  she tests the witness by making her imagine the room   as if she were testing the girl  the narrator s judgment of her method  kept as his   as our teacher  chabashira sensei should have understood what kind of girl sakura was","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the teacher who will not take the witness on trust<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.163–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The faculty room, after homeroom, at the class&#x27;s request; Ayanokōji hangs back.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;A witness? For Sudou’s case?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand what you’re said. However, I can’t simply accept what you’re telling me,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakura, why are you testifying now? When I reported the issue during homeroom, you didn’t step forward. It’s not as though you were absent that day, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re not good at talking with other people, and yet you’ve decided to testify now? Isn’t that strange?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m speaking to Sakura right now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her interrogation of a frightened witness reduces the girl physically: &quot;Sakura hunched and shrank away, much like a frog cornered by a snake.&quot; The narrator adds that she &quot;should have understood what kind of girl Sakura was&quot; and that speaking up at all &quot;had made great progress&quot; — the method is exact and costly.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. So, then you mustered up the courage to come forward?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. Well if you are a witness as you say, naturally I’m obligated to relay that information to the school. However, while the school will listen to the whole story, Sudou may not be declared innocent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you really the witness, Sakura? That’s what I’m getting at. I think that it may be a lie made up by Class D because the students are afraid of receiving a negative evaluation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horrible? If you really had witnessed an event, you should have come forward on the first day. It’s natural to feel suspicious when someone steps up just in the nick of time. Considering that the witness is from Class D, it’s doubly suspicious. Any reasonable person would have doubts. Don’t you think so? Conveniently, a student from the same class happened to be in an infrequently visited building and happened to witness the entire event?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, a witness is a witness. I cannot determine if she’s lying, so for the time being, I will accept her testimony. So, Sakura, I will ask for you to join us on the day of deliberation. I understand that you do not like to associate with others, but can you do this?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you don’t like it, you do have the option to withdraw. Also, we’ll tell Sudou that he will be participating in the deliberation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Sudou himself consents, I will approve it. However, we cannot allow that many people. Only a maximum of two may sit in on the deliberation. Please think on that carefully.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She tests the witness by making her imagine the room: &quot;as if she were testing the girl.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s judgment of her method, kept as his: &quot;As our teacher, Chabashira-sensei should have understood what kind of girl Sakura was.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): she makes Sudou&#x27;s fight public<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the rules she releases one at a time<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 open  the rules she releases one at a time the faculty room before the hearing  hoshinomiya tries to tag along and chabashira pushes her back inside   what are you doing this time   whenever you sneak out  that s around the time i start to feel suspicious   of course you can t  you know that outsiders cannot participate   well then  shall we be going   of course not  this school does have rather complicated rules  but in cases such as these a settlement is reached between the homeroom teacher of the class in question  the concerned parties  and the student council  the venue is disclosed last  after horikita has already agreed to attend  the narrator calls it her habit of revealing  an important detail right at the last minute   if you want to stop  now s the time  horikita  the fourth floor student council room  she enters first and sets the proceedings in motion   sorry we re late   have you already met   this is sakagami sensei  the homeroom teacher for class c  now then   this is the student council president   well then  i would now like to discuss the violent incident that occurred last tuesday with the members of the student council  the involved parties  and their homeroom teachers  you may begin the proceedings  student council secretary tachibana   so  this is all by chance  the question is aimed at the president s claim of attending by choice  he does not answer it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 open: the rules she releases one at a time<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.192–193<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The faculty room before the hearing; Hoshinomiya tries to tag along and Chabashira pushes her back inside. The fourth-floor student council room; she enters first and sets the proceedings in motion.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What are you doing this time?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Whenever you sneak out, that’s around the time I start to feel suspicious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Of course you can’t. You know that outsiders cannot participate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, shall we be going?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course not. This school does have rather complicated rules, but in cases such as these a settlement is reached between the homeroom teacher of the class in question, the concerned parties, and the student council.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The venue is disclosed last, after Horikita has already agreed to attend; the narrator calls it her habit of revealing &quot;an important detail right at the last minute.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you want to stop, now’s the time, Horikita.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry we’re late.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Have you already met?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is Sakagami-sensei, the homeroom teacher for Class C. Now then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is the student council president.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, I would now like to discuss the violent incident that occurred last Tuesday with the members of the student council, the involved parties, and their homeroom teachers. You may begin the proceedings, student council secretary Tachibana.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So, this is all by chance?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question is aimed at the president’s claim of attending by choice; he does not answer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the teacher who will not take the witness on trust<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the witness she dismisses<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 sec  6 1  the witness she dismisses  why are you in such a hurry  sakagami sensei  when sakagami moves to strike the witness  she agrees with him instead of resisting   you d think that chabashira sensei would ally herself with class d  but that didn t seem to be the case   you re certainly right that this is a waste of time  so i suppose we have no choice  you can come down now  sakura  the order is what forces sakura s outburst  the chapter does not say whether chabashira expected it  and the narrator records only that she  ordered sakura to leave  almost as if she d lost interest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the witness she dismisses<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.199–200<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why are you in such a hurry, Sakagami-sensei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You’re certainly right that this is a waste of time, so I suppose we have no choice. You can come down now, Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> When Sakagami moves to strike the witness, she agrees with him instead of resisting: &quot;You’d think that Chabashira-sensei would ally herself with Class D, but that didn’t seem to be the case.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199–200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The order is what forces Sakura’s outburst; the chapter does not say whether Chabashira expected it, and the narrator records only that she &quot;ordered Sakura to leave, almost as if she’d lost interest.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the rules she releases one at a time<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise she will not refuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 sec  6 1  the compromise she will not refuse  compromise   we seem to have already reached a logical conclusion  there s no reason to refuse sakagami sensei s proposal  she treats the settlement as arithmetic rather than advocacy  the proposal is  certainly a reasonable compromise  and she says so in front of her own student   if this matter required some extra time before retrial  then the student council president would have offered a sufficient grace period  in other words  the amount of time granted should be enough for this case  extensions are only offered under special circumstances  the disciplinary settlement is heard by the two homeroom teachers  the concerned students and the student council  the retrial window is fixed by the council and cannot be extended on request  she warns horikita she can still withdraw  then closes the only procedural door horikita asks to reopen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise she will not refuse<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.205–209<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Compromise?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We seem to have already reached a logical conclusion. There’s no reason to refuse Sakagami-sensei’s proposal,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If this matter required some extra time before retrial, then the student council president would have offered a sufficient grace period. In other words, the amount of time granted should be enough for this case. Extensions are…<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She treats the settlement as arithmetic rather than advocacy: the proposal is &quot;certainly a reasonable compromise,&quot; and she says so in front of her own student.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If this matter required some extra time before retrial, then the student council president would have offered a sufficient grace period. In other words, the amount of time granted should be enough for this case. Extensions are only offered under special circumstances,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The disciplinary settlement is heard by the two homeroom teachers, the concerned students and the student council; the retrial window is fixed by the council and cannot be extended on request.<span class=\"pg\">p.192, 209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She warns Horikita she can still withdraw, then closes the only procedural door Horikita asks to reopen.<span class=\"pg\">p.192, 209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the witness she dismisses<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the empty seat and the unexpected ending<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 5  the empty seat and the unexpected ending she arrives with sakagami for the retrial and finds ayanokoji s seat empty   what happened to ayanokouji  horikita   not participating  she stares at the vacant seat  as if the proceedings would be meaningless without him   you re withdrawing your complaint  she chuckles with  a thin smile  as if she found something amusing   oh  excuse me  i was just surprised because i hadn t foreseen this  i figured we would argue all day until one side collapsed  or until we could propose an acceptable compromise  however  unbelievably  they ve said that they want to withdraw the complaint  she confirms the practical result to both sides  no suspension for sudo  no punishment for class c  with this incident as the example to remember next time   of course  the same goes for the students in class c  naturally  youthful zeal is a good quality  however  the next time you think about causing problems  you should remember this incident as an example  do not forget  okay","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the empty seat and the unexpected ending<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.243–246<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She arrives with Sakagami for the retrial and finds Ayanokōji’s seat empty.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What happened to Ayanokouji, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Not participating?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You’re withdrawing your complaint?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She stares at the vacant seat &quot;as if the proceedings would be meaningless without him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She chuckles with &quot;a thin smile, as if she found something amusing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, excuse me. I was just surprised because I hadn’t foreseen this. I figured we would argue all day until one side collapsed, or until we could propose an acceptable compromise. However, unbelievably, they’ve said that they want to withdraw the complaint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> She confirms the practical result to both sides: no suspension for Sudō, no punishment for Class C, with this incident as the example to remember next time.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course. The same goes for the students in Class C, naturally. Youthful zeal is a good quality. However, the next time you think about causing problems, you should remember this incident as an example. Do not forget. Okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise she will not refuse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: what she says to Sudō<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 5  what she says to sudo  i m glad  sudou   personally  i think you should have been punished   the reason this incident occurred at all is because of your behavior  who told the truth and who lied is trivial  it s important that you don t let this kind of thing happen again  you do understand that  yes   however  admitting your own faults isn t  cool  so even if you acknowledge that your personality was partly to blame  you act tough  you get stronger  that s fine  however  if you act like that  you won t be able to make real friends  eventually  horikita will abandon you  she ll leave   there s strength in admitting your mistakes  sudou  the page records it as the first time she has tried to reach out to one of her students as a homeroom teacher   you shouldn t make promises so casually  you ll cause trouble soon again   what do you think  horikita  do you think that sudou will become a model student","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: what she says to Sudō<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246–247<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m glad, Sudou,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Personally, I think you should have been punished,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The reason this incident occurred at all is because of your behavior. Who told the truth and who lied is trivial. It’s important that you don’t let this kind of thing happen again. You do understand that, yes?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, admitting your own faults isn’t ‘cool.’ So even if you acknowledge that your personality was partly to blame, you act tough. You get stronger. That’s fine. However, if you act like that, you won’t be able to make real friends. Eventually, Horikita will abandon you. She’ll leave.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246–247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s strength in admitting your mistakes, Sudou.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The page records it as the first time she has tried to reach out to one of her students as a homeroom teacher.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You shouldn’t make promises so casually. You’ll cause trouble soon again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What do you think, Horikita? Do you think that Sudou will become a model student?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the empty seat and the unexpected ending<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p248-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p248-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 5  the private lesson about ayanokoji  so  what methods did you use  horikita   don t try to dodge the question  they wouldn t withdraw their complaint without a reason  would they   so it s a secret  hmm  well  allow me to change the question  who came up with the strategy that defeated class c   ayanokouji isn t here  so i m a little curious   i see  so you recognize that  hmm   his potential  hmm   there are various things to consider  but if you want to reach class a  i ll give you one bit of advice   the students in class d all have some kind of defect  more or less  to borrow an expression used by others in this school  class d is an assemblage of people that could be called  defective products  you already understand this quite well though  don t you   well  what do you think is ayanokouji s defect   oh  and what is it   he dislikes trouble  hmm  is that what you perceive when you look at ayanokouji   well  horikita  let s try to learn as much as we possibly can about the boy called ayanokouji  without delay  shall we  otherwise  it ll be too late  you already seem to have fallen into ayanokouji s trap   why do you think ayanokouji purposefully got scores of 50 points across on the board on his entrance examination  why do you think ayanokouji is helping you  why do you think that ayanokouji doesn t put himself forward as a superior student  despite having superior ability  is ayanokouji kiyotaka really someone who  dislikes trouble   in my personal opinion  ayanokouji is the most defective student in class d   higher functioning products are more difficult to handle  if you misunderstand how to handle him  the class might be completely destroyed in short order   get to know the person called ayanokouji  what is he thinking  what focal point does he base his actions around  what is his fatal flaw  there s definitely an answer there  she says nothing more  and the page gives no reason for the warning beyond horikita s own unanswered question  her usual manner is  unaware of and unconcerned with her class  which is why the session itself is the surprise","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p248-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.248–251<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So. What methods did you use, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don’t try to dodge the question. They wouldn’t withdraw their complaint without a reason, would they?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So it’s a secret, hmm? Well, allow me to change the question. Who came up with the strategy that defeated Class C?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji isn’t here, so I’m a little curious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. So you recognize that, hmm?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;His potential, hmm?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There are various things to consider. But if you want to reach Class A, I’ll give you one bit of advice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The students in Class D all have some kind of defect, more or less. To borrow an expression used by others in this school, Class D is an assemblage of people that could be called ‘defective products.’ You already understand this quite well though, don’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, what do you think is Ayanokouji’s defect?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh? And what is it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He dislikes trouble, hmm? Is that what you perceive when you look at Ayanokouji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, Horikita. Let’s try to learn as much as we possibly can about the boy called Ayanokouji, without delay, shall we? Otherwise, it’ll be too late. You already seem to have fallen into Ayanokouji’s trap.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Why do you think Ayanokouji purposefully got scores of 50 points across on the board on his entrance examination? Why do you think Ayanokouji is helping you? Why do you think that Ayanokouji doesn’t put himself forward as a superior student, despite having superior ability? Is Ayanokouji Kiyotaka really someone who ‘dislikes trouble’?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In my personal opinion, Ayanokouji is the most defective student in Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Higher functioning products are more difficult to handle. If you misunderstand how to handle him, the class might be completely destroyed in short order.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Get to know the person called Ayanokouji. What is he thinking? What focal point does he base his actions around? What is his fatal flaw? There’s definitely an answer there.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She says nothing more, and the page gives no reason for the warning beyond Horikita’s own unanswered question.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her usual manner is &quot;unaware of and unconcerned with her class,&quot; which is why the session itself is the surprise.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: what she says to Sudō<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner narration","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  cold open in her pov  the icarus gamble the volume opens inside chabashira s first person with no setting and no interlocutor   a soliloquy that retells the myth of daedalus and icarus and then states why she provoked a certain young boy  the myth  her summary  daedalus  confined in a tower by king minos alongside his son icarus  fashions wings of bird feathers  thread and wax  the warning  if you fly too high  the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together  be careful  icarus forgets it  the wax melts  and he falls into the sea and dies  she frames her own predicament in classical myth    greek mythology deals abundantly with human frailty    treating her situation as a fable to be interpreted before it is confessed   for some reason  i thought of icarus  wings when standing before a certain young boy   considering what these past few months had brought  i could say that i made the comparison simply because he resembled icarus   but i immediately came to realize that the two boys were fundamentally different from one another  this boy possessed neither the bravery nor the arrogance of icarus   i had been pushed into a corner  i had no choice but to do it  cornered and out of means  she chose the provocation  incur the boy s divine wrath and turn his quiet rage onto herself   the die cannot be returned once cast  the gamble had already begun  soliloquy register  measured  literary  fatalistic   she narrates her own decision as a fable already decided  with no hedging and no appeal for sympathy  the boy is never named on these pages   only  a certain young boy     this boy  identity left open  not assigned from context","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: cold open in her POV, the Icarus gamble<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.10–12<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The volume opens inside Chabashira&#x27;s first person with no setting and no interlocutor — a soliloquy that retells the myth of Daedalus and Icarus and then states why she provoked a certain young boy.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">The myth, her summary: Daedalus, confined in a tower by King Minos alongside his son Icarus, fashions wings of bird feathers, thread and wax; the warning “If you fly too high, the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together.…<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;For some reason, I thought of Icarus’ wings when standing before a certain young boy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;Considering what these past few months had brought, I could say that I made the comparison simply because he resembled Icarus.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> The myth, her summary: Daedalus, confined in a tower by King Minos alongside his son Icarus, fashions wings of bird feathers, thread and wax; the warning “If you fly too high, the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together. Be careful.”; Icarus forgets it, the wax melts, and he falls into the sea and dies.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She frames her own predicament in classical myth — “Greek mythology deals abundantly with human frailty.” — treating her situation as a fable to be interpreted before it is confessed.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;But I immediately came to realize that the two boys were fundamentally different from one another. This boy possessed neither the bravery nor the arrogance of Icarus.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I had been pushed into a corner. I had no choice but to do it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Cornered and out of means, she chose the provocation: incur the boy&#x27;s divine wrath and turn his quiet rage onto herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The die cannot be returned once cast. The gamble had already begun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Soliloquy register: measured, literary, fatalistic — she narrates her own decision as a fable already decided, with no hedging and no appeal for sympathy.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The boy is never named on these pages — only &quot;a certain young boy&quot; / &quot;this boy&quot;. Identity left open; not assigned from context.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ike-kanji chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 1  she runs the rules that sink the summer beach landing  she takes class d s roll call in the same jersey as the students   keeping on like that would be shameful  ike  so stop talking    and the world widening follow up   there are workplaces where there aren t any chairs in the office  and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls  the world is wider and deeper than you even know   in other words  you are ill equipped to distinguish between what is reality and what isn t     in my opinion  you re all equally worthless  delivers the penalty list verbatim from the manual   thirty for health retirement  twenty for pollution  five per absent student at roll call  disqualification plus private point forfeiture for inter class violence  assembles the cardboard toilet in front of the class and demonstrates the polymer sheet    five uses with one vinyl bag  explains the spot system  eight hour rights of exclusive possession  one provisional bonus point per occupation  fifty point penalty for using another class s spot  brushes off the eavesdropping complaint and the  fate  line  threatens a behavioural report  refuses the emergency bear question on process grounds   the test has already begun  i cannot answer any questions that might possibly influence your results  confirms the school  isn t involved in the test process at all    survival is the test","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.24–39<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Beach landing; she takes Class D&#x27;s roll call in the same jersey as the students.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Keeping on like that would be shameful, Ike, so stop talking.” — and the world-widening follow-up: “There are workplaces where there aren’t any chairs in the office, and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls. The world…”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In other words, you are ill-equipped to distinguish between what is reality and what isn’t.” / “In my opinion, you’re all equally worthless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Keeping on like that would be shameful, Ike, so stop talking.” — and the world-widening follow-up: “There are workplaces where there aren’t any chairs in the office, and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls. The world is wider and deeper than you even know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Delivers the penalty list verbatim from the manual — thirty for health retirement, twenty for pollution, five per absent student at roll call, disqualification plus private-point forfeiture for inter-class violence.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Assembles the cardboard toilet in front of the class and demonstrates the polymer sheet — &quot;five uses with one vinyl bag.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Explains the spot system: eight-hour rights of exclusive possession, one provisional bonus point per occupation, fifty-point penalty for using another class&#x27;s spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Brushes off the eavesdropping complaint and the &quot;fate&quot; line; threatens a behavioural report.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Refuses the emergency-bear question on process grounds: &quot;the test has already begun. I cannot answer any questions that might possibly influence your results.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Confirms the school &quot;isn’t involved in the test process at all&quot; — survival is the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: cold open in her POV, the Icarus gamble<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.8: she announces the retirement<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 8  she announces the retirement reads the class the cost of kouenji s exit without inflection   kouenji complained about being in poor physical condition and returned to the ship  of course  that means that you ve had thirty points deducted  those are the rules  so there s nothing to be done","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.8: she announces the retirement<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.97–98<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Reads the class the cost of Kouenji&#x27;s exit without inflection: &quot;Kouenji complained about being in poor physical condition and returned to the ship. Of course, that means that you’ve had thirty points deducted. Those are the rules, so there’s nothing to be done.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p152-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 5 sec  5 2  the faculty room deal closing ceremonies  she catches him the moment homeroom ends   faculty room  before he leaves   and gives nothing else away until the door shuts   ayanokouji  i have to talk to you before you leave  come to the faculty room  waits in the faculty room doorway and answers in short sentences that raise his  incoming depression  meter   come in   we ll talk inside   you might expect bad things when you re asked to come to the faculty room  but contrary to your expectations  it s a fine place  there aren t eyes all around in here  many things are better said with some personal privacy  uses a faculty room whose security camera is missing   privacy is the point of the venue   that s funny  i thought you didn t have any friends   i ve called you here today because i wanted to tell you my personal story   it s something i haven t talked to anyone about since i had become a homeroom teacher  it s silly  but please listen   don t tell this story to anyone else  if you can do that  please return to your seat   how do i appear to you as class d s homeroom teacher   am i wrong   no  it s as you say  i won t deny it  however  the truth is different  owns the cold teacher verdict outright  then opens with the reason behind it   i was once a student at this school  i was in class d  just like you  she sat where he sits   a student of this school  in class d  once   huh  well  in my time  the class difference wasn t as extreme  you could say that we were in a four way battle  not a three way one  up until we approached graduation in the third semester of our third year  the difference between a and d wasn t even 100 points  it was a close battle  where even one trivial mistake could knock you off balance  her era at the school  four classes fighting as four  a and d under 100 points apart until the third semester of the third year   set against the three way school he knows   yes  it happened rather unexpectedly  class c went to hell because of my mistake  in the end  my goal of reaching class a and my dreams were shattered  one trivial mistake sent class c down and ended her class a dream   the regret the narration reads as still live   i feel that your presence will be vital to reach class a   a few days ago  a certain man contacted the school directly  he said  expel ayanokouji kiyotaka   of course  we can t just expel someone on a third party s whim  as long as you are a student at this school  you are protected by the rules  however if you cause any problems  that s a different story  smoking  bullying  stealing  cheating  if you cause any scandal  expulsion is unavoidable   it has nothing to do with your intentions  if i determine that something seems like an issue  it will become reality  the rule she wields  protection stands until she decides something is a problem   then the scandal  not the intent  decides the expulsion   here s the deal  ayanokouji  you are going to aim for class a for me  i will follow up as extensively as i can in order to protect you  don t you think that sounds like a good offer  names it a deal and dresses the pressure as protection   the narration calls it blackmailing a student outright   that s too bad  ayanokouji  you will be expelled  and once again  class d won t reach class a   let me ask you once more  will you aim for class a  or be expelled  you choose  takes the collar grab over the desk  then laughs in self deprecation   the confidence breaks and the old dream shows   i surprised myself  i realize now that i still haven t given up on reaching class a   i d thought you would lead class d voluntarily  but we don t have any time to waste  you have to decide here and now  will you help me or not   relax  my life is already full of regrets  by the end the cold indifference is gone   misty eyed and forceful  the act put away","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.152–157<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Closing ceremonies: she catches him the moment homeroom ends — faculty room, before he leaves — and gives nothing else away until the door shuts.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji. I have to talk to you before you leave. Come to the faculty room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Come in.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We’ll talk inside.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>31 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Waits in the faculty-room doorway and answers in short sentences that raise his “incoming depression” meter.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might expect bad things when you’re asked to come to the faculty room, but contrary to your expectations, it’s a fine place. There aren’t eyes all around in here. Many things are better said with some personal privacy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Uses a faculty room whose security camera is missing — privacy is the point of the venue.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s funny. I thought you didn’t have any friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve called you here today because I wanted to tell you my personal story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s something I haven’t talked to anyone about since I had become a homeroom teacher. It’s silly, but please listen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t tell this story to anyone else. If you can do that, please return to your seat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How do I appear to you as Class D’s homeroom teacher?”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Am I wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, it’s as you say. I won’t deny it. However, the truth is different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Owns the cold-teacher verdict outright, then opens with the reason behind it.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was once a student at this school. I was in Class D, just like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> She sat where he sits — a student of this school, in Class D, once.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh… Well, in my time, the class difference wasn’t as extreme. You could say that we were in a four-way battle, not a three-way one. Up until we approached graduation in the third semester of our third year, the difference between A and D wasn’t even 100 points. It was a close battle, where even one trivial mistake could knock you off balance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Her era at the school: four classes fighting as four, A and D under 100 points apart until the third semester of the third year — set against the three-way school he knows.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. It happened rather unexpectedly. Class C went to hell because of my mistake. In the end, my goal of reaching Class A and my dreams were shattered.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> One trivial mistake sent Class C down and ended her Class A dream — the regret the narration reads as still live.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel that your presence will be vital to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A few days ago, a certain man contacted the school directly. He said ‘expel Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. We can’t just expel someone on a third party’s whim. As long as you are a student at this school, you are protected by the rules. However…if you cause any problems, that’s a different story. Smoking, bullying, stealing, cheating… If you cause any scandal, expulsion is unavoidable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It has nothing to do with your intentions. If I determine that something seems like an issue, it will become reality.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The rule she wields: protection stands until she decides something is a problem — then the scandal, not the intent, decides the expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Here’s the deal, Ayanokouji. You are going to aim for Class A for me. I will follow up as extensively as I can in order to protect you. Don’t you think that sounds like a good offer?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Names it a deal and dresses the pressure as protection — the narration calls it blackmailing a student outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s too bad, Ayanokouji. You will be expelled, and once again, Class D won’t reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me ask you once more. Will you aim for Class A? Or be expelled? You choose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes the collar grab over the desk, then laughs in self-deprecation — the confidence breaks and the old dream shows.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I surprised myself. I realize now that I still haven’t given up on reaching Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d thought you would lead Class D voluntarily, but we don’t have any time to waste. You have to decide here and now. Will you help me or not?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Relax. My life is already full of regrets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> By the end the cold indifference is gone — misty-eyed and forceful, the act put away.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.8: she announces the retirement<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p248-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the Icarus talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p248-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7  the icarus talk intercepts him on the empty side of the ship and confirms  through the icarus myth  that the man who demanded his expulsion is his father   may i have a word with you   i don t really feel sociable  is it okay if i refuse  chabashira sensei   if you really don t want to  i can just start talking here  you don t mind if we stand outside  do you   it s hot  so please keep it brief   is it safe to say that for the time being  you re satisfied   yes  first  i d like to say that you did wonderfully  i m honestly impressed   well  tell me something  is it really true  did he demand i be expelled from school   do you have any basis for saying that the story is true   i know quite a lot about you  might not that be the reason  more than anything else  other teachers don t know about your true abilities  but i have no doubts  claims knowledge of his true abilities that the other teachers do not have   i m sure that you ve heard of this rather famous myth  the wings of icarus   why do you bring that up   icarus flew out of the tower where he was imprisoned in order to gain his freedom  however  that wasn t achieved through one person s abilities alone  it was because his father  daedalus  had constructed wings and instructed him to fly  he didn t fly because of his own intentions  don t you think that sounds exactly like your current predicament   i can t understand   that man no  your father said this   sooner or later  kiyotaka will gladly chase the means of his expulsion from school  you re welcoming your end  much like how icarus fell into the sea and died after his wings were burned  because he d flown too close to the sun  the man who demanded his expulsion from the school is named as his father  with the father s own words quoted   so  what do you plan to do  she asked   you should know  sensei  icarus won t heed daedalus  warnings  answers her myth with the myth   burned wings and all  he flies on for his freedom","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p248-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the Icarus talk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.248–249<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Intercepts him on the empty side of the ship and confirms, through the Icarus myth, that the man who demanded his expulsion is his father.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“May I have a word with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I don’t really feel sociable. Is it okay if I refuse, Chabashira-sensei?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you really don’t want to, I can just start talking here. You don’t mind if we stand outside, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s hot, so please keep it brief.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it safe to say that for the time being, you’re satisfied?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. First, I’d like to say that you did wonderfully. I’m honestly impressed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, tell me something. Is it really true? Did he demand I be expelled from school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you have any basis for saying that the story is true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know quite a lot about you. Might not that be the reason, more than anything else? Other teachers don’t know about your true abilities. But I have no doubts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Claims knowledge of his true abilities that the other teachers do not have.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sure that you’ve heard of this rather famous myth, the wings of Icarus.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you bring that up?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Icarus flew out of the tower where he was imprisoned in order to gain his freedom. However, that wasn’t achieved through one person’s abilities alone. It was because his father, Daedalus, had constructed wings and instructed him to fly. He didn’t fly because of his own intentions. Don’t you think that sounds exactly like your current predicament?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That man—no, your father—said this: ‘Sooner or later, Kiyotaka will gladly chase the means of his expulsion from school.’ You’re welcoming your end, much like how Icarus fell into the sea and died after his wings were burned, because he’d flown too close to the sun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The man who demanded his expulsion from the school is named as his father, with the father’s own words quoted.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, what do you plan to do?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should know, Sensei. Icarus won’t heed Daedalus’ warnings.”<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Answers her myth with the myth — burned wings and all, he flies on for his freedom.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  the class a leverage  named twice named in ayanokoji s cabin reverie   the leverage that brought him to class a s track  the threat that binds him  she  threatened to expel me from this paradise  unless he works toward class a  the narrator contrasts her with mashima  where she seems  unmotivated and unnaturally uncooperative  he is  impossible to read  still holds him with the class a ultimatum three days after the island test","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the Class A leverage, named twice<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.12, p.34<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ayanokōji’s cabin reverie — the leverage that brought him to Class A’s track.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The threat that binds him: she “threatened to expel me from this paradise” unless he works toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator contrasts her with Mashima: where she seems “unmotivated and unnaturally uncooperative,” he is “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Still holds him with the Class A ultimatum three days after the island test.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.3: in the teachers’ corner<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p121-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  in the teachers  corner she shares a sofa with hoshinomiya and mashima as ayanokoji approaches  named in the three teacher group he finds relaxing off the deck  sips her drink like a cocktail while hoshinomiya downs whiskey in one gulp  the conversation turns familiar   she is called sae chan and asked about her focus on ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: in the teachers’ corner<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.121–122<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She shares a sofa with Hoshinomiya and Mashima as Ayanokōji approaches.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named in the three-teacher group he finds relaxing off the deck.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sips her drink like a cocktail while Hoshinomiya downs whiskey in one gulp.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The conversation turns familiar — she is called Sae-chan and asked about her focus on Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the Class A leverage, named twice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p166-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.3: the midnight point question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p166-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 4 sec  4 3  the midnight point question meets ayanokoji by the night pool after his call  answers the buy anything exceptions question  survives hoshinomiya s drunk interruption  and gets asked for a future favour   sorry to keep you waiting  ayanokouji   it s okay  i m sorry for calling you so late   his line  in exchange   an instructor is obligated to consult with a student  it s nothing out of the ordinary  besides  for better or worse  this is the first time you ve actually called me  doesn t treat class d with love  students wouldn t normally come to her   his read of why the first call matters   don t worry about it  adult issues  anyway  what did you want to ask  pale  alcohol on her breath    adult issues  waved off while he works the exceptions question   yes  exceptions exist  naturally  for example  if you request to buy the life of a teacher or student  we cannot honor that request  private points cannot buy a life   the standing exception to  anything   you re drunk  aren t you  chabashira sensei said   to hoshinomiya   jeez  you can really hold your liquor  you handled yourself today  and you re fine now  too   about hoshinomiya s iron liver  grabs her by the nape and drags her off  stays calm under the sneaking around bait   ayanokouji requested this location  he wanted to consult me in private   a big problem  as a teacher  it s only natural for me to consult my students and soothe their anxieties  answered chabashira sensei   good  now hurry up and leave already  i ll head back soon myself   sorry  she s troublesome   well  i can only speak from my own experience  but it was when someone wanted   to change the school rules  of course  you re limited to a certain realistic scope  for example  you could change the class start time in order to avoid being late to class  she answered  the largest point spend she has seen  a system change within a realistic scope   hypotheticals only  no facts   are you dissatisfied with my answer   you could have just emailed me that question  i don t understand why you wanted me to meet you  accepts the no email reason  no record  eyes him with suspicion when he calls the future favour over his shoulder   i ll ask you for a favor in the near future  i called   his line  her reaction recorded  the teacher rivalry read  competing and deceiving for the top class   salaries or a school days grudge  he can t tell","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p166-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.3: the midnight point question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.166–169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ayanokōji by the night pool after his call; answers the buy-anything exceptions question, survives Hoshinomiya’s drunk interruption, and gets asked for a future favour.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sorry to keep you waiting, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s okay. I’m sorry for calling you so late.” (his line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“An instructor is obligated to consult with a student. It’s nothing out of the ordinary. Besides, for better or worse, this is the first time you’ve actually called me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t treat Class D with love; students wouldn’t normally come to her — his read of why the first call matters.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry about it. Adult issues. Anyway, what did you want to ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pale, alcohol on her breath — “adult issues” waved off while he works the exceptions question.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Exceptions exist, naturally. For example, if you request to buy the life of a teacher or student, we cannot honor that request.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Private points cannot buy a life — the standing exception to “anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re drunk, aren’t you?” Chabashira-sensei said. (to Hoshinomiya)<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jeez. You can really hold your liquor. You handled yourself today, and you’re fine now, too.” (about Hoshinomiya’s iron liver)<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Grabs her by the nape and drags her off; stays calm under the sneaking-around bait; “Ayanokouji requested this location. He wanted to consult me in private.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167-168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A big problem? As a teacher, it’s only natural for me to consult my students and soothe their anxieties,” answered Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good. Now hurry up and leave already. I’ll head back soon myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. She’s troublesome.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I can only speak from my own experience, but it was when someone wanted … to change the school rules. Of course, you’re limited to a certain realistic scope. For example, you could change the class start time in order to avoid being late to class,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.168-169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The largest point spend she has seen: a system change within a realistic scope — hypotheticals only, no facts.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you dissatisfied with my answer?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You could have just emailed me that question. I don’t understand why you wanted me to meet you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Accepts the no-email reason (no record); eyes him with suspicion when he calls the future favour over his shoulder.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll ask you for a favor in the near future,” I called. (his line, her reaction recorded)<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The teacher rivalry read: competing and deceiving for the top class — salaries or a school-days grudge, he can’t tell.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p121-1\">← Before: Ch.3: in the teachers’ corner<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p71-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  a passing mention ak compares manabu s interest in him to chabashira s   the 50  entrance scores and the resume versus report gap  she is the other adult who has fixated on him for the same reason  no scene with her in this chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p71-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK compares Manabu&#x27;s interest in him to Chabashira&#x27;s — the 50% entrance scores and the resume-versus-report gap.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She is the other adult who has fixated on him for the same reason; no scene with her in this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p87-1\">→ After: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p87-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  a passing mention ak credits his island and cruise ship restraint to the partial displays he gave her  she is the reason he had to show off on the island  horikita has no clue about the arrangement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.87<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK credits his island and cruise-ship restraint to the partial displays he gave her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She is the reason he had to show off on the island; Horikita has no clue about the arrangement.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p71-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.6: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p159-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6  a passing mention ak names her as one of the people he would bring in to eliminate karuizawa s enemies  the promise makes her the class s last resort protection behind hirata","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.159<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK names her as one of the people he would bring in to eliminate Karuizawa&#x27;s enemies.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The promise makes her the class&#x27;s last-resort protection behind Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4_5-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 1  the sports festival briefing afternoon homeroom runs two hours  she distributes the festival handout and weekly schedules in a detached  matter of fact manner   however  from september to the beginning of october  we will be holding more physical education classes to prepare for the school sports festival   in any case  this event will massively impact each and every class    answers hirata s special exam question vaguely  explains the red white split   class d and class a ride the red team together   you in class d are assigned to the red team   their reward will be not having any points deducted    the cruel  brief answer to the winning team question   in the sports festival  you can earn test points as a prize  which you can then apply to a written exam    lets out a slight laugh  an unusual sight  reads out the ten lowest penalty  for first years  ten points off the next written exam   should you fall short of the minimum required number of people for competitions for all participants  you will be deemed unable to continue and disqualified   a substitute requires 100 000 private points per competition   next period s location will move to gymnasium 1  where you ll meet with students from other classes and grade levels","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the sports festival briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16–25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Afternoon homeroom runs two hours: she distributes the festival handout and weekly schedules in a detached, matter-of-fact manner.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“However, from September to the beginning of October, we will be holding more physical education classes to prepare for the school sports festival.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In any case, this event will massively impact each and every class.” — answers Hirata’s special-exam question vaguely.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You in Class D are assigned to the Red Team.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Explains the Red/White split — Class D and Class A ride the Red Team together.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Their reward will be not having any points deducted.” — the cruel, brief answer to the winning-team question.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the sports festival, you can earn test points as a prize, which you can then apply to a written exam.” — lets out a slight laugh, an unusual sight.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Reads out the ten-lowest penalty: for first-years, ten points off the next written exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Should you fall short of the minimum required number of people for competitions for all participants, you will be deemed unable to continue and disqualified,”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A substitute requires 100,000 private points per competition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Next period’s location will move to Gymnasium 1, where you’ll meet with students from other classes and grade levels.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p21-1\">→ After: Ch.2–8: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p21-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 8  passing mentions homeroom rules and gate warnings where she is the authority voice off the main beat  written test point and substitute rules attributed to her briefing  sports festival name check in the cafe debrief s rules recap  class strategy pages cite her as the teacher who logs reports  after the false injury trap  her preventative report is already the ch7 spine  these pages repeat her name in horikita s self reproach  same thread  chabashira sensei mentioned while horikita searches for sudou  substitute negotiation with ayanokouji names her as the approver  she accepts the 100 000 point substitute plan for the scavenger hunt","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2–8: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.21, 32, 47, 157–158, 173–174<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Homeroom rules and gate warnings where she is the authority voice off the main beat.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Written-test-point and substitute rules attributed to her briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sports-festival name-check in the café debrief’s rules recap.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Class strategy pages cite her as the teacher who logs reports.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After the false-injury trap, her preventative report is already the ch7 spine; these pages repeat her name in Horikita’s self-reproach.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Same thread: Chabashira-sensei mentioned while Horikita searches for Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Substitute negotiation with Ayanokouji names her as the approver.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She accepts the 100,000-point substitute plan for the scavenger hunt.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the sports festival briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the gate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 3  the gate spraying water at the main gate after school  she s on duty and clocks that he stayed behind later than usual   you stayed behind longer than usual  ayanokouji   are you prepared for the sports festival   in your case  i would have thought that you d already have some eccentric idea or strategy in place   but if you don t show me some results soon  i ll stop covering for you  their talk stops when their eyes meet   public discussion helps no one  she accepts his right to choose his path but puts a deadline on her cover  blank page sits inside the dialogue  page number and watermark only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the gate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.35–37<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spraying water at the main gate after school; she’s on duty and clocks that he stayed behind later than usual.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You stayed behind longer than usual, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you prepared for the sports festival?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In your case, I would have thought that you’d already have some eccentric idea or strategy in place,”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if you don’t show me some results soon, I’ll stop covering for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Their talk stops when their eyes meet — public discussion helps no one; she accepts his right to choose his path but puts a deadline on her cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page sits inside the dialogue (page number and watermark only).<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2–8: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3: Watches the homeroom from the back<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3 sec  3  watches the homeroom from the back chabashira moves to the back of the classroom during hirata s two hour homeroom and does not speak   she intends to watch the class run itself  lets hirata run the session unopposed   she speaks no word during the whole strategy meeting  the chapter prints nothing further about her  her last stated posture is watching from the back  p 39","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3: Watches the homeroom from the back<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira moves to the back of the classroom during Hirata’s two-hour homeroom and does not speak — she intends to watch the class run itself.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Lets Hirata run the session unopposed — she speaks no word during the whole strategy meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The chapter prints nothing further about her; her last stated posture is watching from the back (p.39).<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the gate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6: the report she cannot prove<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 sec  6  the report she cannot prove chabashira approaches hirata on the ground after sudou s punch and reads the rage immediately   what s going on   did you hit him  sudou does not deny it    so what if i did  what then    so she has the answer she needed  accepts hirata s fall story only enough to log a preventative report  the pair are told to keep apart  and superiors will hear later   if the victim says that nothing happened  then there s no problem  she adds that she can tell something is going on  tells them to keep their distance from each other  and will give her superiors a report later as a preventative measure  detached  matter of fact  she knows the cover is thin and files it as prevention rather than discipline","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6: the report she cannot prove<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.133<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira approaches Hirata on the ground after Sudou’s punch and reads the rage immediately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What’s going on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Did you hit him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If the victim says that nothing happened, then there’s no problem.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou does not deny it — “So what if I did? What then?” — so she has the answer she needed.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Accepts Hirata’s fall story only enough to log a preventative report: the pair are told to keep apart, and superiors will hear later.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She adds that she can tell something is going on, tells them to keep their distance from each other, and will give her superiors a report later as a preventative measure.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Detached, matter-of-fact: she knows the cover is thin and files it as prevention rather than discipline.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3: Watches the homeroom from the back<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.1: relays Kinoshita’s accusation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 1  relays kinoshita s accusation in the infirmary chabashira tells horikita that kinoshita claims she was knocked down deliberately   i had kushida fetch you  looks like she was quick about it   well  kinoshita says that you deliberately knocked her down  horikita   kinoshita claims that  during the race  you repeatedly looked back at her   even if that s true  though  she claims you kicked her   i believe you re innocent  but as long as we have no proof one way or the other  we must consider the matter  names the devil s proof and warns a foul play finding would invalidate scores and bar the recommended events   you haven t forgotten what happened to sudou after his fight  have you   under the circumstances  it would probably be easy for the school to believe that the incident was intentional rather than accidental   kinoshita won t accept that   her testimony  and the footage  make this fairly damning   kushida consulted me on the matter   okay  i ll let you try","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.1: relays Kinoshita’s accusation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.146–148<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the infirmary Chabashira tells Horikita that Kinoshita claims she was knocked down deliberately.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I had Kushida fetch you. Looks like she was quick about it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, Kinoshita says that you deliberately knocked her down, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Kinoshita claims that, during the race, you repeatedly looked back at her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if that’s true, though, she claims you kicked her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you’re innocent, but as long as we have no proof one way or the other, we must consider the matter,”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Names the Devil’s Proof and warns a foul-play finding would invalidate scores and bar the recommended events.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You haven’t forgotten what happened to Sudou after his fight, have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Under the circumstances, it would probably be easy for the school to believe that the incident was intentional rather than accidental.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kinoshita won’t accept that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Her testimony, and the footage, make this fairly damning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida consulted me on the matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I’ll let you try,”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6: the report she cannot prove<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.1: presses the look-back, objects to Ryuuen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 1  presses the look back  objects to ryuuen chabashira presses horikita on why she looked back during the race  then tries to stop ryuuen s kneeling demand   horikita  you only looked behind you when you raced with kinoshita  why did you do that   is that true  kinoshita   ryuuen  this is going too far   you still have about twenty minutes  you haven t eaten yet  right","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.1: presses the look-back, objects to Ryuuen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.151–156<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira presses Horikita on why she looked back during the race, then tries to stop Ryuuen’s kneeling demand.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Horikita, you only looked behind you when you raced with Kinoshita. Why did you do that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is that true, Kinoshita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ryuuen. This is going too far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You still have about twenty minutes. You haven’t eaten yet, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.1: relays Kinoshita’s accusation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p169-1\">→ After: Ch.8 sec. 8.2: accepts Ayanokouji as substitute<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p169-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 8 sec  8 2  accepts ayanokouji as substitute chabashira raises an eyebrow at ayanokouji volunteering for sudou s three legged place   so  you re going to be sudou s substitute  ayanokouji   rather unusual  since you tend to prefer watching on the sidelines  notes his usual sideline habit while approving the entry","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8 sec. 8.2: accepts Ayanokouji as substitute<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira raises an eyebrow at Ayanokouji volunteering for Sudou’s three-legged place.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, you’re going to be Sudou’s substitute, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Rather unusual, since you tend to prefer watching on the sidelines.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notes his usual sideline habit while approving the entry.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.1: presses the look-back, objects to Ryuuen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p30-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ike-kanji hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  midterm posting and paper shuffle briefing homeroom opens with class d s nervous midterm atmosphere  chabashira posts the results   take your seats  it seems you prepared quite a bit in advance for this   my  my  you all look so serious  it s hard to imagine you re class d   the school will expel you immediately if you fail the midterm or final exam  i told you as much before  so i imagine it s fresh in your memory  passing   40 per subject  sports festival scores can lift a subject to perfect  bottom ten lose 10 per subject  sudou s rise to twelfth  average 57  draws her genuine compliment that no one drops out this time   as you can see  no one has to drop out of school due to their midterm scores this time  all of you managed to pass   it would be reasonable to expect a private point increase in november  i must say  in the three years i ve taught at this school  no other class d has held on this long without any students dropping out  well done  stops at ike s desk for an honest school evaluation  answers his quiz panic  fields his question creation frustration   no  from a student s perspective  this is quite a paradise  even as a teacher  i feel that this school is almost excessively lavish  it treats the students here so well that it almost defies common sense  stops at hirata s desk  does he like the school   whenever i m nervous  i work harder with everyone else  short test  100 questions  junior high third year level  no grade impact but huge final exam impact  pairs from it take the final together  under 60 combined in a subject expels both  aggregate historically  700   i would love to help you understand  sudou  the school has decided that this next quiz s results will help determine which students to partner in class   in years past  it s been around seven hundred points  cited with horikita as an excellent student still at risk depending on partner   don t be so hasty  i ll explain the overall requirements in more detail later  partner with bottom panic from sudou and yamauchi s reply   well said  ike  many of you probably think the same thing  which is why i m going to give you just one piece of advice  don t assume that you understand how this school works just because you ve finished the first semester of your first year  in the future  you ll face countless exams far more difficult than those you face now   well  it s the truth  in years past  we call it the  paper shuffle  but one or two pairs are usually expelled due to this test  most of them are from class d  this is by no means a threat  i m just telling you the facts   lastly  although this is obvious  cheating is forbidden  anyone who cheats will immediately be disqualified and expelled  along with their partner  the same applies to all midterm and final examinations  classes write 400 questions for another class  higher class score takes 50 points  tie   no change  teachers revise unfair questions   do you understand  ike  after his absurd hardness panic   after the submission deadline passes  the school will utilize its own premade questions  however  please keep in mind that those questions will be easier   each class will choose another class to compete against  and i will report that request to my superiors  if another class makes the same choice  representatives will draw lots  however  if there are no duplicate nominations  your choice of class will be honored  i ll accept your nomination for the class you d like to go up against next week  the day before the short test  you should think very carefully  her gentler side is new  horikita reads it as the creepier signal that something worse is coming  suzune   you praising us feels weird","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: midterm posting and Paper Shuffle briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.30–39<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Homeroom opens with Class D’s nervous midterm atmosphere; Chabashira posts the results.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Take your seats. It seems you prepared quite a bit in advance for this”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My, my. You all look so serious. It’s hard to imagine you’re Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The school will expel you immediately if you fail the midterm or final exam. I told you as much before, so I imagine it’s fresh in your memory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Passing = 40 per subject; sports-festival scores can lift a subject to perfect; bottom ten lose 10 per subject.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou’s rise to twelfth (average 57) draws her genuine compliment that no one drops out this time.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As you can see, no one has to drop out of school due to their midterm scores this time. All of you managed to pass.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would be reasonable to expect a private point increase in November. I must say, in the three years I’ve taught at this school, no other Class D has held on this long without any students dropping out. Well done.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Stops at Ike’s desk for an honest school evaluation; answers his quiz panic; fields his question-creation frustration.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. From a student’s perspective, this is quite a paradise. Even as a teacher, I feel that this school is almost excessively lavish. It treats the students here so well that it almost defies common sense”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Stops at Hirata’s desk: does he like the school; “whenever I’m nervous, I work harder with everyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Short test: 100 questions, junior-high third-year level, no grade impact but huge final-exam impact; pairs from it take the final together; under 60 combined in a subject expels both; aggregate historically ~700.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I would love to help you understand, Sudou. The school has decided that this next quiz’s results will help determine which students to partner in class”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In years past, it’s been around seven hundred points”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Cited with Horikita as an excellent student still at risk depending on partner.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be so hasty. I’ll explain the overall requirements in more detail later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Partner-with-bottom panic from Sudou and Yamauchi’s reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well said, Ike. Many of you probably think the same thing, which is why I’m going to give you just one piece of advice. Don’t assume that you understand how this school works just because you’ve finished the first semester of your first year. In the future, you’ll face countless exams far more difficult than those you face now”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it’s the truth. In years past… We call it the ‘Paper Shuffle,’ but one or two pairs are usually expelled due to this test. Most of them are from Class D. This is by no means a threat; I’m just telling you the facts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Lastly, although this is obvious, cheating is forbidden. Anyone who cheats will immediately be disqualified and expelled, along with their partner. The same applies to all midterm and final examinations.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Classes write 400 questions for another class; higher class score takes 50 points; tie = no change; teachers revise unfair questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Do you understand, Ike?” after his absurd-hardness panic.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After the submission deadline passes, the school will utilize its own premade questions. However, please keep in mind that those questions will be easier”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Each class will choose another class to compete against, and I will report that request to my superiors. If another class makes the same choice, representatives will draw lots. However, if there are no duplicate nominations, your choice of class will be honored. I’ll accept your nomination for the class you’d like to go up against next week, the day before the short test. You should think very carefully”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her gentler side is new; Horikita reads it as the creepier signal that something worse is coming.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Suzune: “You praising us feels weird.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3–7: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p40-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3 7  passing mentions named across exam prep and test day margins where she is not the section s focus  class strategy talk runs while horikita fetches hirata  chabashira s earlier hint frames the plan  ayanokoji recalls her hint about the test s wording difficulty  chabashira s man who wants to see me remark stays in ayanokoji s caution list  invigilator for the final  places papers and forbids turning over early  exam opens under her signal  average students analysis follows  rooftop switch talk does not include her  named only as the teacher kushida confirmed with","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3–7: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.40–41, 51, 192–193, 202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named across exam-prep and test-day margins where she is not the section’s focus.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Class strategy talk runs while Horikita fetches Hirata; Chabashira’s earlier hint frames the plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji recalls her hint about the test’s wording difficulty.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira’s man-who-wants-to-see-me remark stays in Ayanokōji’s caution list.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Invigilator for the final: places papers and forbids turning over early.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Exam opens under her signal; average-students analysis follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Rooftop switch talk does not include her; named only as the teacher Kushida confirmed with.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.3: midterm posting and Paper Shuffle briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: cited from the Pallet table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p54-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3 sec  3 2  cited from the pallet table horikita cites chabashira s first class d without expulsions and the historical one or two pair figure while arguing pairs are balanced  her earlier briefing is the premise of the balanced pairs inference  chabashira is not present at pallet  only her prior rules are quoted","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2: cited from the Pallet table<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.54<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita cites Chabashira’s first Class D without expulsions and the historical one-or-two-pair figure while arguing pairs are balanced.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her earlier briefing is the premise of the balanced-pairs inference.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira is not present at Pallet; only her prior rules are quoted.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3–7: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p76-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5: nomination and quiz day<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p76-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji satou-maya chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 5 sec  5  nomination and quiz day leaves the classroom after homeroom begins at 6 p m  hirata takes the podium with her permission  confirms class d s class c nomination had no competing conflict  classes a and b both nominated class d   we will begin shortly  but i d like to say something  you nominated class c as the class you wanted to attack for this test  since there was no conflict with any other class  your nomination was approved   class c will attack class d  they also had no competing nominations that conflicted with that decision  teases ike s dark circles  warns him not to do something he ll regret   at any rate  you look like you re doing quite well  ike  yamauchi  you usually have dark circles under your eyes right before you take a test  did you happen to come up with some secret strategy   don t do something you ll regret later  it would be better if you took this quiz seriously   right  your final grade won t reflect your score on this at all   sure  if things go the way you expect them to go  that is  probes horikita s certainty about pair selection before the quiz begins   aren t you worried that you re wrong about how the pairs are selected   well then  let s begin  i needn t remind you that no form of cheating is allowed  if someone gets caught cheating  then there will be no mercy  short utterance  begin  announces the short quiz pairings and the final exam partner list   well  i will now announce the pairings for the final exam   the results indicate that some among you understood this short quiz s purpose   students were to be paired based on the difference in points  with the highest scorer partnered with the lowest  and so on  if students had the same scores  the pairings would have been determined at random  it s probably not necessary for me to explain the system  but i thought i would anyway","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5: nomination and quiz day<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.76, 80–83<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves the classroom after homeroom begins at 6 p.m.; Hirata takes the podium with her permission.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“We will begin shortly, but I’d like to say something. You nominated Class C as the class you wanted to attack for this test. Since there was no conflict with any other class, your nomination was approved,”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Class C will attack Class D. They also had no competing nominations that conflicted with that decision.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“At any rate, you look like you’re doing quite well, Ike. Yamauchi, you usually have dark circles under your eyes right before you take a test. Did you happen to come up with some secret strategy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Confirms Class D’s Class C nomination had no competing conflict; Classes A and B both nominated Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Teases Ike’s dark circles; warns him not to do something he’ll regret.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t do something you’ll regret later. It would be better if you took this quiz seriously.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. Your final grade won’t reflect your score on this at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sure. If things go the way you expect them to go, that is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Probes Horikita’s certainty about pair selection before the quiz begins.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Aren’t you worried that you’re wrong about how the pairs are selected?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, let’s begin. I needn’t remind you that no form of cheating is allowed. If someone gets caught cheating, then there will be no mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Short utterance: Begin.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Announces the short-quiz pairings and the final-exam partner list.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I will now announce the pairings for the final exam,”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The results indicate that some among you understood this short quiz’s purpose,”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Students were to be paired based on the difference in points, with the highest scorer partnered with the lowest, and so on. If students had the same scores, the pairings would have been determined at random. It’s probably not necessary for me to explain the system, but I thought I would anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: cited from the Pallet table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the day-before leak window (named only)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p105-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 5  the day before leak window  named only  named as the teacher who would receive class d s final questions and answers the day before the test  the submission channel ayanokoji flags as ready to be stolen  no dialogue from chabashira on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the day-before leak window (named only)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the teacher who would receive Class D’s final questions and answers the day before the test.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The submission channel Ayanokōji flags as ready to be stolen.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue from Chabashira on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p76-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5: nomination and quiz day<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.0: conditions, the reveal, the warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p179-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru sakagami-sensei chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 0  conditions  the reveal  the warning takes horikita s envelope at the staff room after sakagami has taken ryuuen s  bargains conditions before honouring secrecy   i ll hold on to them   you want me to turn down absolutely anyone who asks to see them   that s not the issue  i understand that you re afraid of information leaking  and the school has no right to refuse your request  however  there are conditions   the entire class needs to agree to this  has everyone approved this measure   you can t say that for sure  some students might very well want to lose   on that note  can you guarantee that these are the exam questions your class wishes to use  not everyone in class saw and agreed to all of them  right   i m saying that it s not that simple  i can t be entirely sure that you  horikita suzune  are acting for your class s sake  that said  i ll honor your request  if any student asks  i absolutely won t disclose the questions and answers you created   however  i will say this generally  it s not ideal to restrict information in this manner  it proves that the class isn t united   you ve changed  horikita   as i said  i ll honor your request  in case of unforeseen circumstances  though  i d like to add one provision to our arrangement  as long as they have your permission  horikita  i ll disclose information to those asking to see the questions  is that okay   of course  someone might lie about having your permission  after all  in the event that someone comes looking for the questions  well  i ll tell them everything you said  as a teacher  i can t lie   that s right  that s required of me  as a teacher   not until we confirm that there isn t anything abnormal about them   what do you mean by that   my response is that the school already accepted and finished reviewing questions from class d   correct  the school won t use the questions you just handed me   unfortunately  horikita  i already finished reviewing another student s questions  that student shared similar concerns  they wanted me to keep the questions secret  too  this student said that  in the event that another student selfishly showed up and asked to change the problems  i should merely accept the new questions and hold on to them  they also wanted me to tell them who asked to swap those questions afterward   kushida kikyou   yes  however  the deadline is the end of today  if you wish to change the test questions  please bring kushida here   i can only speculate about which one of you is lying  horikita  i don t know the truth  i also acknowledge that an unknown third party might be pulling the strings here  if you don t resolve this dispute within your class  it ll be bad   until 6 p m   aren t you going to look for kushida  horikita   no  i received no such instructions   it s all right  horikita  ryuuen left   at any rate  this is a difficult situation  said chabashira sensei  a rare look of genuine concern on her face   i ve never had a request like this in all the time i ve managed class d  i didn t expect such caution and deception  however  you won t always take the day  horikita  if there are traitors like this among your classmates  you re doomed to fail   really  in that case  i look forward to it  holds the envelope under secrecy terms  deadline to change accepted questions is 6 p m  the same day  cannot lie as a teacher  so she will report everything horikita said if someone claims permission  conditions the favour  reveals kushida s prior acceptance  then warns that traitors doom the class  notes she has changed  names her as the prior submitter who also asked to be told who tried to swap  ignores him at the side  signals him gone before horikita drops the act  sakagami takes ryuuen s envelope moments before she takes horikita s","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.0: conditions, the reveal, the warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.179–187<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Takes Horikita’s envelope at the staff room after Sakagami has taken Ryuuen’s; bargains conditions before honouring secrecy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll hold on to them,”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You want me to turn down absolutely anyone who asks to see them?”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s not the issue. I understand that you’re afraid of information leaking, and the school has no right to refuse your request. However, there are conditions,”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>28 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The entire class needs to agree to this. Has everyone approved this measure?”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t say that for sure. Some students might very well want to lose,”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “On that note, can you guarantee that these are the exam questions your class wishes to use? Not everyone in class saw and agreed to all of them, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m saying that it’s not that simple. I can’t be entirely sure that you, Horikita Suzune, are acting for your class’s sake. That said, I’ll honor your request. If any student asks, I absolutely won’t disclose the questions and answers you created,”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, I will say this—generally, it’s not ideal to restrict information in this manner. It proves that the class isn’t united,”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve changed, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As I said, I’ll honor your request. In case of unforeseen circumstances, though, I’d like to add one provision to our arrangement. As long as they have your permission, Horikita, I’ll disclose information to those asking to see the questions. Is that okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Someone might lie about having your permission, after all. In the event that someone comes looking for the questions, well, I’ll tell them everything you said. As a teacher, I can’t lie,”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. That’s required of me, as a teacher,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not until we confirm that there isn’t anything abnormal about them,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean by that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My response is that the school already accepted and finished reviewing questions from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Correct. The school won’t use the questions you just handed me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, Horikita, I already finished reviewing another student’s questions. That student shared similar concerns. They wanted me to keep the questions secret, too. This student said that, in the event that another student selfishly showed up and asked to change the problems, I should merely accept the new questions and hold on to them. They also wanted me to tell them who asked to swap those questions afterward,”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida Kikyou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. However, the deadline is the end of today. If you wish to change the test questions, please bring Kushida here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can only speculate about which one of you is lying, Horikita. I don’t know the truth. I also acknowledge that an unknown third party might be pulling the strings here. If you don’t resolve this dispute within your class, it’ll be bad,”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Until 6 p.m.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Aren’t you going to look for Kushida, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I received no such instructions,”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s all right, Horikita. Ryuuen left,”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At any rate, this is a difficult situation,” said Chabashira-sensei, a rare look of genuine concern on her face. “I’ve never had a request like this in all the time I’ve managed Class D. I didn’t expect such caution and deception. However, you won’t always take the day, Horikita. If there are traitors like this among your classmates, you’re doomed to fail.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? In that case, I look forward to it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Holds the envelope under secrecy terms; deadline to change accepted questions is 6 p.m. the same day; cannot lie as a teacher, so she will report everything Horikita said if someone claims permission.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Conditions the favour, reveals Kushida’s prior acceptance, then warns that traitors doom the class; notes she has changed.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Names her as the prior submitter who also asked to be told who tried to swap.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ignores him at the side; signals him gone before Horikita drops the act.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">sakagami-sensei<\/b> Sakagami takes Ryuuen’s envelope moments before she takes Horikita’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v6-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the day-before leak window (named only)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p54-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ayanokouji-atsuomi chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  the urgent summons fakes paperwork to wait for ayanokoji  then walks him to the principal s office with an unusually vulnerable face   ayanokouji   yes  follow me  we need to talk   as a teacher  i don t want to be careless  but circumstances being what they are  this is necessary   unfortunately  you can t refuse  this is extremely urgent   you ll understand soon   principal  i ve brought ayanokouji kiyotaka kun  summons him under a horikita meeting lie  her nervousness is what worries him most  introduces him at the door  bows out with the principal  normally inhumanly composed  here visibly flustered  does not explain before the door opens","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the urgent summons<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.54–56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fakes paperwork to wait for Ayanokōji, then walks him to the principal’s office with an unusually vulnerable face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. Follow me. We need to talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“As a teacher, I don’t want to be careless. But circumstances being what they are, this is necessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, you can’t refuse. This is extremely urgent,”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ll understand soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Principal, I’ve brought Ayanokouji Kiyotaka-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Summons him under a Horikita-meeting lie; her nervousness is what worries him most.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> Introduces him at the door; bows out with the principal.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Normally inhumanly composed; here visibly flustered; does not explain before the door opens.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p70-1\">→ After: Ch.3: unmasked on the walk back<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p70-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ayanokouji-atsuomi hoshinomiya-chie horikita-suzune kouenji-rokusuke hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  unmasked on the walk back waits outside the office  walks him down the hall  and loses every lie in one exchange   how did it go with your father   you understand what  exactly   what are you talking about   umm no  your father wanted my cooperation  i ve been trying to get you expelled   the chairman told you   ayanokouji  did you trick me   that s just speculation  ayanokouji   i see  she said   your abilities certainly aren t those of an ordinary first year high school student   wise beyond your years isn t that how the saying goes  i guess that describes you pretty well   you re right  she continued  the composure she d so struggled to maintain had collapsed   i never met your father before today  but i really could have you expelled if i wanted to  i could claim you committed a serious violation of the rules  expulsion is the one thing you absolutely want to avoid  no   exactly   may i ask why you re so certain   so even though you know everything now  you re still done trying to reach class a  she asked   and if i keep after you  what then   allow me to rephrase the question  are you so certain that i won t take you down with me when i do lose hope  the bluff about the chairman  the exposed class a obsession  the empty expulsion threat  the retreat  admits she never met him before today   the contact was a lie  old friend whose teasing about  be dominated by a younger man  read as chabashira s class a hunger  named with kouenji  hirata  kushida as the hopeful students who re lit her ambition  same hope list  same hope list  same hope list  normally composed collapses under one reverse bluff  still threatens expulsion  ends out of ammo but not out of ambition","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p70-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: unmasked on the walk back<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.70–76<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits outside the office, walks him down the hall, and loses every lie in one exchange.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“How did it go with your father?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You understand what, exactly?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Umm…no. Your father wanted my cooperation. I’ve been trying to get you expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The chairman told you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji, did you trick me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s just speculation, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see,” she said. “Your abilities certainly aren’t those of an ordinary first-year high school student. ‘Wise beyond your years’—isn’t that how the saying goes? I guess that describes you pretty well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re right,” she continued. The composure she’d so struggled to maintain had collapsed. “I never met your father before today. But I really could have you expelled if I wanted to. I could claim you committed a serious violation of the rules. Expulsion is the one thing you absolutely want to avoid, no?”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “May I ask why you’re so certain?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So even though you know everything now, you’re still done trying to reach Class A?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And if I keep after you? What then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Allow me to rephrase the question. Are you so certain that I won’t take you down with me when I do lose hope?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The bluff about the chairman, the exposed Class A obsession, the empty expulsion threat, the retreat.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> Admits she never met him before today — the contact was a lie.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Old friend whose teasing about “be dominated by a younger man” read as Chabashira’s Class A hunger.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Named with Kouenji, Hirata, Kushida as the hopeful students who re-lit her ambition.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Same hope list.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Same hope list.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Same hope list.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Normally composed collapses under one reverse bluff; still threatens expulsion; ends out of ammo but not out of ambition.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the urgent summons<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p85-1\">→ After: Ch.3: name-checked in the father talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p85-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  name checked in the father talk passing mention  ayanokoji recalls chabashira sensei s expulsion threat while weighing his father s return  no new dialogue  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: name-checked in the father talk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.85<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Ayanokōji recalls Chabashira-sensei’s expulsion threat while weighing his father’s return; no new dialogue.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p70-1\">← Before: Ch.3: unmasked on the walk back<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p98-1\">→ After: Ch.4: leaves without a word<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p98-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 4  leaves without a word glances at ryuuen s party and walks out  another class visit is not a brawl  so she does not intervene  the visitor she ignores  left holding the classroom after her exit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: leaves without a word<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.98<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Glances at Ryuuen’s party and walks out; another-class visit is not a brawl, so she does not intervene.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The visitor she ignores.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Left holding the classroom after her exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p85-1\">← Before: Ch.3: name-checked in the father talk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the closing lecture and the private-point test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p152-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakayanagi-arisu horikita-suzune horikita-manabu karuizawa-kei chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 sec  6 1  the closing lecture and the private point test closes the second semester with renovation warnings  then surprises the class with a rare praise  later meets ayanokoji alone in the empty classroom   parts of the school will undergo renovations  so those areas will be off limits  also  all clubs will take the day off after the closing ceremony  be sure to head back as soon as you can   i m sure that many of you are already aware of this  but your promotion to class c is almost guaranteed  well done   however  don t get sloppy  if you get in trouble over the break  it might affect your class points  don t forget  even during the holidays  you represent this school   what are you planning  didn t you wash your hands of me   i ll wait in the classroom   if this is like previous years  it ll probably snow   do you like snow   i used to  then i grew up and came to hate it   you said that you have something to discuss  what do you want with me   this school s designed to make teachers  as well as students  compete with one another  it s only natural that everyone wants to rise up the ranks   that s different  it was personal  i have nothing to say to you   it seems that this is a waste of time  i m going back to work   is that what this is about  i thought you already wriggled free of my grasp  didn t you   what are you talking about   i see your ulterior motive  you can t resolve this situation on your own  but a teacher has powers you don t  and i could help conceal your involvement  a perfect resolution  yes   don t get carried away  ayanokouji  i have no intention of cooperating with you   the school doesn t exactly look kindly on teachers intervening in problems between students   to think that a student would threaten a teacher  the tables have certainly turned   if refusing to help you with this means that we never make it to class a  then so be it   what   what are you planning  ayanokouji  how long do you intend to wait   right now   yes  i remember  you and horikita together paid a hundred thousand points for that   that s true  sudou wasn t expelled  was he   it s not that easy to get private points  this year s class d has managed to accumulate a decent number  but that s a departure from normal  most years  class d has about half that amount  besides  not every student in the class gets along  at least not enough to use their private points to save a classmate  even if that means accepting a drop in class points   that might be true   do you think it was too expensive   what are you trying to say  ayanokouji   in other words  you re asking whether the price i named you and horikita was something that the school decided on in advance   it s not like i can answer any question you ask of me   think whatever you want   speculate as you wish  but this is an odd conversation  given the circumstances  karuizawa is   enough  do you think i can answer those questions  even if i were able to  there s no way you could confirm the truth     are you trying to find a gap in the rules   a few students are already doing just that  aren t they  look at ichinose and ryuuen  both accumulating private points   understood  very well  i ll answer your question  it s true that the key to beating the system lies in understanding the actual rules surrounding private point use  students from previous years have approached the problem from various perspectives  as you re doing now  even class d  the collection of  defective products  is no exception  some students have been quicker than others on the uptake  though  additionally  the school has established thousands of detailed rules to cover every possible scenario  buying and selling points  sweeping violent incidents under the rug  preventing expulsion  there s a point value attached to every single one of those  however  teachers are very limited in what we re allowed to reveal or allude to  in fact  we re prohibited from revealing most of this information  there might even be rules the teachers aren t aware of yet   so  you truly can t answer my question   correct   does this conversation have anything to do with what s happening now   not at all  i was just having a friendly chat   i don t fully understand what s happening  but i do know that karuizawa is suffering terribly at class c s hands    you should call someone else   are you insane  if you do  the entire school will know your identity   if you do this  you ll be the talk of the school  you ll destroy all possibility of leading a quiet life here   perhaps i was mistaken   mistaken   chairman sakayanagi told me about you before you enrolled  he said that you were an extremely special student  a superior one  and that you were a student we must protect  that you were raised in an environment that was far from loving  the chairman and i concluded  after much discussion  that we wanted you to feel attached to this school  and to want to stay here  then i told you that your father wanted you expelled  it wasn t true at the time  but it appears to be now   so  my mistake was in trying to use you so carelessly  hmm  i suppose i got carried away  chasing my pipe dream of class d overtaking class a   i suppose  you ve already achieved what past classes haven t  do you really think horikita can do that  though   are you really planning to step back   back to the topic at hand  you re free to make your grand entrance and expose your identity  but will that really resolve the problem   are you planning to have horikita go to the rooftop in your place   what s going on   wait  ayanokouji  what would you have done if horikita didn t agree to help  confirms under pressure that private point prices are pre legislated and teachers can only disclose them when conditions are met   one mystery solved about the 100 000 per test point rate  rare public praise then private resignation  admits the chairman s briefing and her own careless use of ayanokoji  still refuses to intervene on the roof  the student she once manipulated  now testing her and telling her he is stepping back  chairman sakayanagi s pre enrolment briefing is cited  the chairman is the father  not arisu  named as co payer of the sudou point and as the one who will unite the class  shocked when the former president arrives as witness  the suffering student whose crisis drives the rooftop decision","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the closing lecture and the private-point test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.152, 156–165<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Closes the second semester with renovation warnings, then surprises the class with a rare praise; later meets Ayanokōji alone in the empty classroom.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Parts of the school will undergo renovations, so those areas will be off-limits. Also, all clubs will take the day off after the closing ceremony. Be sure to head back as soon as you can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sure that many of you are already aware of this, but your promotion to Class C is almost guaranteed. Well done.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“However, don’t get sloppy. If you get in trouble over the break, it might affect your class points. Don’t forget, even during the holidays, you represent this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>58 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you planning? Didn’t you wash your hands of me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll wait in the classroom,”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If this is like previous years, it’ll probably snow,”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you like snow?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I used to. Then I grew up and came to hate it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You said that you have something to discuss. What do you want with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This school’s designed to make teachers, as well as students, compete with one another. It’s only natural that everyone wants to rise up the ranks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s different. It was personal. I have nothing to say to you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems that this is a waste of time. I’m going back to work.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that what this is about? I thought you already wriggled free of my grasp, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see your ulterior motive. You can’t resolve this situation on your own, but a teacher has powers you don’t, and I could help conceal your involvement. A perfect resolution, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t get carried away, Ayanokouji. I have no intention of cooperating with you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school doesn’t exactly look kindly on teachers intervening in problems between students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To think that a student would threaten a teacher. The tables have certainly turned.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If refusing to help you with this means that we never make it to Class A, then so be it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you planning, Ayanokouji? How long do you intend to wait?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, I remember. You and Horikita together paid a hundred thousand points for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true. Sudou wasn’t expelled, was he?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not that easy to get private points. This year’s Class D has managed to accumulate a decent number, but that’s a departure from normal. Most years, Class D has about half that amount. Besides, not every student in the class gets along. At least not enough to use their private points to save a classmate, even if that means accepting a drop in class points,”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That might be true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think it was too expensive?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you trying to say, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, you’re asking whether the price I named you and Horikita was something that the school decided on in advance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not like I can answer any question you ask of me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think whatever you want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Speculate as you wish, but this is an odd conversation, given the circumstances. Karuizawa is—”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Enough. Do you think I can answer those questions? Even if I were able to, there’s no way you could confirm the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “………”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you trying to find a gap in the rules?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A few students are already doing just that, aren’t they? Look at Ichinose and Ryuuen, both accumulating private points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understood. Very well, I’ll answer your question. It’s true that the key to beating the system lies in understanding the actual rules surrounding private point use. Students from previous years have approached the problem from various perspectives, as you’re doing now. Even Class D, the collection of ‘defective products’, is no exception. Some students have been quicker than others on the uptake, though. Additionally, the school has established thousands of detailed rules to cover every possible scenario. Buying and selling points, sweeping violent incidents under the rug, preventing expulsion —there’s a point value attached to every single one of those. However, teachers are very limited in what we’re allowed to reveal or allude to. In fact, we’re prohibited from revealing most of this information. There might even be rules the teachers aren’t aware of yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you truly can’t answer my question?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Correct.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Does this conversation have anything to do with what’s happening now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not at all. I was just having a friendly chat,”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t fully understand what’s happening, but I do know that Karuizawa is suffering terribly at Class C’s hands. … you should call someone else,”<span class=\"pg\">p.162–163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you insane? If you do, the entire school will know your identity.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you do this, you’ll be the talk of the school. You’ll destroy all possibility of leading a quiet life here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Perhaps I was mistaken,”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Mistaken?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Chairman Sakayanagi told me about you before you enrolled. He said that you were an extremely special student. A superior one. And that you were a student we must protect. That you were raised in an environment that was far from loving. The chairman and I concluded, after much discussion, that we wanted you to feel attached to this school, and to want to stay here. Then I told you that your father wanted you expelled. It wasn’t true at the time, but it appears to be now,”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, my mistake was in trying to use you so carelessly, hmm? I suppose I got carried away, chasing my pipe dream of Class D overtaking Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose. You’ve already achieved what past classes haven’t. Do you really think Horikita can do that, though?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you really planning to step back?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Back to the topic at hand. You’re free to make your grand entrance and expose your identity. But will that really resolve the problem?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you planning to have Horikita go to the rooftop in your place?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s going on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, Ayanokouji. What would you have done if Horikita didn’t agree to help?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Confirms under pressure that private-point prices are pre-legislated and teachers can only disclose them when conditions are met — one mystery solved about the 100,000-per-test-point rate.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rare public praise then private resignation; admits the chairman’s briefing and her own careless use of Ayanokōji; still refuses to intervene on the roof.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The student she once manipulated, now testing her and telling her he is stepping back.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Chairman Sakayanagi’s pre-enrolment briefing is cited; the chairman is the father, not Arisu.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Named as co-payer of the Sudou point and as the one who will unite the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.159–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Shocked when the former president arrives as witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The suffering student whose crisis drives the rooftop decision.<span class=\"pg\">p.161–163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p98-1\">← Before: Ch.4: leaves without a word<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6: waiting below with the former president<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p191-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu karuizawa-kei chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6  waiting below with the former president named as one of the two people a few steps down the stairs who know the circumstances and can handle the soaked uniform  ayanokoji s line to karuizawa  the former student council president and chabashira sensei are waiting below  called aside as the only teacher adjacent presence on the roof   chabashira sensei aside  it d be bad if another teacher found them  the trusted adult who knows enough to clean up without being told the full story  the student who briefed her enough to wait on the stairs  the other waiter below  the soaked uniform is hers to handle","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: waiting below with the former president<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.191–192<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the two people a few steps down the stairs who know the circumstances and can handle the soaked uniform.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s line to Karuizawa: the former student council president and Chabashira-sensei are waiting below.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Called aside as the only teacher-adjacent presence on the roof; “Chabashira-sensei aside, it’d be bad if another teacher found them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The trusted adult who knows enough to clean up without being told the full story.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The student who briefed her enough to wait on the stairs.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The other waiter below.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The soaked uniform is hers to handle.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the closing lecture and the private-point test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7_5-p12-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  the stair witness after the roof waiting with the former student council president when karuizawa left the roof  considerate  helped her back to the dorms on kiyotaka s instructions  acting on his instructions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7_5-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the stair witness after the roof<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.12<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waiting with the former student council president when Karuizawa left the roof.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Considerate; helped her back to the dorms on Kiyotaka’s instructions.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Acting on his instructions.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7_5-p150-1\">→ After: Ch.5: named as a potential target<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7_5-p150-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 5  named as a potential target internal threat list only  passing mention   on top of that  there was chabashira sensei and chairman sakayanagi    still potential targets alongside the chairman  passing mention only  teacher who knows his leverage  listed with the chairman as residual risk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7_5-p150-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: named as a potential target<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.150<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Internal threat list only.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “On top of that, there was Chabashira-sensei and Chairman Sakayanagi.” — still potential targets alongside the chairman.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Teacher who knows his leverage; listed with the chairman as residual risk.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v7_5-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the stair witness after the roof<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p11-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ike-kanji chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 1  the mixed training camp briefing on the class c bus chabashira hands out the exam handout and delivers the full mixed training camp rules before phones are collected   i m sorry  you are class c now  allow me to give you newly promoted students an overview of the special exam   yes  the penalty is expulsion   expulsion will only apply to the small group within that large group whose average score falls below the threshold set by the school   there are significant benefits to being a group representative  the representative and the representative s classmates will receive double the rewards   the revocation of expulsion costs twenty million private points and an additional three hundred class points   the use of phones will be forbidden for a week   the boys will use the main building  and the girls will take the other   private points are not pocket money  you d do well to remember that   the only one who can protect you is you  yourself   people who work hard are rewarded  that much is obvious  answers hirata s lifeline question  then frames her  not pocket money  advice as a promotion reward that undercuts his even split motion  asks if the advice was unnecessary after the vote fails  uses ike as the example of a student who might need a million private points alone   chabashira always played by the rules    ayanokoji reads her cohesion breaking advice as possibly school policy  chapter ends with the bus briefing and arrival  no further pages this chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the Mixed Training Camp briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.11–32<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the Class C bus Chabashira hands out the exam handout and delivers the full Mixed Training Camp rules before phones are collected.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry. You are Class C now. Allow me to give you newly promoted students an overview of the special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. The penalty is expulsion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Expulsion will only apply to the small group within that large group whose average score falls below the threshold set by the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are significant benefits to being a group representative. The representative and the representative’s classmates will receive double the rewards.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The Revocation of Expulsion costs twenty million private points and an additional three hundred class points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “the use of phones will be forbidden for a week”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The boys will use the main building, and the girls will take the other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “private points are not pocket money. You’d do well to remember that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The only one who can protect you is you, yourself”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “People who work hard are rewarded. That much is obvious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Answers Hirata’s lifeline question, then frames her “not pocket money” advice as a promotion reward that undercuts his even-split motion; asks if the advice was unnecessary after the vote fails.<span class=\"pg\">p.25, 28–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Uses Ike as the example of a student who might need a million private points alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Chabashira always played by the rules” — Ayanokōji reads her cohesion-breaking advice as possibly school policy.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chapter ends with the bus briefing and arrival; no further pages this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p12-1\">→ After: Ch.2: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p12-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  passing mentions named across the mixed training camp briefing and bus pages without individual rows until the ch6 turnaround scene  announces the bus s arrival and starts the boys  syllabary roll call","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.12–17, 19–21, 24, 27, 33<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named across the Mixed Training Camp briefing and bus pages without individual rows until the ch6 turnaround scene.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Announces the bus’s arrival and starts the boys’ syllabary roll call.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p11-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the Mixed Training Camp briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p160-1\">→ After: Ch.6 half 1: the turnaround teacher<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p160-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 half 1  the turnaround teacher waiting at the turnaround  arms crossed  holds roll call as the tail end teacher   the second years and third years have turned back  you guys are all that s left   it s almost eleven o clock now   wait  we ll be taking roll call before you head back down  each person has to state their class and name   you re the last one  kouenji  you have forty minutes left   roll call  kouenji  you ll be disqualified otherwise   well  he gave his name  let s cut him some slack  waits the tail with him  notes he seems to have nothing he wants to discuss with her  time check  disqualification warning  slack on the missing class  arms crossed practicality   records the stragglers without a scene","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 half 1: the turnaround teacher<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.160–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waiting at the turnaround, arms crossed; holds roll call as the tail-end teacher.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The second-years and third-years have turned back. You guys are all that’s left”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s almost eleven o’clock now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait. We’ll be taking roll call before you head back down. Each person has to state their class and name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the last one, Kouenji. You have forty minutes left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Roll call, Kouenji. You’ll be disqualified otherwise”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, he gave his name. Let’s cut him some slack.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Waits the tail with him; notes he seems to have nothing he wants to discuss with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.160–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Time check, disqualification warning, slack on the missing class.<span class=\"pg\">p.161–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Arms-crossed practicality — records the stragglers without a scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.160–162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p185-1\">→ After: Ch.6 closer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p185-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 closer no presence in chapter 6 after half 1","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p185-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 closer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.185<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> No presence in chapter 6 after half 1.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v8-p160-1\">← Before: Ch.6 half 1: the turnaround teacher<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p39-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae named as the exam s silent teacher cafe study talk  yukimura plans around the end of year exam  narration  chabashira gave no special explanation for the end of year exam  so it will be written as usual and a failing grade means expulsion  homeroom instructor whose silence is read as  written exam as usual  chabashira does not appear  only named as the source of the  non briefing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Named as the exam’s silent teacher<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.39–40<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Cafe study talk; Yukimura plans around the end-of-year exam.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Narration: Chabashira gave no special explanation for the end-of-year exam, so it will be written as usual and a failing grade means expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Homeroom instructor whose silence is read as “written exam as usual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira does not appear; only named as the source of the (non-)briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p107-1\">→ After: The provisional test briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p107-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the provisional test briefing end of lessons   chabashira explains tomorrow s comprehensive provisional test   tomorrow on the 15th  all of you will be expected to complete a comprehensive provisional test  provisional exam on the 15th has no effect on grades  questions similar to the finals  warning not to slack after promotion to class c  her briefing closes the day right before he questions horikita about kushida  class c promoted   the warning names the promotion explicitly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The provisional test briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.107–108<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">End of lessons — Chabashira explains tomorrow’s comprehensive provisional test.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Tomorrow on the 15th, all of you will be expected to complete a comprehensive provisional test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Provisional exam on the 15th has no effect on grades; questions similar to the finals; warning not to slack after promotion to Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her briefing closes the day right before he questions Horikita about Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C promoted — the warning names the promotion explicitly.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p39-1\">← Before: Named as the exam’s silent teacher<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p180-1\">→ After: The school’s intervention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p180-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the school s intervention announces the school will punish anyone spreading meaningless rumors  with close to twenty rumors circulating   i won t go into the details  but we ve already confirmed that there has been an ongoing exchange of slander amongst the first year students   moving forward  anyone found spreading meaningless rumors may be subjected to punishment  intervenes to stop the rumors against her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The school’s intervention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.180<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Announces the school will punish anyone spreading meaningless rumors, with close to twenty rumors circulating.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I won’t go into the details, but we’ve already confirmed that there has been an ongoing exchange of slander amongst the first-year students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Moving forward, anyone found spreading meaningless rumors may be subjected to punishment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Intervenes to stop the rumors against her.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v9-p107-1\">← Before: The provisional test briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p12-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji sudou-ken chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  exam results and the hallway encounter announces exam results  red line of fate  zero expulsions  praises the class   everyone  this next special exam will be the last one this year  reveals next special exam on march 8  watches hirata encourage the class  present in hallway during nagumo manabu conversation  not directly involved  horikita came third  tutored sudo in english  the encouragement line  everyone  this next special exam will be the last one this year  let s all work together and try our best  if we do  our class should be able to aim for class a without anyone being expelled  is spoken by hirata as he addresses the class  spreads a large piece of paper on the blackboard and draws the red line of fate   calm yourself  you ll know in a couple of minutes   are you feeling confident  ike   you studied hard  huh  yet you re still so uneasy   sudo  you always seem to be in the running for the lowest score  so how are you feeling   the results this time   everyone successfully passed the exam  these have been your best results so far   sudo  this past year  you managed to improve your grades better than anyone  you seemed confident that you d pass as well  i m looking forward to seeing how you ll succeed in the future  reports that all classes passed and class c came in 3rd by average score   i have to hand it to you guys  it may be a simple thing to say  but well done   nevertheless ike  you re getting a bit too excited  special exams aside  at an academic level  it s only natural for you to pass an exam like this one  and besides  this exam wasn t nearly as difficult as other national level exams  cuts into the cheerful atmosphere to announce the next special exam  scheduled for march 8th   most of you were probably already aware of this  but just because you ve finished this end of term exam doesn t mean that testing has finished for the year  there will be a particularly important special exam soon  and as in previous years  it s scheduled to begin on march 8th  reveals a relieved smile as the class responds to hirata s encouragement   the way things have been going recently  i m starting to think that all of you might just be able to graduate together two years from now   but don t get too cocky  your last exam is only a week away  and by no means will it be easy  questions ike about confidence and notes he came in last but passed  praises sudo s improvement and confidence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Exam results and the hallway encounter<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.12–29<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Announces exam results; red line of fate; zero expulsions; praises the class. Reveals next special exam on March 8; watches Hirata encourage the class. Present in hallway during Nagumo-Manabu conversation (not directly involved). Reports that all classes passed and Class C came in 3rd by average score. Cuts into the cheerful atmosphere to announce the next special exam, scheduled for March 8th. Reveals a relieved smile as the class responds to Hirata’s encouragement.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everyone. This next special exam will be the last one this year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Calm yourself. You’ll know in a couple of minutes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you feeling confident, Ike?”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita came third; tutored Sudō in English.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The encouragement line “Everyone. This next special exam will be the last one this year. Let’s all work together and try our best. If we do, our class should be able to aim for class A without anyone being expelled.” is spoken by Hirata as he addresses the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Spreads a large piece of paper on the blackboard and draws the red line of fate.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You studied hard, huh? Yet you’re still so uneasy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudō, you always seem to be in the running for the lowest score, so how are you feeling?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The results this time-”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Everyone successfully passed the exam. These have been your best results so far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudō. This past year, you managed to improve your grades better than anyone. You seemed confident that you’d pass as well. I’m looking forward to seeing how you’ll succeed in the future.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have to hand it to you guys. It may be a simple thing to say, but well done.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nevertheless Ike, you’re getting a bit too excited. Special exams aside, at an academic level, it’s only natural for you to pass an exam like this one. And besides, this exam wasn’t nearly as difficult as other national-level exams.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Most of you were probably already aware of this, but just because you’ve finished this end-of-term exam doesn’t mean that testing has finished for the year. There will be a particularly important special exam soon, and as in previous years, it’s scheduled to begin on March 8th.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The way things have been going recently, I’m starting to think that all of you might just be able to graduate together two years from now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But don’t get too cocky. Your last exam is only a week away, and by no means will it be easy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Questions Ike about confidence and notes he came in last but passed.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Praises Sudō’s improvement and confidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p30-1\">→ After: Ch.2: The Class Vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p30-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  the class vote announces the supplementary exam  the class is tense  explains  the class poll  rules  explains abstention is prohibited  20 million points can override expulsion  explains revote if all totals are zero  explains protection points and 20 million point override","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: The Class Vote<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.30–84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Announces the supplementary exam; the class is tense. Explains “The Class Poll” rules. Explains abstention is prohibited; 20 million points can override expulsion. Explains revote if all totals are zero. Explains protection points and 20 million point override.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Exam results and the hallway encounter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p197-1\">→ After: Ch.5: Observing the class discussion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p197-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 5  observing the class discussion ends homeroom after school and remains in the classroom as horikita asks everyone to stay  watches as horikita begins a class discussion about the special exam  is visibly impressed when horikita says they should decide who to expel rather than avoid the issue  after hirata declares he will vote for horikita and the discussion ends  chabashira asks if horikita is finished and then addresses the class  she tells the students she will not give her perspective on their discussion but urges them to think carefully before voting tomorrow   i m not going to provide my perspective on this discussion of yours  i believe everybody s participation has been valuable  i hope you all think carefully before you cast your votes tomorrow  observes her leadership of the class discussion and confirms when she is finished  witnesses his refusal to accept expelling a classmate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p197-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: Observing the class discussion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.197–226<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ends homeroom after school and remains in the classroom as Horikita asks everyone to stay. Watches as Horikita begins a class discussion about the special exam. Is visibly impressed when Horikita says they should decide who to expel rather than avoid the issue. After Hirata declares he will vote for Horikita and the discussion ends, Chabashira asks if Horikita is finished and then addresses the class. She tells the students she will not give her perspective on their discussion but urges them to think carefully before voting tomorrow.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not going to provide my perspective on this discussion of yours. I believe everybody’s participation has been valuable. I hope you all think carefully before you cast your votes tomorrow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Observes her leadership of the class discussion and confirms when she is finished.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Witnesses his refusal to accept expelling a classmate.<span class=\"pg\">p.221–225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2: The Class Vote<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p291-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Conducting the vote and aftermath<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p291-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae epilogue  conducting the vote and aftermath enters the classroom and begins the class poll  directing students to the voting room  tells yamauchi to be quiet and announces she will reveal the results  announces the praise vote rankings and states ayanokoji placed first with 42 votes  announces yamauchi haruki received 33 censure votes and is expelled  tries to calm yamauchi  asks for proof of his promise with sakayanagi  and orders him to leave  on monday  announces the final special exam to class c  oversees his expulsion from the class  announces his first place praise vote result  announces his second place praise vote result","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p291-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Conducting the vote and aftermath<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.291–362<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Enters the classroom and begins the Class Poll, directing students to the voting room. Tells Yamauchi to be quiet and announces she will reveal the results. Announces the praise-vote rankings and states Ayanokōji placed first with 42 votes. Announces Yamauchi Haruki received 33 censure votes and is expelled. Tries to calm Yamauchi, asks for proof of his promise with Sakayanagi, and orders him to leave. On Monday, announces the final special exam to Class C.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Oversees his expulsion from the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.291, 303–309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Announces his first-place praise-vote result.<span class=\"pg\">p.306<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Announces his second-place praise-vote result.<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v10-p197-1\">← Before: Ch.5: Observing the class discussion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p14-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"mashima-tomonari hoshinomiya-chie tsukishiro chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  after the staff meeting watches as mashima challenges acting director tsukishiro in the staff meeting  tells mashima that is enough when his resistance becomes futile  calls mashima and hoshinomiya aside in the hallway to discuss the upcoming exam  notes the 20 million private point override does not require class points this time but remains dissatisfied with tsukishiro s approach  warns hoshinomiya not to do anything reckless and denies fantasizing about reaching class a  rejects mashima s attempt to bring up the past and says personal feelings are irrelevant to the time passed  tells hoshinomiya to be careful and leaves for class c  stops his protests in the meeting and talks with him afterward  discusses the exam and their rivalry with her  is dissatisfied with his decisions   mashima sensei  that s enough   mashima sensei  hoshinomiya sensei  i d like to borrow the two of you for a bit   in any case  i can t help but feel dissatisfied about acting director tsukishiro s way of doing things   complaining isn t going to change anything  if you say too much  your neck will fly   you seem pretty calm even though we ve started to close the gap   no  even i m not that foolish   she s right  it s completely irrelevant   just refrain from doing anything careless  chie  that s all i m going to say","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: After the staff meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.14–25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches as Mashima challenges Acting Director Tsukishiro in the staff meeting. Tells Mashima that is enough when his resistance becomes futile. Calls Mashima and Hoshinomiya aside in the hallway to discuss the upcoming exam. Notes the 20 million private-point override does not require class points this time but remains dissatisfied with Tsukishiro’s approach. Warns Hoshinomiya not to do anything reckless and denies fantasizing about reaching Class A. Rejects Mashima’s attempt to bring up the past and says personal feelings are irrelevant to the time passed. Tells Hoshinomiya to be careful and leaves for Class C.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“…Mashima-sensei, that’s enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Mashima-sensei, Hoshinomiya-sensei. I’d like to borrow the two of you for a bit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In any case, I can’t help but feel dissatisfied about Acting Director Tsukishiro’s way of doing things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Stops his protests in the meeting and talks with him afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.18, 21–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Discusses the exam and their rivalry with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Is dissatisfied with his decisions.<span class=\"pg\">p.18, 22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Complaining isn’t going to change anything. If you say too much, your neck will fly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem pretty calm even though we’ve started to close the gap.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…No. Even I’m not that foolish.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s right. It’s completely irrelevant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just refrain from doing anything careless, Chie. That’s all I’m going to say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Announcing the Event Selection Exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p27-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  announcing the event selection exam enters class c on march 8 to announce the final special exam  explains the event selection exam as a comprehensive competition between classes  uses white and yellow cards to show that the class must propose ten events  prompts ike to speak and takes his rock paper scissors example seriously  explains event rules must be fair  understandable  and include tiebreakers to prevent draws  outlines the exam schedule and says seven events will be randomly selected from the five chosen by each class  explains that a commander is required  can intervene in events  and will be expelled if the class loses  says the class matchups will be decided by raffle among commanders after school  warns that losing could drop class c back to class d and explains class point changes  encourages him to ask questions and uses his example  answers her questions about events  rules  and matchups   without any further ado  i will now announce the final special exam   we will be finishing off the year with one final special exam where you ll be asked to show off a culmination of everything that you ve learned up until now  including knowledge  physical ability  cooperation  and maybe even a little bit of luck  in short  all of you will need to demonstrate the full extent of your potential   the special exam is called the  event selection exam  an exam where each class will compete in terms of their comprehensive ability  the class you ll be competing against will be decided in accordance with the rules  similar to how it was during the paper shuffle exam  attaches ten white cards and yellow name cards to the blackboard to illustrate the exam   to start things off  i ll use these cards to make the explanation easier for all of you to understand  there are ten white cards and a certain number of yellow ones  modeled after the number of students in the class   if there s something on your mind  why don t you speak up   either way  i just can t get ahold of myself unless you get this nonsense off your chest   okay  so let s suppose you chose rock paper scissors as one of the events","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Announcing the Event Selection Exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.27–41<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Enters Class C on March 8 to announce the final special exam. Explains the Event Selection Exam as a comprehensive competition between classes. Uses white and yellow cards to show that the class must propose ten events. Prompts Ike to speak and takes his rock-paper-scissors example seriously. Explains event rules must be fair, understandable, and include tiebreakers to prevent draws. Outlines the exam schedule and says seven events will be randomly selected from the five chosen by each class. Explains that a commander is required, can intervene in events, and will be expelled if the class loses. Says the class matchups will be decided by raffle among commanders after school. Warns that losing could drop Class C back to Class D and explains class-point changes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“-Without any further ado, I will now announce the final special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We will be finishing off the year with one final special exam where you’ll be asked to show off a culmination of everything that you’ve learned up until now, including knowledge, physical ability, cooperation, and maybe even a…”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The special exam is called the ‘Event Selection Exam’, an exam where each class will compete in terms of their comprehensive ability. The class you’ll be competing against will be decided in accordance with the rules, similar to…”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Encourages him to ask questions and uses his example.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Answers her questions about events, rules, and matchups.<span class=\"pg\">p.33, 35, 38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We will be finishing off the year with one final special exam where you’ll be asked to show off a culmination of everything that you’ve learned up until now, including knowledge, physical ability, cooperation, and maybe even a little bit of luck. In short, all of you will need to demonstrate the full extent of your potential.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The special exam is called the ‘Event Selection Exam’, an exam where each class will compete in terms of their comprehensive ability. The class you’ll be competing against will be decided in accordance with the rules, similar to how it was during the Paper Shuffle exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Attaches ten white cards and yellow name cards to the blackboard to illustrate the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To start things off, I’ll use these cards to make the explanation easier for all of you to understand. There are ten white cards and a certain number of yellow ones, modeled after the number of students in the class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s something on your mind, why don’t you speak up?”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Either way, I just can’t get ahold of myself unless you get this nonsense off your chest.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, so let’s suppose you chose rock-paper-scissors as one of the events.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p14-1\">← Before: Ch.1: After the staff meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p59-1\">→ After: Ch.3: Commanders’ meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p59-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka mashima-tomonari chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  commanders  meeting instructs the class to send the commander to the hallway and goes with ayanokoji to the special building  questions ayanokoji about volunteering as commander and warns him of the responsibility  attends the commanders  meeting and helps explain the exam day system  demonstrates the participant selection interface on the computer  accompanies him and oversees the commanders  meeting  explains the commander procedures together with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Commanders’ meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.59–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Instructs the class to send the commander to the hallway and goes with Ayanokōji to the special building. Questions Ayanokōji about volunteering as commander and warns him of the responsibility. Attends the commanders’ meeting and helps explain the exam-day system. Demonstrates the participant-selection interface on the computer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Accompanies him and oversees the commanders’ meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Explains the commander procedures together with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Announcing the Event Selection Exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p139-1\">→ After: Ch.4: Class and hallway<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p139-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 4  class and hallway casts a sidelong glance at horikita before leaving as the after school discussion begins  confronts hoshinomiya after seeing her talk with ayanokoji and says he is her student  listens as ayanokoji offers to explain the conversation  reacts dismissively when ayanokoji says they talked about room sharing  observes her taking charge of the discussion  intervenes in hoshinomiya s approach to him and questions their conversation  confronts her over talking to ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p139-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: Class and hallway<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.139, 168–169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Casts a sidelong glance at Horikita before leaving as the after-school discussion begins. Confronts Hoshinomiya after seeing her talk with Ayanokōji and says he is her student. Listens as Ayanokōji offers to explain the conversation. Reacts dismissively when Ayanokōji says they talked about room sharing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Observes her taking charge of the discussion.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Intervenes in Hoshinomiya’s approach to him and questions their conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Confronts her over talking to Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p59-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Commanders’ meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p328-1\">→ After: Ch.7: Exam day<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p328-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7  exam day follows ichinose and ryuen to the other side of the partition for the class b vs class d matchup  accompanies her as the exam matchups are separated  accompanies him to the class b vs class d side","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p328-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: Exam day<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.328<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Follows Ichinose and Ryūen to the other side of the partition for the Class B vs Class D matchup.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Accompanies her as the exam matchups are separated.<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Accompanies him to the Class B vs Class D side.<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p139-1\">← Before: Ch.4: Class and hallway<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p370-1\">→ After: Ch.8: Proctoring Class B vs Class D<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p370-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru mashima-tomonari chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 8  proctoring class b vs class d warns ryuen about his language when he pressures for the exam to continue  supports proceeding with the fifth event drawing  reprimands him during the matchup  acts alongside him as the exam proceeds","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p370-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8: Proctoring Class B vs Class D<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.370–371<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Warns Ryūen about his language when he pressures for the exam to continue. Supports proceeding with the fifth event drawing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reprimands him during the matchup.<span class=\"pg\">p.370–371<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Acts alongside him as the exam proceeds.<span class=\"pg\">p.371<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11-p328-1\">← Before: Ch.7: Exam day<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11_5-p47-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"","w":"tsukishiro sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  chess exam meeting participates in the meeting with ayanokoji  sakayanagi  tsukishiro  and other teachers concerning the chess exam  hears sakayanagi claim that ayanokoji was the original winner of the chess game and that the process was manipulated  takes part in the teachers  response as the issue of acting director tsukishiro s interference is pressed  confronts the acting director over exam interference  hears her accusation regarding the chess exam  present in the meeting involving his exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v11_5-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Chess exam meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.47–87<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Participates in the meeting with Ayanokōji, Sakayanagi, Tsukishiro, and other teachers concerning the chess exam. Hears Sakayanagi claim that Ayanokōji was the original winner of the chess game and that the process was manipulated. Takes part in the teachers’ response as the issue of Acting Director Tsukishiro’s interference is pressed.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Confronts the acting director over exam interference.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Hears her accusation regarding the chess exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Present in the meeting involving his exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p27-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  oaa app and special exam tells the class to install the oaa app on their phones  explains the oaa ratings and shows ayanokoji s first year scores  explains why social contribution has less weight on overall ability  announces the first special exam  second years pair with first years  explains the exam is an improved version of paper shuffle  explains partner choosing rules and the 5  late penalty  says the exam is very difficult and shows estimated scores by rating  calms ike and explains how to improve ratings  briefs him and the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: OAA app and special exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.27–49<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Tells the class to install the OAA app on their phones. Explains the OAA ratings and shows Ayanokōji’s first-year scores. Explains why Social Contribution has less weight on Overall Ability. Announces the first special exam: second-years pair with first-years. Explains the exam is an improved version of Paper Shuffle. Explains partner-choosing rules and the 5% late penalty. Says the exam is very difficult and shows estimated scores by rating. Calms Ike and explains how to improve ratings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Briefs him and the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p27-2\">→ After: Chabashira delivers the exam briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p27-2","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira delivers the exam briefing  everyone s here  right   while the world as a whole is slowly shifting over to a meritocracy  many japanese companies are still bound up in the concepts of seniority and lifetime employment   let s consider the concept of grade skipping   don t worry  it has been set up so that  no matter how many of you are unable to find partners  nobody will be left without one   pairs formed past the deadline will be subject to a 5  penalty to their overall score   the three extra students will have their exam scores doubled to make up for their missing partner  enters with an  extremely serious look  announces the partner exam calmly as if a normal lesson  gives the scripted grade skipping justification  and field s students  questions  laterally  indifferently  about penalties and the leftover first years","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p27-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira delivers the exam briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.27, 40–47<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Everyone&#x27;s here, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;While the world as a whole is slowly shifting over to a meritocracy, many Japanese companies are still bound up in the concepts of seniority and lifetime employment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;let&#x27;s consider the concept of grade skipping.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don&#x27;t worry. It has been set up so that, no matter how many of you are unable to find partners, nobody will be left without one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;pairs formed past the deadline will be subject to a 5% penalty to their overall score.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The three extra students will have their exam scores doubled to make up for their missing partner.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Enters with an &quot;extremely serious look,&quot; announces the partner exam calmly as if a normal lesson, gives the scripted grade-skipping justification, and field&#x27;s students&#x27; questions (laterally, indifferently) about penalties and the leftover first-years.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2: OAA app and special exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p50-1\">→ After: Chabashira&#x27;s score estimates and exam scope<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p50-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira s score estimates and exam scope  to tell you the truth  there are many extremely difficult questions on the exam   it ll definitely be one of the most challenging exams you ve taken so far   the exam has been designed so that even students with an e rating in academic ability can score at least 150 points without any prior preparation   if you study properly  you should be able to get a score close to those shown here  however  don t forget that if you re conceited and neglect your studies  you may end up with a lower score than this   it s unlikely that anyone will score over 90 points in each subject  let alone get a perfect score   that should be everything for the overview of the special exam you ll be taking in april  get ready to buckle down and do your best  score estimates by rating  e 150 200  d 200 250  c 250 300  b  350  a  400  two e rated partners would put the second year at risk of expulsion  blunt and matter of fact   frames the exam as one of the hardest yet  displays the score table  and warns against blindly trusting it  notes the test scope is mostly last year s material","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira&#x27;s score estimates and exam scope<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.50–52<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;To tell you the truth, there are many extremely difficult questions on the exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;ll definitely be one of the most challenging exams you&#x27;ve taken so far.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The exam has been designed so that even students with an E rating in Academic Ability can score at least 150 points without any prior preparation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you study properly, you should be able to get a score close to those shown here. However, don&#x27;t forget that if you&#x27;re conceited and neglect your studies, you may end up with a lower score than this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;it&#x27;s unlikely that anyone will score over 90 points in each subject, let alone get a perfect score.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That should be everything for the overview of the special exam you&#x27;ll be taking in April. Get ready to buckle down and do your best.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Score estimates by rating: E 150–200, D 200–250, C 250–300, B ~350, A ~400. Two E-rated partners would put the second-year at risk of expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blunt and matter-of-fact — frames the exam as one of the hardest yet, displays the score table, and warns against blindly trusting it; notes the test scope is mostly last year&#x27;s material.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p27-2\">← Before: Chabashira delivers the exam briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p143-1\">→ After: Ch.4: OAA refresh<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p143-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 4  oaa refresh oaa refreshes  34 new pairs formed  notes class 1 d has no partners yet  briefs the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p143-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: OAA refresh<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.143–147<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">OAA refreshes; 34 new pairs formed. Notes Class 1-D has no partners yet.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Briefs the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p50-1\">← Before: Chabashira&#x27;s score estimates and exam scope<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5: Library and study sessions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p205-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 5  library and study sessions oaa update noted  holds study sessions  supports her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: Library and study sessions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.205, 227<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">OAA update noted. Holds study sessions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Supports her.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p143-1\">← Before: Ch.4: OAA refresh<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p333-1\">→ After: Ch.6: Treating Ayanokōji’s hand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p333-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6  treating ayanokoji s hand is called by ayanokoji and brings a towel  treats his hand","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p333-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Treating Ayanokōji’s hand<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.333<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is called by Ayanokōji and brings a towel.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Treats his hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.333<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5: Library and study sessions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p349-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Calling Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p349-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae epilogue  calling ayanokoji calls ayanokoji to meet tsukishiro  asks about tsukishiro s plans  calls him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p349-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Calling Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.349–352<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Calls Ayanokōji to meet Tsukishiro. Asks about Tsukishiro’s plans.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Calls him.<span class=\"pg\">p.349–352<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p333-1\">← Before: Ch.6: Treating Ayanokōji’s hand<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p350-1\">→ After: Chabashira keeps the knife incident quiet; summons Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p350-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka tsukishiro chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira keeps the knife incident quiet  summons ayanokoji  how awfully cold  where would you be if not for my help the other day   i see i ve interrupted you  but it s urgent  acting director tsukishiro is asking for you  come   just so you know  according to mashima sensei  it seems like acting director tsukishiro didn t do anything out of the ordinary during the special exam   being stabbed with a knife is no laughing matter  you know  your father took action  didn t he   great  i need you here  i need you to be useful for me  your perfect score on the math test has made it clear to me just how special you really are after all  helped keep ayanokoji s knife wound confidential  worries tsukishiro might forcibly remove him  take you out of the school by force  and is proven right that his perfect math score reveals his special nature  leads him to tsukishiro s office  is secretly allied with him  keeps his secret and summons him  reports his apparent inactivity during the exam  is uneasy about his intentions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p350-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira keeps the knife incident quiet; summons Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.350–352<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How awfully cold. Where would you be if not for my help the other day?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I see I&#x27;ve interrupted you, but it&#x27;s urgent. Acting Director Tsukishiro is asking for you. Come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Just so you know… According to Mashima-sensei, it seems like Acting Director Tsukishiro didn&#x27;t do anything out of the ordinary during the special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Being stabbed with a knife is no laughing matter, you know. Your father took action, didn&#x27;t he?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Great. I need you here, I need you to be useful for me. Your perfect score on the math test has made it clear to me just how special you really are after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Helped keep Ayanokōji&#x27;s knife wound confidential, worries Tsukishiro might forcibly remove him (&quot;take you out of the school by force&quot;), and is proven right that his perfect math score reveals his special nature; leads him to Tsukishiro&#x27;s office.<span class=\"pg\">p.350–352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is secretly allied with him; keeps his secret and summons him.<span class=\"pg\">p.350–352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Reports his apparent inactivity during the exam; is uneasy about his intentions.<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v1-p349-1\">← Before: Epilogue: Calling Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p12-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae coverage note  passing mentions  chabashira had called him away and he had gone off somewhere  so he resorted to waiting in the classroom for him to return   in stark contrast to the overjoyed chabashira  his expression was somewhat resentful   yes  although i tried to confirm it with chabashira sensei tactfully  she didn t show signs she knew about it   shortly after  i could hear chabashira and kouenji from around the corner   chabashira  presumably standing face to face with kouenji  waited for his question   chabashira to leave  in a bit  the sound of her footsteps disappeared   as she entered the classroom  chabashira s natural expression turned serious  and the atmosphere grew heavy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Coverage note: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.12–139<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Chabashira had called him away and he had gone off somewhere, so he resorted to waiting in the classroom for him to return.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In stark contrast to the overjoyed Chabashira, his expression was somewhat resentful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Yes. Although I tried to confirm it with Chabashira-sensei tactfully, she didn’t show signs she knew about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Shortly after, I could hear Chabashira and Kouenji from around the corner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Chabashira, presumably standing face to face with Kouenji, waited for his question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Chabashira to leave. In a bit, the sound of her footsteps disappeared.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “As she entered the classroom, Chabashira’s natural expression turned serious, and the atmosphere grew heavy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1\">→ After: Chabashira waits<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka tsukishiro chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira waits waiting not far from the reception room when ayanokoji emerges under tsukishiro s watch  she falls in beside him casually   you ll be a bit of a celebrity from now on   ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment  how are you going to explain it to your own class  you ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous  but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math test  of course they won t leave you alone now  have you prepared for this scenario beforehand   this is going to be hard for you  prepare yourself to be bombarded with questions  the perfect score uproar has moved her  the homeroom teacher mask slips   she is overflowing with joy she tries to suppress  and fails with him specifically  she does not know the white room exists  she waits for him wrongly  eagerly  openly   to him  a manipulable counterpart  she was briefed against leaving without seeing him  the summons was hers to answer for too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira waits<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.23–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waiting not far from the reception room when Ayanokōji emerges under Tsukishiro&#x27;s watch; she falls in beside him casually.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’ll be a bit of a celebrity from now on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment, how are you going to explain it to your own class? You’ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous, but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math…”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This is going to be hard for you. Prepare yourself to be bombarded with questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ignoring the students in the other classes for a moment, how are you going to explain it to your own class? You’ve always done your best to try and seem inconspicuous, but suddenly you get a perfect score in that difficult math test. Of course they won’t leave you alone now. Have you prepared for this scenario beforehand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The perfect-score uproar has moved her; the homeroom-teacher mask slips — she is overflowing with joy she tries to suppress, and fails with him specifically; she does not know the White Room exists.<span class=\"pg\">p.24–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She waits for him wrongly, eagerly, openly — to him, a manipulable counterpart.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> She was briefed against leaving without seeing him; the summons was hers to answer for too.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p12-1\">← Before: Coverage note: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1\">→ After: The briefing continues<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the briefing continues the first class begins differently   she brings up the general exam topic after the attendance ceremony   it seems like everyone is here  that s good   i ve been with you guys for a while now  so i m sure you must ve guessed what this is   it s true that we ll be discussing the topic of the special exam after this  but to maintain the suspense for a bit longer  i ll pick it up later  first  let s talk about summer vacation   now i ll explain to you what ll happen in the summer vacation before it actually starts   from august 4 to august 11  you can enjoy to your heart s content your summer vacation on this luxury cruise for a total of eight days and seven nights  you can watch plays or pamper your taste buds  and there will not be anything like a special exam on the cruise   but in order to fully enjoy this cruise trip  you must successfully complete the next special exam   looks like you re indeed learning   usually  the course of events would be such that the test would start the same day or the next day  but unfortunately  this test is still a ways away  the next special exam will be held during summer vacation   you will have to participate in the  uninhabited island survival  special exam and compete with each other   you all probably recalled the uninhabited island survival exam from last year  but the exam this year is very different from the previous one  it s probably going to be tougher and more unforgiving than any other special exam before  of course  in turn  the number of class points and private points you can get has increased dramatically   first  i ll start by explaining the schedule in detail  there s no need to take notes now because you can download and check them afterwards on your smartphone or tablet   unfortunately  there will be no making up for that time  the shortening of the summer vacation is final   however  as compensation  there ll be a week s voyage on the luxury cruise ship  based on how you think about it  this week should be worth more than       the two weeks that you will lose  as i just said  that period of time during the voyage would be free time purely for your enjoyment   okay  now back to the topic at hand  although the uninhabited island survival exam was also held last year  the biggest difference between them can be said to be  scale  the duration of the exam is two weeks  and the area of the uninhabited island used for this exam will be larger than before   also  not just students from the same year  but all the students from all the school years will be competing against each other   the number of people you ll have to fight will also be higher than ever before   i know what you re saying  but i m going to state in advance that no exam can be 100  fair  even just taking you 2nd years as an example  there s almost a year s difference between the students who were born late and early in the same year  but you re still fighting on the same stage  right   if a first year asked for advice  as a senpai  it is the nature of a senior to at least answer it  but how much one says is up to them  it is the same when you ask the third years for advice   although there are more or less some gaps between the school years  everyone s basically fighting under the same stage  therefore  in order to fill in the gaps between the school years  the younger students will receive higher rewards  and their corresponding penalties will be lighter   in order to understand the rules of the uninhabited island survival exam  you must understand the groups   the next special exam  the uninhabited island survival exam  will have a rule which allows a maximum of 6 people to form a big group to work with each other  remember this first  if the people you group with are in the same year  you will be allowed to form the group regardless of any class boundaries   in the period from today till friday  july 16 inclusive  approximately four       weeks  you have the right to select up to two second year students of your choice to form a small group of a maximum of 3 people  the small groups form the basis of the big groups  however  although i said you could form the group with whoever you liked  there are still rules that exist  first  as i already said  you can only group up with students from the same grade  you can t form a group with 1st or 3rd years   and then  for the ratio of boys to girls in the next exam  when both boys and girls form a mixed group  the proportion of girls to boys must be at least 2 to 3   what happen   s if you don t form a group  or if you can t form a group   although there will also be students who think that it would be easier with only one person  there would be nothing better than having as many people as possible  apart from the advantages of having more people  special privileges are afforded to groups with more people  therefore  i would not recommend choosing to fight on your own except as a last resort   there s nothing but advantages to forming a group  but there s also a point worthy of attention  that is  once you ve established a group  you can t switch to another group whatever the reason may be   yeah  that s the key point  after the special exam starts  the small groups will be allowed to come together  2 groups of 3 people or 3 groups of 2 p   eople or even 6 lone wolves could form one big group  however  the conditions for forming a group still exist  in a big group of more than 4 people  the percentage of girls in the group must be at least 50   although you are allowed to group with anyone freely  it will be extremely difficult to form your ideal big group in the exam  situations  where one wants to form a big group with the maximum of 6 people but isn t able to  could be very common   okay  i also know that asking you guys to form groups as you please might still leave you confused  after all  if you don t know the contents of the exam  you won t be able to target the people you need   i cannot tell you the contents of the next exam  however  let me touch upon what kinds of abilities will be needed   in last year s uninhabited island survival exam  there were many students who were worried because they didn t get a chance to show their potential  but this year s exam can be considered to require  all types of abilities  academic ability  physical ability  mental ability  communication ability  in addition to the abilities i just listed  there s a high likelihood that you ll need to use the abilities in which you re good at   although forming a group with students who you are close with is important  it s very likely that the overall ability of the group will directly relate to the results you ll get on the special exam  so i advise everyone to consider the right talents when forming your groups   suppose that during the special exam  hirata is met with some kind of accident and could not continue the exam  of course  if he was participating alone  his group would be disqualified immediately  and will pay the penalties   while hirata will be disqualified and sent back to the ship  the other two members can continue the exam without any issues  and if that group persevered until the very end and got first place  hirata  as one of the group members  would also be considered as ending up in first place   no matter how many    people drop out in the middle of the exam  the group can continue to function without any issues until the last person drops out  to put it simply  the more people there are in a group  the more chances they have to survive   if you decide that there s no benefit in that  then you can just form groups with students of your own class  that is all   i ve given you all a tedious explanation so far  but there s more to explain apart from that   take a look at this   these are like items that can affect the uninhabited island survival exam  and everyone will receive one of these  except for one of them  there is no harm to having one of these  you can more or less understand that by reading the instructions   each student will receive one of these eight cards at random  the cards will be distributed tomorrow morning  and until the special exam begins  you can transfer or trade the card you get  so long as it is within your school year  anyone can look up who holds what card in the oaa  you can either sell them to students who want to buy them  or you could collect multiple cards by buying them  but the effects of the same cards do not stack  so there s absolutely no point in getting two identical cards   also  of the three special cards  they will be randomly distributed  and each school year will get only one of each type  therefore  it is possible that one       class might       coincidentally end up with all three of the special cards  that is all   there s plenty of time for you to think slowly about what strategy for grouping to use  the rewards structure and the card system as printed  she briefed him on the end  he watched every word","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The briefing continues<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.117–137<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The first class begins differently — she brings up the general exam topic after the attendance ceremony.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It seems like everyone is here, that’s good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve been with you guys for a while now, so I’m sure you must’ve guessed what this is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s true that we’ll be discussing the topic of the special exam after this, but to maintain the suspense for a bit longer, I’ll pick it up later. First, let’s talk about summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>41 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now I’ll explain to you what’ll happen in the summer vacation before it actually starts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From August 4 to August 11, you can enjoy to your heart’s content your summer vacation on this luxury cruise for a total of eight days and seven nights. You can watch plays or pamper your taste buds. And there will not be anything like a special exam on the cruise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But in order to fully enjoy this cruise trip, you must successfully complete the next special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you’re indeed learning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Usually, the course of events would be such that the test would start the same day or the next day, but unfortunately, this test is still a ways away. The next special exam will be held during summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You will have to participate in the “Uninhabited Island Survival” special exam and compete with each other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You all probably recalled the uninhabited island survival exam from last year, but the exam this year is very different from the previous one. It’s probably going to be tougher and more unforgiving than any other special exam before. Of course, in turn, the number of class points and private points you can get has increased dramatically.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First, I’ll start by explaining the schedule in detail. There’s no need to take notes now because you can download and check them afterwards on your smartphone or tablet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, there will be no making up for that time. The shortening of the summer vacation is final.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, as compensation, there’ll be a week’s voyage on the luxury cruise ship. Based on how you think about it, this week should be worth more than …  …  the two weeks that you will lose. As I just said, that period of time during the voyage would be free time purely for your enjoyment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, now back to the topic at hand. Although the uninhabited island survival exam was also held last year, the biggest difference between them can be said to be “scale”. The duration of the exam is two weeks, and the area of the uninhabited island used for this exam will be larger than before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, not just students from the same year, but all the students from all the school years will be competing against each other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The number of people you’ll have to fight will also be higher than ever before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know what you’re saying, but I’m going to state in advance that no exam can be 100% fair. Even just taking you 2nd years as an example, there’s almost a year’s difference between the students who were born late and early in the same year, but you’re still fighting on the same stage, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If a first-year asked for advice, as a senpai, it is the nature of a senior to at least answer it, but how much one says is up to them. It is the same when you ask the third years for advice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although there are more or less some gaps between the school years, everyone’s basically fighting under the same stage. Therefore, in order to fill in the gaps between the school years, the younger students will receive higher rewards, and their corresponding penalties will be lighter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In order to understand the rules of the uninhabited island survival exam, you must understand the groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next special exam, the uninhabited island survival exam, will have a rule which allows a maximum of 6 people to form a big group to work with each other. Remember this first; if the people you group with are in the same year, you will be allowed to form the group regardless of any class boundaries.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the period from today till Friday, July 16 inclusive, approximately four …  …  weeks, you have the right to select up to two second-year students of your choice to form a small group of a maximum of 3 people. The small groups form the basis of the big groups. However, although I said you could form the group with whoever you liked, there are still rules that exist. First, as I already said, you can only group up with students from the same grade. You can’t form a group with 1st or 3rd years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And then, for the ratio of boys to girls in the next exam, when both boys and girls form a mixed group, the proportion of girls to boys must be at least 2 to 3.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What happen … s if you don’t form a group… or if you can’t form a group?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although there will also be students who think that it would be easier with only one person, there would be nothing better than having as many people as possible. Apart from the advantages of having more people, special privileges are afforded to groups with more people. Therefore, I would not recommend choosing to fight on your own except as a last resort.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing but advantages to forming a group, but there’s also a point worthy of attention. That is, once you’ve established a group, you can’t switch to another group whatever the reason may be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that’s the key point. After the special exam starts, the small groups will be allowed to come together. 2 groups of 3 people or 3 groups of 2 p … eople or even 6 lone wolves could form one big group. However, the conditions for forming a group still exist. In a big group of more than 4 people, the percentage of girls in the group must be at least 50%.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although you are allowed to group with anyone freely, it will be extremely difficult to form your ideal big group in the exam. Situations, where one wants to form a big group with the maximum of 6 people but isn’t able to, could be very common.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, I also know that asking you guys to form groups as you please might still leave you confused. After all, if you don’t know the contents of the exam, you won’t be able to target the people you need.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I cannot tell you the contents of the next exam. However, let me touch upon what kinds of abilities will be needed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In last year’s uninhabited island survival exam, there were many students who were worried because they didn’t get a chance to show their potential. But this year’s exam can be considered to require ‘all types of abilities’. Academic ability, physical ability, mental ability, communication ability. In addition to the abilities I just listed, there’s a high likelihood that you’ll need to use the abilities in which you’re good at.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although forming a group with students who you are close with is important, it’s very likely that the overall ability of the group will directly relate to the results you’ll get on the special exam, so I advise everyone to consider the right talents when forming your groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Suppose that during the special exam, Hirata is met with some kind of accident and could not continue the exam. Of course, if he was participating alone, his group would be disqualified immediately, and will pay the penalties.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “While Hirata will be disqualified and sent back to the ship, the other two members can continue the exam without any issues. And if that group persevered until the very end and got first place, Hirata, as one of the group members, would also be considered as ending up in first place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No matter how many …  people drop out in the middle of the exam, the group can continue to function without any issues until the last person drops out. To put it simply, the more people there are in a group, the more chances they have to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you decide that there’s no benefit in that, then you can just form groups with students of your own class. That is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve given you all a tedious explanation so far, but there’s more to explain apart from that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Take a look at this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “These are like items that can affect the uninhabited island survival exam, and everyone will receive one of these. Except for one of them, there is no harm to having one of these. You can more or less understand that by reading the instructions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Each student will receive one of these eight cards at random. The cards will be distributed tomorrow morning, and until the special exam begins, you can transfer or trade the card you get, so long as it is within your school year. Anyone can look up who holds what card in the OAA. You can either sell them to students who want to buy them, or you could collect multiple cards by buying them. But the effects of the same cards do not stack, so there’s absolutely no point in getting two identical cards.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, of the three special cards, they will be randomly distributed, and each school year will get only one of each type. Therefore, it is possible that one …  …  class might …  …  coincidentally end up with all three of the special cards. That is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s plenty of time for you to think slowly about what strategy for grouping to use.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The rewards structure and the card system as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She briefed him on the end; he watched every word.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p23-1\">← Before: Chabashira waits<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p329-1\">→ After: Chabashira&#x27;s last blessing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p329-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira s last blessing the final briefing  all 39 students present  no sick ones   it s the start of summer vacation today  but you guys look like you re having a tough time  well  i suppose that can t be helped   then we ll start with the final check  if you re not feeling well now  you have to report it   no problems  that s great   this is not your first time taking a special exam  you have been fighting in this school for more than a year  and have overcome all manner of hardships  nonetheless  this special exam will not be easy to pass   i ve only got one wish for all of you  if you can  don t let a single one of your classmates disappear  and return to this classroom once again   we ll gather in the court in 10 minutes for a roll call  remember to go to the bathroom first  if you need to  her wish is aimed straight at him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p329-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira&#x27;s last blessing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.329<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The final briefing; all 39 students present; no sick ones.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s the start of summer vacation today, but you guys look like you’re having a tough time. Well, I suppose that can’t be helped.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Then we’ll start with the final check. If you’re not feeling well now, you have to report it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No problems, that’s great.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is not your first time taking a special exam. You have been fighting in this school for more than a year, and have overcome all manner of hardships. Nonetheless, this special exam will not be easy to pass.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve only got one wish for all of you. If you can, don’t let a single one of your classmates disappear, and return to this classroom once again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ll gather in the court in 10 minutes for a roll call. Remember to go to the bathroom first, if you need to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her wish is aimed straight at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v2-p117-1\">← Before: The briefing continues<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v3-p16-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira present at the briefing she is present during mashima s briefing about the uninhabited island exam rules  professional and informative","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v3-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira present at the briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.16–35<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She is present during Mashima&#x27;s briefing about the uninhabited island exam rules.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Professional and informative.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4-p268-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira and the boat  if you look closely at the end of the small boat  you could see mashima sensei and chabashira sensei  and that s how tsukishiro found out    narration   if they had checked all the students by gps  would the rescue have arrived and changed the situation  now  from the map  you can see that a student from class a and another from class d from the second year have lost the gps response of their watches  i think it was more of a question of trust      tsukishiro notes the rescue was inevitable   in the end  the boat landed and mashima sensei and chabashirasensei got off    narration   nothing has occurred here  ayanokouji kun and i just had a chat    tsukishiro to the teachers  the fight is made invisible by him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4-p268-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira and the boat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.268–272<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If you look closely at the end of the small boat, you could see Mashima-sensei and Chabashira-sensei. And that&#x27;s how Tsukishiro found out.” — narration.<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “If they had checked all the students by GPS, would the rescue have arrived and changed the situation? Now, from the map, you can see that a student from class A and another from class D from the second year have lost the GPS response of their watches. I think it was more of a question of trust. ” — Tsukishiro notes the rescue was inevitable.<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “In the end, the boat landed and Mashima-sensei and Chabashirasensei got off.” — narration.<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nothing has occurred here. Ayanokouji-kun and I just had a chat.” — Tsukishiro to the teachers; the fight is made invisible by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4-p271-1\">→ After: Chabashira and the rescue<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4-p271-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira and the rescue  nothing has occurred here  ayanokouji kun and i just had a chat    tsukishiro to the teachers  the boat crew includes chabashira sensei","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4-p271-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira and the rescue<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.271<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Nothing has occurred here. Ayanokouji-kun and I just had a chat.” — Tsukishiro to the teachers; the boat crew includes Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.271<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4-p268-1\">← Before: Chabashira and the boat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p161-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae mentions  chabashira seen on the island  mashima sensei and chabashira had seen him  so his role had become known","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p161-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mentions: Chabashira seen on the island<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.161<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Mashima-sensei and Chabashira had seen him, so his role had become known.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p225-1\">→ After: The late-night bar: Chabashira on the next special exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p225-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie mashima-tomonari ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the late night bar  chabashira on the next special exam after 1 a m  in the adults only bar lounge  meets mashima and hoshinomiya  admonishes the slumped  complaining hoshinomiya  you ve had more than enough rest   you never change   anyway  i m relieved about this uninhabited island exam  that the second years didn t lose  that is   nobody said that  however  i m just saying that this class is superior to the classes from previous years   what in the world are you talking about  when did i rely on ayanokoji   i thought last year s class poll wasn t that supposed to be a substitute for this   i m going back to my room  professional but secretly troubled  dismisses hoshinomiya s complaints  insists this year s class d is better than past years  and admits no reliance on ayanokoji  when mashima reveals the next special exam  the one she and hoshinomiya suffered 11 years ago  she falls silent  eyes closed  and leaves rather than discuss it   still haunted by having failed to save her class then  her drinking companion and old rival  they spar  and hoshinomiya brutally needles her for chasing after her  boring love  fellow teacher  reveals the next exam s outline  defends him as one of many promising students  denies relying on him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The late-night bar: Chabashira on the next special exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.225–232<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After 1 a.m. in the adults-only bar lounge, meets Mashima and Hoshinomiya; admonishes the slumped, complaining Hoshinomiya (&quot;you&#x27;ve had more than enough rest&quot;).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;you never change.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Anyway, I&#x27;m relieved about this uninhabited island exam. That the second-years didn&#x27;t lose, that is.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Nobody said that. However, I&#x27;m just saying that this class is superior to the classes from previous years.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What in the world are you talking about? When did I rely on Ayanokōji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I thought last year&#x27;s class poll…wasn&#x27;t that supposed to be a substitute for this?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m going back to my room.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Professional but secretly troubled —Dismisses Hoshinomiya&#x27;s complaints, insists this year&#x27;s Class D is better than past years, and admits no reliance on Ayanokōji; when Mashima reveals the next special exam (the one she and Hoshinomiya suffered 11 years ago) she falls silent, eyes closed, and leaves rather than discuss it — still haunted by having failed to save her class then.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Her drinking companion and old rival; they spar, and Hoshinomiya brutally needles her for chasing after her &quot;boring love.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225–233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Fellow teacher; reveals the next exam&#x27;s outline.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Defends him as one of many promising students; denies relying on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p161-1\">← Before: Mentions: Chabashira seen on the island<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p234-1\">→ After: Mentions: Sae-chan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p234-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae mentions  sae chan hoshinomiya   if sae chan had chosen the right answer  we would ve graduated from class a you know    she never names her   for us  graduating from class a was a long held dream    hoshinomiya  naming neither  mashima refuses hoshinomiya   i have no intention of getting involved with you or chabashira  it ll only cause trouble","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p234-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mentions: Sae-chan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.234–236<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Hoshinomiya: &quot;If Sae-chan had chosen the right answer, we would’ve graduated from Class A you know?&quot; — she never names her.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;For us, graduating from Class A was a long-held dream.&quot; — Hoshinomiya, naming neither.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Mashima refuses Hoshinomiya: &quot;I have no intention of getting involved with you or Chabashira. It&#x27;ll only cause trouble.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p225-1\">← Before: The late-night bar: Chabashira on the next special exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p257-1\">→ After: Chabashira and Tsukishiro in the concert hall<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p257-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka tsukishiro chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira and tsukishiro in the concert hall past 2am at the concert hall  chabashira and ayanokoji meet  tsukishiro reveals himself   dismissed as acting director  the chancellor reinstated  the last negotiation  the left hand handshake   students aren t allowed to leave their cabins at this time  you know   don t say that  this was the only time when we could be sure that it was just the two of us   don t worry  the teachers  night watch only lasts until midnight   when the summer vacation is over  the second semester will begin  and then  the next exam will take place   how do you analyse your class   a teacher who  while thinking she can t win  can t give up hope  in a nutshell  is it something like that   i m what kind of teacher do i look like to you   what if i told you i m throwing my past self behind   acting director tsukishiro  this is   you don t have to trust me  however  from the moment i showed up here  ayanokoji kun was aware of my presence  if there is a disturbance in emotions  it s communicated through the performance  but i didn t see even the slightest hint unrest in your performance  why was that   tsk   that s all right   i m not bothered   but no matter how exceptional you are  you are still only a child  you should understand that that man sent me here with your strength in mind   i didn t see it that way though   i m sorry  on account of me calling you out so easily  i gave acting director tsukishiro an opportunity to take advantage you  ayanokoji reports chabashira called him out at 2am   technically an off cabin violation  the meeting is also about the next exam  tsukishiro plays on the sexual misconduct framing  chabashira steps back  the scene ends with the boy scouts left hand handshake and a warning to disperse within five minutes  he corners her too   he knows she knows about the next exam  both are expendable to him now that chancellor sakayanagi is reinstated  he talks to her about uniting the class  plays the piano  fur elise  she applauds","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p257-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira and Tsukishiro in the concert hall<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.257–267<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Past 2am at the concert hall; Chabashira and Ayanokōji meet; Tsukishiro reveals himself — dismissed as Acting Director; the Chancellor reinstated; the last negotiation; the left-hand handshake.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Students aren&#x27;t allowed to leave their cabins at this time, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Don&#x27;t say that. This was the only time when we could be sure that it was just the two of us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don&#x27;t worry. The teachers’ night watch only lasts until midnight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the summer vacation is over, the second semester will begin. And then, the next exam will take place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How do you analyse your class?”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A teacher who, while thinking she can&#x27;t win, can&#x27;t give up hope. In a nutshell, is it something like that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m…What kind of teacher do I look like to you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What if I told you I&#x27;m throwing my past self behind?”<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Acting Director Tsukishiro, this is…”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don&#x27;t have to trust me. However, from the moment I showed up here, Ayanokōji-kun was aware of my presence. If there is a disturbance in emotions, it&#x27;s communicated through the performance, but I didn&#x27;t see even the slightest hint unrest in your performance… Why was that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Tsk…”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s all right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m not bothered.”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But no matter how exceptional you are, you are still only a child. You should understand that that man sent me here with your strength in mind.”<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn&#x27;t see it that way though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m sorry. On account of me calling you out so easily, I gave Acting Director Tsukishiro an opportunity to take advantage you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji reports Chabashira called him out at 2am — technically an off-cabin violation; the meeting is also about the next exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Tsukishiro plays on the sexual misconduct framing; Chabashira steps back; the scene ends with the Boy Scouts left-hand handshake and a warning to disperse within five minutes.<span class=\"pg\">p.261–264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> He corners her too — he knows she knows about the next exam; both are expendable to him now that Chancellor Sakayanagi is reinstated.<span class=\"pg\">p.261–267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He talks to her about uniting the class; plays the piano (&quot;Für Elise&quot;); she applauds.<span class=\"pg\">p.257–267<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v4_5-p234-1\">← Before: Mentions: Sae-chan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p7-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"narration","w":"hoshinomiya-chie chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira s monologue  the nightmare of the exam that cost her class a from her own pov  reveals a recurring nightmare she s never told anyone about   the events of the special exam in her third year  which always ends the same way   i keep having a recurring nightmare   by the time i reached my third year  the number of classmates who had left me had swelled to six   i believed that i could graduate from class a without having to leave anyone behind   my best friend  chie  approaches me with an angry expression and grabs my chest   the class  which had been united as one  collapsed in an instant   the relationship between the two of us ended just as it had begun  haunted by guilt   she was in class b  close to class a  and vowed to graduate without leaving anyone  the graduation special exam destroyed the class and cost her a  companion   a boy who reached for her hand under the evening sky  whom she called  irreplaceable  the memory is the source of her drive to protect her current class and her trauma over the coming exam  her best friend  chie  who angrily grabbed her in the nightmare   they were on opposite sides  the  companion  is unnamed in these pages  the text describes him as an irreplaceable friend and opposite sex person   no roster id assigned  no name on the page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira&#x27;s monologue: the nightmare of the exam that cost her Class A<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.7–8<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">From her own POV, reveals a recurring nightmare she&#x27;s never told anyone about — the events of the special exam in her third year, which always ends the same way.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I keep having a recurring nightmare.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;By the time I reached my third-year, the number of classmates who had left me had swelled to six.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I believed that I could graduate from Class A without having to leave anyone behind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;My best friend, Chie, approaches me with an angry expression and grabs my chest.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;The class, which had been united as one, collapsed in an instant.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;The relationship between the two of us ended just as it had begun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Haunted by guilt — she was in Class B, close to Class A, and vowed to graduate without leaving anyone; the graduation special exam destroyed the class and cost her a &quot;companion&quot; (a boy who reached for her hand under the evening sky, whom she called &quot;irreplaceable&quot;). The memory is the source of her drive to protect her current class and her trauma over the coming exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.7–8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Her best friend &quot;Chie,&quot; who angrily grabbed her in the nightmare — they were on opposite sides.<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The &quot;companion&quot; is unnamed in these pages; the text describes him as an irreplaceable friend and opposite-sex person — no roster id assigned (no name on the page).<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p13-1\">→ After: Chabashira announces the second-semester events<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p13-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira announces the second semester events arrives in homeroom looking the same as the first semester  outlines a packed second semester   an october sports festival  a november cultural festival  the school s first  midterm and final exams  plus a school trip   in this second semester  there are a few big events coming up for you guys   and in november  we will be holding a cultural festival  which will be our first cultural festival in the history of advanced nurturing high school   furthermore  in between these events  there will of course be midterm and final exams   the cultural festival will be held with a large number of guests   it is possible that there will be conflicts with other classes and grades regarding the location of the stall  but only one class per location can use that location   the school will not disclose which class will be doing what kind of performance or where the stalls will be until the day of the festival   if the information is leaked  you should expect to be faced with consequences   if there s something you can t get on the premises  you can apply for and get it from outside if you gain permission   these are the descriptions of the cultural festival and its rules  cultural festival  second years get 5 000 private points each  first years 5 500  third years 4 500  usable only for the festival  extra funds for student council club contributions  100 class points for 1st 4th place  50 for 5th 8th  none for 9th 12th  unused funds confiscated  stall locations cost points  main gate 1   10 000  one class per location  conflicts settled by bidding war to the school  stall details secret until the day  outside items allowed with permission  straightforward and professional   no drama in the delivery  explains the cultural festival first precisely because preparations need two months  ayanokoji notes the straightforwardness makes him suspect there is more to it  delivers the briefing  he notes she looks the same as first semester and suspects a hidden  more to it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira announces the second-semester events<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.13–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives in homeroom looking the same as the first semester; outlines a packed second semester — an October sports festival, a November cultural festival (the school&#x27;s first), midterm and final exams, plus a school trip.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;In this second semester, there are a few big events coming up for you guys.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;And in November, we will be holding a cultural festival, which will be our first cultural festival in the history of Advanced Nurturing High School.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Furthermore, in between these events, there will of course be midterm and final exams.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The cultural festival will be held with a large number of guests.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It is possible that there will be conflicts with other classes and grades regarding the location of the stall, but only one class per location can use that location.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The school will not disclose which class will be doing what kind of performance or where the stalls will be until the day of the festival.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If the information is leaked, you should expect to be faced with consequences.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If there&#x27;s something you can&#x27;t get on the premises, you can apply for and get it from outside if you gain permission.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;These are the descriptions of the cultural festival and its rules.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Cultural festival: second-years get 5,000 private points each (first-years 5,500; third-years 4,500), usable only for the festival; extra funds for student-council/club contributions; 100 class points for 1st–4th place, 50 for 5th–8th, none for 9th–12th; unused funds confiscated.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Stall locations cost points (Main Gate 1 = 10,000); one class per location; conflicts settled by bidding war to the school; stall details secret until the day; outside items allowed with permission.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Straightforward and professional — no drama in the delivery; explains the cultural festival first precisely because preparations need two months; Ayanokōji notes the straightforwardness makes him suspect there is more to it.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Delivers the briefing; he notes she looks the same as first semester and suspects a hidden &quot;more to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13–16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p7-1\">← Before: Chabashira&#x27;s monologue: the nightmare of the exam that cost her Class A<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p26-1\">→ After: Chabashira checks in on Ayanokōji after the maid-café reveal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p26-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira checks in on ayanokoji after the maid cafe reveal catches ayanokoji at the special building as sato s demonstration winds down  remarks on the performance and what they re planning   you ve seen sato and the others   not a bad idea   i was wondering how you were doing personally  so i thought i d come check on you  how have things been going   ayanokoji leading a maid cafe   horikita makes some pretty interesting suggestions   as for understanding otaku culture  that may be true   that s why it s important for you to supervise them   you ve got to be hungry for the opportunity to learn something other than studying   ayanokoji  next time you re free  can you give me a few minutes of your time   i ll send you a message soon  would that be okay   ayanokoji leading a maid cafe  is followed by  chabashira sensei laughed somewhat mirthlessly as she gave me a pitiful look    adjacent narration attribution  kept as printed  she asks for a few minutes of his time  he agrees  though she gives no reason on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira checks in on Ayanokōji after the maid-café reveal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.26–27<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Catches Ayanokōji at the special building as Satō&#x27;s demonstration winds down; remarks on the performance and what they&#x27;re planning.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;ve seen Satō and the others?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Not a bad idea.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was wondering how you were doing personally, so I thought I&#x27;d come check on you. How have things been going?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokōji leading a maid café...?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horikita makes some pretty interesting suggestions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As for understanding otaku culture, that may be true.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s why it&#x27;s important for you to supervise them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;ve got to be hungry for the opportunity to learn something other than studying.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokōji. Next time you&#x27;re free... can you give me a few minutes of your time?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll send you a message soon. Would that be okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> &quot;Ayanokōji leading a maid café...?&quot; is followed by &quot;Chabashira-sensei laughed somewhat mirthlessly as she gave me a pitiful look.&quot; — adjacent-narration attribution; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She asks for a few minutes of his time; he agrees, though she gives no reason on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p13-1\">← Before: Chabashira announces the second-semester events<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p29-1\">→ After: Chabashira: the Unanimous Voting Exam briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p29-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira  the unanimous voting exam briefing  before the sports festival in october  you will have to undergo a new special exam   the school is giving you the recognition you deserve  you second years have performed very well   happiness and sadness are two sides of the same coin  so the risk is the benefit  right   you ll be taking part in what s known as the  unanimous voting exam   in order to pass this special test  you must unanimously complete five questions within five hours   if you do not complete all questions within 5 hours you will lose 300 class points   it is strictly forbidden to make any agreements with other students that bind them to vote for a particular option in this exam  professional and quietly proud   frames the exam as recognition of the second years  strong performance  walks the class through examples  and stresses the anti collusion and overtime expulsion rules  ayanokoji senses she s inwardly happy  her  sweet side  showing more than ever  delivers the exam  he reads her restrained pride  she calmly accepts the risk as benefit framing  winning approval","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira: the Unanimous Voting Exam briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.29–44<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Before the sports festival in October, you will have to undergo a new special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The school is giving you the recognition you deserve; you second years have performed very well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Happiness and sadness are two sides of the same coin. So the risk is the benefit, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;ll be taking part in what&#x27;s known as the &#x27;Unanimous Voting Exam&#x27;.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In order to pass this special test, you must unanimously complete five questions within five hours.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you do not complete all questions within 5 hours you will lose 300 class points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;it is strictly forbidden to make any agreements with other students that bind them to vote for a particular option in this exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Professional and quietly proud — frames the exam as recognition of the second-years&#x27; strong performance, walks the class through examples, and stresses the anti-collusion and overtime-expulsion rules; Ayanokōji senses she&#x27;s inwardly happy (her &quot;sweet side&quot; showing more than ever).<span class=\"pg\">p.29–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Delivers the exam; he reads her restrained pride.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She calmly accepts the risk-as-benefit framing, winning approval.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p26-1\">← Before: Chabashira checks in on Ayanokōji after the maid-café reveal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p70-1\">→ After: Coverage-gate mention records<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p70-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae coverage gate mention records yagami plays the recording of chabashira s briefing for kushida   yagami pressed the play button and heard chabashira s voice in the middle of the explanation  giving an overview of the special unanimous voting exam announced for the second year students   on the side of the podium  the facilitator of this special exam  chabashira sensei  and the teacher in charge of monitoring  are stationed at the back of the classroom   even chabashira sensei  who announced the standard phrases  showed signs of fatigue   i thought so  but chabashira sensei just stood there and stared at the students absentmindedly   while checking the time  chabashira sensei resumed the proceedings that had been halted   the voices were quickly drowned out by the sharp stares of chabashira sensei   now  let me move on to the third question  chabashira sensei s demeanor hadn t changed since the beginning  but there was a slight change in the tone of her voice   chabashira sensei was momentarily at a loss for words   chabashira sensei muttered to herself as if she were prepared for everything and continued on her way   it seemed that all the votes had been cast in about 30 seconds  and chabashira sensei displayed the results on a monitor   chabashira sensei informed us of the time   if i were to get a confirmation from chabashira sensei  i can say that i know the flow of points at this moment  and you can t avoid that the situation will be bad at once   there is some skepticism as to whether the teacher  chabashira  is aware of the transfer of points between individuals at any time  and whether she would leak personal information   if you want  i can ask chabashira sensei to bring my phone now   you know what chabashira sensei said  private points are for your own protection   staring at chabashira sensei  haruka makes a formal statement   chabashira sensei  who had been watching the fierce exchange  forgot to report the end of the exam and just looked at airi and haruka   only if you have 20 million private points at this moment and use them    she tries to continue the explanation and stops halfway   airi replies to chabashira sensei in a quiet voice  but without hesitation   as for sakura  you will have to come with me to the staff room afterwards  so stay in the classroom","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p70-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Coverage-gate mention records<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.70–242<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Yagami plays the recording of Chabashira&#x27;s briefing for Kushida: &quot;Yagami pressed the play button and heard Chabashira&#x27;s voice in the middle of the explanation, giving an overview of the special unanimous voting exam announced for the second-year students.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;On the side of the podium, the facilitator of this special exam, Chabashira-sensei, and the teacher in charge of monitoring, are stationed at the back of the classroom.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Even Chabashira-sensei, who announced the standard phrases, showed signs of fatigue.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;I thought so, but Chabashira-sensei just stood there and stared at the students absentmindedly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;While checking the time, Chabashira-sensei resumed the proceedings that had been halted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;the voices were quickly drowned out by the sharp stares of Chabashira-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Now, let me move on to the third question.&quot; Chabashira-sensei&#x27;s demeanor hadn&#x27;t changed since the beginning, but there was a slight change in the tone of her voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei was momentarily at a loss for words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei muttered to herself as if she were prepared for everything and continued on her way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;It seemed that all the votes had been cast in about 30 seconds, and Chabashira-sensei displayed the results on a monitor.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei informed us of the time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;If I were to get a confirmation from Chabashira-sensei, I can say that I know the flow of points at this moment, and you can&#x27;t avoid that the situation will be bad at once.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;There is some skepticism as to whether the teacher, Chabashira, is aware of the transfer of points between individuals at any time, and whether she would leak personal information.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;If you want, I can ask Chabashira-sensei to bring my phone now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;You know what Chabashira-sensei said. Private points are for your own protection-&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Staring at Chabashira-sensei, Haruka makes a formal statement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei, who had been watching the fierce exchange, forgot to report the end of the exam and just looked at Airi and Haruka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Only if you have 20 million private points at this moment and use them...&quot; — she tries to continue the explanation and stops halfway.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Airi replies to Chabashira-sensei in a quiet voice, but without hesitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;As for Sakura, you will have to come with me to the staff room afterwards, so stay in the classroom.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p29-1\">← Before: Chabashira: the Unanimous Voting Exam briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p76-1\">→ After: Chabashira&#x27;s morning (her POV): the mirror, the exam nerves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p76-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ikari-sensei chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira s morning  her pov  the mirror  the exam nerves at 6 a m  the alarm clock kept for ten years tumbles off the mini table  the battery cover taped on with cellophane tape  sleep deprived  dark circles under her eyes  she applies makeup  the skin s elasticity is gone  eleven years since she saw  him   it s already six o clock   i ll be more careful tomorrow  so forgive me   calm down  this isn t my fight  the situation is different from that time  i m sure my current class will be able to get through this without a hitch   prepare yourself  morning meeting with the four homeroom teachers  ikari sensei auditing  hoshinomiya sensei  chie  questions why homeroom teachers remain assigned to their own class  previously shuffled  sakayanagi sensei answers it s the fundamental decision of the top brass  ikari sensei explains the exam s reach   um  i know it s a little late  but do you have a minute    chie s line  adjacent attributed  in this special exam  our teachers  utmost concern should be to not intervene in the exam    ikari sensei s line  printed untagged in the print  named via the auditing narration outside the staff room chie confronts her   it s finally here  sae chan  you couldn t sleep last night because you were thinking about the special exam  right     sae chan doesn t have the qualifications to aim for class a  never forget that  she cannot lift her head until the corner   this class has nothing to do with me  it doesn t matter if the students clear it easily or not  the print carries the drop cap style at the chapter head  translator credit changes mid volume in this book  princeyg 6558 pp 1 28 and pp 76 167 and pp 232 243  rhymar 7433 pp 29 75 and pp 168 231    kept as printed  see the volume s notes   sakayanagi sensei   a teacher at the morning meeting  is not on the roster   two lines are printed under him  no roster id assigned  owner to resolve  ambiguous with sakayanagi arisu and sakayanagi narimori  eleven years since she saw  him  applies makeup with trembling hands  lies to herself that  this isn t my fight    the mirror tells the truth  ikari sensei warns the teachers to not intervene  advice    warning  repetition   pay cut  malicious intervention   demotion  her sleep has been wrecked for days  her oldest sparring partner   chie spotted the insomnia instantly and needles her with it  auditing teacher  his warning is formal  his imagery is terrifying","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira&#x27;s morning (her POV): the mirror, the exam nerves<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.76–81<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At 6 a.m. the alarm clock kept for ten years tumbles off the mini-table; the battery cover taped on with cellophane tape; sleep deprived, dark circles under her eyes; she applies makeup; the skin&#x27;s elasticity is gone; eleven years since she saw &quot;him.&quot; Morning meeting with the four homeroom teachers (Ikari-sensei auditing); Hoshinomiya-sensei (Chie) questions why homeroom teachers remain assigned to their own class (previously shuffled); Sakayanagi-sensei answers it&#x27;s the fundamental decision of the top brass; Ikari-sensei explains the exam&#x27;s reach. Outside the staff room Chie confronts her: &quot;It&#x27;s finally here, Sae-chan... You couldn&#x27;t sleep last night because you were thinking about the special exam, right?&quot; — &quot;Sae-chan doesn&#x27;t have the qualifications to aim for Class A. Never forget that.&quot; She cannot lift her head until the corner.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ikari-sensei\">Ikari-sensei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s already six o&#x27;clock...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ll be more careful tomorrow, so forgive me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Calm down. This isn&#x27;t my fight. The situation is different from that time. I&#x27;m sure my current class will be able to get through this without a hitch.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Prepare yourself...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Um, I know it&#x27;s a little late, but do you have a minute?&quot; — Chie&#x27;s line; adjacent-attributed<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In this special exam, our teachers&#x27; utmost concern should be to not intervene in the exam.&quot; — Ikari-sensei&#x27;s line; printed untagged in the print; named via the auditing narration<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This class has nothing to do with me. It doesn&#x27;t matter if the students clear it easily or not.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The print carries the drop-cap style at the chapter head; translator credit changes mid-volume in this book (PrinceYG#6558 pp.1–28 and pp.76–167 and pp.232–243; Rhymar#7433 pp.29–75 and pp.168–231) — kept as printed; see the volume&#x27;s notes.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> &quot;Sakayanagi-sensei&quot; (a teacher at the morning meeting) is not on the roster — two lines are printed under him; no roster id assigned; owner to resolve (ambiguous with sakayanagi-arisu and sakayanagi-narimori).<span class=\"pg\">p.78–79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Eleven years since she saw &quot;him&quot;; applies makeup with trembling hands; lies to herself that &quot;This isn&#x27;t my fight.&quot; — the mirror tells the truth; Ikari-sensei warns the teachers to not intervene (&quot;advice&quot; = warning, repetition = pay cut; malicious intervention = demotion); her sleep has been wrecked for days.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Her oldest sparring partner — Chie spotted the insomnia instantly and needles her with it.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ikari-sensei<\/b> Auditing teacher; his warning is formal; his imagery is terrifying.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p70-1\">← Before: Coverage-gate mention records<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p84-1\">→ After: Coverage-gate mention records<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p84-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae coverage gate mention records  two minutes before the start  the homeroom teacher  chabashira sensei  begins to explain   raising her hand  horikita  who was sitting in front of the chabashira sensei  stood up and then turned around   raised her voice towards chabashira sensei","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p84-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Coverage-gate mention records<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.84–225<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Two minutes before the start, the homeroom teacher, Chabashira-sensei, begins to explain.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Raising her hand, Horikita, who was sitting in front of the Chabashira-sensei, stood up and then turned around.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;raised her voice towards Chabashira-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p76-1\">← Before: Chabashira&#x27;s morning (her POV): the mirror, the exam nerves<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p106-1\">→ After: Chabashira&#x27;s collapse; her old story<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p106-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira s collapse  her old story as the final question begins  her complexion has visibly worsened over the exam  hirata asks if she s okay  but she denies it  unaware  or unwilling to admit  her own condition   the  60 second count will now begin  students are asked to  begin voting    her voice shaky  teachers are not allowed to guide the students to a particular choice   however  may i tell you an old story   i also attended the advanced nurturing high school  and i ve taken this special exam when i was a student   the last one you re facing right now is the same word for word   that is to give it your all with no regrets   whichever choice you decide to find a path that will not leave you regretting the outcome  visibly ill but determined   stumbles and nearly falls at the podium  risks punishment by telling an  old story   she took this same exam 11 years ago  the last question identical    offering not guidance but heartfelt advice to choose without regret  the monitoring teacher lets her speak to the end  he notes her condition is tied to the final question  her own trauma  she provides the students words to face the exam  he asks if she s okay  she brushes it off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira&#x27;s collapse; her old story<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.106–125<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As the final question begins, her complexion has visibly worsened over the exam; Hirata asks if she&#x27;s okay, but she denies it, unaware (or unwilling to admit) her own condition.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The... 60-second count will now begin. Students are asked to... begin voting.&quot; — her voice shaky<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Teachers are not allowed to guide the students to a particular choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;However, may I tell you an old story?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I also attended the Advanced Nurturing High School. And I&#x27;ve taken this special exam when I was a student.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;the last one you&#x27;re facing right now is the same word for word.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That is to give it your all with no regrets.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Whichever choice you decide to find a path that will not leave you regretting the outcome.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Visibly ill but determined — stumbles and nearly falls at the podium; risks punishment by telling an &quot;old story&quot; (she took this same exam 11 years ago, the last question identical) — offering not guidance but heartfelt advice to choose without regret; the monitoring teacher lets her speak to the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He notes her condition is tied to the final question (her own trauma); she provides the students words to face the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He asks if she&#x27;s okay; she brushes it off.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p84-1\">← Before: Coverage-gate mention records<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p232-1\">→ After: Chabashira&#x27;s confession on the roof: a farewell to the past<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p232-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke sakura-airi chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira s confession on the roof  a farewell to the past meets ayanokoji on the rooftop stairs  as promised at 6 p m  unlocks the roof and leans on the railing  stressed after the exam  offers her  confession   the  sacrament of forgiveness   every year  the school s attitude toward rooftop use is getting tougher   if you forgive me  you can listen to my confession   we  the 3rd year class b  were on the verge of catching up with class a before the graduation exam   eventually  my classmates slowly began to lean towards the idea that class a would make the sacrifice to get the 100 class points   i  of all people  was the one who kept voting against it   for me  that student was a leader  a friend  and a  and a lover more important than anyone else   i protect him  he protects me  such a stalemate went on and on   but when the unanimous special exams ended  our relationship naturally ended as well   i will fulfill my role as a teacher to guide the students in my class to continue fighting without regret   i ve decided  ayanokoji  i m going to make sure our class graduates from class a  anyway i can  finally unburdened   recounts how  11 years ago  her class  then class b  73 points from class a  faced the same exam  her lover  a  combination of hirata and ike  the class leader  volunteered to be expelled  and she alone voted against to protect him  costing them 300 points and a 523 point deficit  they never saw each other again  hearing ayanokoji s analysis of her mistake  she makes peace with the past  a farewell to the past  and resolves to lead her current class to class a   visibly  radiant  her mind finally caught up to her age  confides in him and accepts his blunt analysis  admits she could never make decisions  without hesitation  as he does  her old lover was  a combination of hirata and ike    leader and mood maker  asks whether he could have saved sakura","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p232-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira&#x27;s confession on the roof: a farewell to the past<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.232–239<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ayanokōji on the rooftop stairs (as promised at 6 p.m.), unlocks the roof and leans on the railing, stressed after the exam; offers her &quot;confession&quot; (the &quot;Sacrament of Forgiveness&quot;).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Every year, the school&#x27;s attitude toward rooftop use is getting tougher.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you forgive me, you can listen to my confession...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We, the 3rd year Class B, were on the verge of catching up with Class A before the graduation exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Eventually, my classmates slowly began to lean towards the idea that Class A would make the sacrifice to get the 100 class points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I, of all people, was the one who kept voting against it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For me, that student was a leader, a friend, and a... and a lover more important than anyone else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I protect him, he protects me. Such a stalemate went on and on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But when the unanimous special exams ended, our relationship naturally ended as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I will fulfill my role as a teacher to guide the students in my class to continue fighting without regret.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ve decided, Ayanokōji. I&#x27;m going to make sure our class graduates from Class A, anyway I can.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Finally unburdened — recounts how, 11 years ago, her class (then Class B, 73 points from Class A) faced the same exam; her lover (a &quot;combination of Hirata and Ike,&quot; the class leader) volunteered to be expelled, and she alone voted against to protect him, costing them 300 points and a 523-point deficit; they never saw each other again. Hearing Ayanokōji&#x27;s analysis of her mistake, she makes peace with the past (&quot;a farewell to the past&quot;) and resolves to lead her current class to Class A — visibly &quot;radiant,&quot; her mind finally caught up to her age.<span class=\"pg\">p.232–239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Confides in him and accepts his blunt analysis; admits she could never make decisions &quot;without hesitation&quot; as he does.<span class=\"pg\">p.232–239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Her old lover was &quot;a combination of Hirata and Ike&quot; — leader and mood-maker.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Asks whether he could have saved Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v5-p106-1\">← Before: Chabashira&#x27;s collapse; her old story<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p28-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke ichinose-honami chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  attendance  the sports festival rules she takes attendance   kushida  hasebe and wan   three students are absent  that s unusual    hasebe and wan called in sick and she accepted their leaves  kushida has not contacted her   she will call her afterwards to check  she throws in an exaggerated possibility that kushida just overslept  she warns the class that prolonged absences will start costing class points   kushida  hasebe and wan   three students are absent  that s unusual   hasebe and wan have both called in sick  and i ve accepted their leaves  i haven t heard from kushida  so i ll call her afterwards to check  i ll quickly find out if she just overslept  or if she was so sick she couldn t wake up   don t look so anxious  a day or two of absences won t hurt your class points  after all  it is entirely possible that three people just happened to fall sick at the same time   that said  that won t hold if their absences continue  especially if it turns out that they re feigning illness   little by little  problems will start to surface   maybe calling it a pretend illness is too much  all i m saying is  there s a limit to how long you can be ill without giving us the specific name of your sickness  i d like to see them recover as soon as possible  she announces the sports festival s rules   the student council president s experiment   a realization of his experiment  and will heavily incorporate his proposal to emphasize individual ability  she walks the class through the summary and rules on the monitor  9am 4pm with a 12pm 1pm break  parallel events  everyone starts with 5 points  at least 5 events required  1 point participation prize  from the 6th event onwards 1 point cost with no prize  max 10 events  forfeiture under 5 events  unsigned withdrawals  2 points  fundamental  individual  vs special  team   2  competitions  1st 5   2nd 3   3rd 1 points  per year class ranking rewards 150   50   0    150  individual rewards 2m private points or a class change ticket  limited time    1m   500k  forfeiture of ticket if events tie  pre booking via app from 10pm  cancel up to three times  100m race walkthrough  club restriction clause   while their absence is concerning  we can t get stuck on that  the unanimous consent special exam is now over  and all of you have to turn and face the next challenge   i m going to explain the details of the sports festival  and the special rules in play this year  listen carefully   the new way for this school that the student council president has been proposing is being accepted  such as with the uninhabited island exam  this sports festival will be a realization of his experiment  and will heavily incorporate his proposal to emphasize individual ability   i am sure more than a few of you are worried about this  but this time the sports festival has been adjusted to ensure that nobody will get expelled for lack of ability  and nobody will have to suffer any penalty alone  after all  no individual can be the perfect embodiment of athletic and academic skills at once   that is this year s sports festival  the summary and an outline of the rules   participating in competitions and winning the rewards from a high rank finish will be your first priority  but you must also prepare a careful plan for the day   since the rewards for the team battles vary from event to event  you will be able to check them separately   those were the rewards for the classes  now i will announce the individual rewards   the school is being quite careful about the introduction of this new system  even the protect points were unheard of in previous generations  and these are being introduced not long after  however  students who have demonstrated their individual ability naturally have a right to rise to the top   you will receive the right to change classes  but  that doesn t mean you can get it made right away  therefore  the words  limited time  here refer to the period during which you can use the ticket  you can only exercise this right during the second semester  therefore  if you haven t done so by the time the third semester starts  the ticket will expire   both the boy and the girl who place first will get to choose whichever they want  sudou  if you are planning to reach the top through individual battles  you should carefully think about what you want   moving on  let s go into a bit more detail  there will be competitions which will be opened in advance  and events which will only be opened on the day of the festival  so  there will be events for you to participate in even if you go into the festival entirely unprepared   because of restrictions on the number of participants and time limits  it is not guaranteed that you will be able to participate in all of the events you want to  if you plan your day without consideration for the schedule  you might fail to arrive at the event on time and will be considered as having withdrawn from it  don t forget that you run the risk of losing points that way   for the events that will be opened beforehand  you will be able to use a special app to pre book your participation from 10pm today  it will be first come first serve across the entire school  you will be allowed to cancel until one week before the sports festival  but you won t be able to use the cancel feature more than thrice  the deadline for pre booking is two days before the sports festival  if you haven t booked the upper limit of five events by then  you will automatically be assigned to the open slots   for demonstration  let s sign up for the 100 meter race   another important point is that you cannot participate in an event if it belongs to a club you are or have ever been a member of  hirata cannot participate in events related to soccer and sudou cannot participate in events related to basketball   it is true that they are very alike  if you press the button for a time slot  you will be able to see in real time who will be participating in that event at that time   yes  but  sooner or later those people will run into the three time limit of the cancel feature   and  if multiple students individually get the same points  the private point reward will be split between them and they will not be able to get the class change ticket  the corpus prints the attendance line with    en dash  between  wan  and  three students    kept as printed  he asks the first question about special rules  the individual rewards are made for him  the club restriction names him and sudo in one clause  her class has 40 starting points more than the absentee short class  400 vs 380","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Attendance; the Sports Festival rules<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.28–33<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes attendance: “Kushida, Hasebe and Wan – three students are absent. That’s unusual.” — Hasebe and Wan called in sick and she accepted their leaves; Kushida has not contacted her — she will call her afterwards to check; she throws in an exaggerated possibility that Kushida just overslept; she warns the class that prolonged absences will start costing class points. She announces the Sports Festival&#x27;s rules — the Student Council President&#x27;s experiment, “a realization of his experiment, and will heavily incorporate his proposal to emphasize individual ability”; she walks the class through the Summary and Rules on the monitor: 9AM–4PM with a 12PM–1PM break, parallel events; everyone starts with 5 points, at least 5 events required, 1 point participation prize, from the 6th event onwards 1 point cost with no prize; max 10 events; forfeiture under 5 events; unsigned withdrawals −2 points; fundamental (individual) vs special (team, ≥2) competitions; 1st 5 / 2nd 3 / 3rd 1 points; per-year class ranking rewards 150 / 50 / 0 / −150; individual rewards 2M private points or a Class Change Ticket (Limited Time) / 1M / 500k; forfeiture of ticket if events tie; pre-booking via app from 10PM; cancel up to three times; 100m race walkthrough; club restriction clause.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Kushida, Hasebe and Wan – three students are absent. That’s unusual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hasebe and Wan have both called in sick, and I’ve accepted their leaves. I haven’t heard from Kushida, so I’ll call her afterwards to check. I’ll quickly find out if she just overslept, or if she was so sick she couldn’t wake…”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t look so anxious. A day or two of absences won’t hurt your class points. After all, it is entirely possible that three people just happened to fall sick at the same time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hasebe and Wan have both called in sick, and I’ve accepted their leaves. I haven’t heard from Kushida, so I’ll call her afterwards to check. I’ll quickly find out if she just overslept, or if she was so sick she couldn’t wake up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That said, that won’t hold if their absences continue. Especially if it turns out that they’re feigning illness – little by little, problems will start to surface.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe calling it a pretend illness is too much. All I’m saying is, there’s a limit to how long you can be ill without giving us the specific name of your sickness. I’d like to see them recover as soon as possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “While their absence is concerning, we can’t get stuck on that. The Unanimous Consent Special Exam is now over, and all of you have to turn and face the next challenge.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to explain the details of the Sports Festival, and the special rules in play this year. Listen carefully.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The new way for this school that the Student Council President has been proposing is being accepted, such as with the Uninhabited Island Exam. This Sports Festival will be a realization of his experiment, and will heavily incorporate his proposal to emphasize individual ability.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am sure more than a few of you are worried about this, but this time the Sports Festival has been adjusted to ensure that nobody will get expelled for lack of ability, and nobody will have to suffer any penalty alone. After all, no individual can be the perfect embodiment of athletic and academic skills at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That is this year’s Sports Festival, the summary and an outline of the rules.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Participating in competitions and winning the rewards from a high-rank finish will be your first priority, but you must also prepare a careful plan for the day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since the rewards for the team battles vary from event to event, you will be able to check them separately.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Those were the rewards for the classes. Now I will announce the individual rewards.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school is being quite careful about the introduction of this new system. Even the Protect Points were unheard of in previous generations, and these are being introduced not long after. However, students who have demonstrated their individual ability naturally have a right to rise to the top.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You will receive the right to change classes. But, that doesn’t mean you can get it made right away. Therefore, the words ‘Limited Time’ here refer to the period during which you can use the ticket. You can only exercise this right during the second semester. Therefore, if you haven’t done so by the time the third semester starts, the ticket will expire.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Both the boy and the girl who place first will get to choose whichever they want. Sudou, if you are planning to reach the top through individual battles, you should carefully think about what you want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Moving on, let’s go into a bit more detail. There will be competitions which will be opened in advance, and events which will only be opened on the day of the festival. So, there will be events for you to participate in even if you go into the festival entirely unprepared.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because of restrictions on the number of participants and time limits, it is not guaranteed that you will be able to participate in all of the events you want to. If you plan your day without consideration for the schedule, you might fail to arrive at the event on time and will be considered as having withdrawn from it. Don’t forget that you run the risk of losing points that way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the events that will be opened beforehand, you will be able to use a special app to pre-book your participation from 10PM today. It will be first come first serve across the entire school. You will be allowed to cancel until one week before the Sports Festival, but you won’t be able to use the cancel feature more than thrice. The deadline for pre-booking is two days before the Sports Festival. If you haven’t booked the upper limit of five events by then, you will automatically be assigned to the open slots.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For demonstration, let’s sign up for the 100 meter race.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Another important point is that you cannot participate in an event if it belongs to a club you are or have ever been a member of. Hirata cannot participate in events related to soccer and Sudou cannot participate in events related to basketball.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It is true that they are very alike. If you press the button for a time slot, you will be able to see in real time who will be participating in that event at that time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. But, sooner or later those people will run into the three time limit of the cancel feature.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And, if multiple students individually get the same points, the private point reward will be split between them and they will not be able to get the Class Change Ticket.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The corpus prints the attendance line with “–” (en dash) between “Wan” and “three students” — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He asks the first question about special rules; the individual rewards are made for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The club restriction names him and Sudō in one clause.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her class has 40 starting points more than the absentee-short class (400 vs 380).<span class=\"pg\">p.31–33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p59-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Named in other-POV pages<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p59-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  named in other pov pages toc   credit page   but  as chabashira told us during homeroom    ak narrates chabashira s homeroom intervention   the kind words chabashira sensei had said to me earlier    horikita s closing resolve  ch 3 corridor   chabashira sensei did say that kushida san s secret still wasn t widely known    horikita pov reflection  wang s pov  the door is closed so nobody would notice  chabashira sensei nodded once and is covering for the class  anchored references   quoted corpus verbatim where shown  see rows for pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Named in other-POV pages<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.59–173<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Anchored references — quoted corpus verbatim where shown; see rows for pages.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> TOC — credit page.<span class=\"pg\">p.5<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “But, as Chabashira told us during homeroom,” — AK narrates Chabashira&#x27;s homeroom intervention.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “the kind words Chabashira-sensei had said to me earlier.” — Horikita&#x27;s closing resolve (Ch.3 corridor).<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Chabashira-sensei did say that Kushida-san’s secret still wasn’t widely known.” — Horikita POV reflection.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Wang&#x27;s POV: the door is closed so nobody would notice; Chabashira-sensei nodded once and is covering for the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Attendance; the Sports Festival rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.1: The corridor — Sakura&#x27;s five thousand points<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p60-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  the corridor   sakura s five thousand points she summons him by tablet    come out of the class after me    he finds her in the corridor  the school found evidence sakura spent about five thousand private points after the exam but before formal processing completed  items purchased in school are the student s property  but this is a gray area  she will let him pay the sum if he wishes  he agrees  she asks if this concerns him   he denies it  she tells him to watch over each and every one of his students as they grow   yes  there is something i must tell you  it s about sakura   when she was expelled  the school naturally went through all the procedures  arranging her luggage  reclaiming her private points  well  that kind of thing  like  post processing   items already purchased in the school are fundamentally the student s personal property  and how they are dealt with is up to the student  whether you take them along or not  it s fine either way  the formalities for expulsion are processed in the staffroom but  well  an unexpected thing happened before that   yeah  after the unanimous consent special test was finished  we found evidence that sakura spent about five thousand of her private points  and well  you can say we re not sure how to handle that   yeah  but  as i said earlier  that only happens after the formal processing  however  the school considers this a gray area  say you transferred all your points to someone else  the school wouldn t accept that  right   are you saying you will pay that sum   no  it ll just be you spending your private points as you are entitled to  so the school should have no objections to it   i wanted to ask does this  have something to do with you   at any rate  it s a small matter  but i m still glad to have taken care of this  the state of the class being what it is  there are very few things to be happy about after all   what do you mean  she summons him to settle sakura s five thousand point gray area  he pays it himself  she asks if it concerns him  her five thousand private points spent post exam pre processing   a gray area the school could not classify  ak absorbs the cost","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: The corridor — Sakura&#x27;s five thousand points<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.60–63<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She summons him by tablet — “Come out of the class after me.” — he finds her in the corridor; the school found evidence Sakura spent about five thousand private points after the exam but before formal processing completed; items purchased in-school are the student&#x27;s property, but this is a gray area; she will let him pay the sum if he wishes; he agrees; she asks if this concerns him — he denies it; she tells him to watch over each and every one of his students as they grow.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. There is something I must tell you. It’s about Sakura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“When she was expelled, the school naturally went through all the procedures. Arranging her luggage, reclaiming her private points. Well, that kind of thing, like, post-processing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Items already purchased in the school are fundamentally the student’s personal property, and how they are dealt with is up to the student. Whether you take them along or not, it’s fine either way. The formalities for expulsion…”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Items already purchased in the school are fundamentally the student’s personal property, and how they are dealt with is up to the student. Whether you take them along or not, it’s fine either way. The formalities for expulsion are processed in the staffroom but… well, an unexpected thing happened before that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. After the Unanimous Consent Special Test was finished, we found evidence that Sakura spent about five thousand of her private points, and well, you can say we’re not sure how to handle that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. But, as I said earlier, that only happens after the formal processing. However, the school considers this a gray area. Say you transferred all your points to someone else, the school wouldn’t accept that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you saying you will pay that sum?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. It’ll just be you spending your private points as you are entitled to, so the school should have no objections to it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to ask—does this… have something to do with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At any rate, it’s a small matter, but I’m still glad to have taken care of this. The state of the class being what it is, there are very few things to be happy about after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She summons him to settle Sakura&#x27;s five-thousand-point gray area; he pays it himself; she asks if it concerns him.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her five thousand private points spent post-exam pre-processing — a gray area the school could not classify; AK absorbs the cost.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p59-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Named in other-POV pages<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p101-1\">→ After: Ch.3: The corridor talks; the long stare (Horikita&#x27;s POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p101-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka hasebe-haruka wang-mei-yu chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  the corridor talks  the long stare  horikita s pov  five days of three absences    that concludes homeroom    chabashira sensei lets horikita walk with her  she grants the three a reprieve on their prior behavior  warns the 100 class points will disappear if the absences continue  accepts horikita s  wavering  her counsel   don t be afraid of failure  she places her hand on horikita s shoulder   you ve changed  haven t you  chabashira sensei    she explains she has  started behaving like a teacher   think nothing of it  as a teacher  doing at least this much should be the natural thing to do   that concludes homeroom   it s the fifth day that kushida san  wang san  and hasebe san have been absent from school   ah  about that  two of them are ostensibly still sick  they ve continued to call in as such  however  they still haven t been examined at the clinic as they should have  as for hasebe  she s consistently said that she would be absent  but she hasn t told me any details   don t worry about that  especially for diligent students like wang and kushida  there are rules in place that allow for somewhat prolonged absences  even with hasebe  she s not a problem student  so right now it s not such a big deal  if they didn t have good grades or had a track record of bad behavior  it would be a different story   exactly  in addition  there might be healthy students who nonchalantly ditch school  but there also are students who will be down in the dumps for a week due to heartbreak  distinguishing between the two is difficult  so  we have to make the decision by looking at their grades and how they have behaved in school   also  the school isn t fiendish  they aren t plotting to force students to come to school and traumatize them mentally  you know  anyhow  the three of those haven t even been late to school before  and they had been taking their classes seriously  they ve easily earned a reprieve   that said  the time limit is close  if they continue being absent next week  the 100 class points you guys obtained after such desperation will  without mercy  disappear   wait a minute  horikita  you look like you still have something you want to say   are you regretting your choice   i want to give you an answer  but there s nothing i can say   it s not that  it s just that  at this stage  you can t prove whether or not you were right  sure  there were students who thought your decision was a bit despotic and self serving  those opinions are weighing on you  and you are beginning to feel that you may have been mistaken   however  is it really that important  nobody is perfect from the beginning  no matter who they may be  we make mistakes on simple arithmetic  learn from it  and move on  i myself have lived a life full of mistakes   even when i took the same special exam  that was the case  i couldn t even figure out whether i was right or wrong before time ran out  you  on the other hand  managed to produce a single answer  that s something you did well  nobody can score a 100 without gaining experience first  during that   special exam  you were recognized as a leader and given due authority  in addition  you were prepared to sacrifice someone to protect kushida  from here on out is where you make everyone recognize that you made the right choice   it s fine for you to not aim for a 100 now  after all  your only two choices were to either logically cut off the lowest ranked person on the oaa  or to prioritize your promise and receive a handicap   there will be times when you lose sight of your surroundings  there will also be times when you will doubt if your decision was correct once you cool down   until now  you ve only had to make decisions that  in a positive sense  could be considered appropriate  but  in a negative sense  could also be considered just simple  right  of course  that s normal  after all  the uniqueness of this school is what made you seek out a new choice   you fought within the rules the school set  didn t you   were you set on protecting kushida from the start  and the promise was just a lie in order to get assent   if that s the case  then there s no problem  sure  keeping your promise is important  however  sometimes  even adults have to go back on their word  i understand that your thinking changed  and you took that action because you realized it would be better if kushida remained in the class  people are free to make fun of you  disrespect you  or ignore you now  just as there are people who will follow you  there are also those who will not  uniting a class of nearly 40 people is no easy task  even for ryuuen  sakayanagi  or ichinose  even while some students might ostensibly act as yes men  there s no telling what they are really thinking on the inside   don t be afraid of failure  i m not the kind of adult who won t accept and won t forgive a child s mistakes    i suppose so  but that means that you need to protect that choice you made until the very end   is it weird that  after being cold for too long  i ve now started behaving like a teacher   hm  i m not so sure  during the incident with kushida  he took drastic action  if he didn t trust you  he probably would have just left you alone   you seem to trust and value him quite a bit more now   if it was hirata  then  no  i m not sure when it comes to kushida  if you took an upfront  good natured  virtuous person to her  i can t imagine her simply opening the door for him   unfortunately  i can t think of the right person for the job  but it might not be a bad idea to try looking for someone outside of your classmates   it s definitely necessary to balance the pros and cons  still  it doesn t mean you absolutely can t tell anyone about it  for instance  some of us teachers already know about kushida s past  and  out of those who don t  there are probably teachers who would stay quiet if you consulted them  i don t think it s that much of a secret   it s about time i get going  it may be a bother  but let me say one last thing  what s most important is what you want to do with kushida  think hard about that   think nothing of it  as a teacher  doing at least this much should be the natural thing to do  a teacher reborn   strict  heartfelt  threatens the loss of the 100 class points  gently advises  protects the corridor   i don t think it s that much of a secret  her new old student   the counsel that rebuilds her resolve  the one she won t convince herself  the idea of teachers as outside the class persuaders  she thinks he s observing horikita and values her quite a bit  she d never said that before  hasebe s absence   never told any details  a special reprieve due to her good grades  wang s absence    diligent students like wang and kushida    a reprieve","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p101-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: The corridor talks; the long stare (Horikita&#x27;s POV)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.101–111<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Five days of three absences — “That concludes homeroom.” — Chabashira-sensei lets Horikita walk with her; she grants the three a reprieve on their prior behavior; warns the 100 class points will disappear if the absences continue; accepts Horikita&#x27;s “wavering”; her counsel: “Don’t be afraid of failure.”; she places her hand on Horikita&#x27;s shoulder; “You’ve changed, haven’t you, Chabashira-sensei?” — she explains she has “started behaving like a teacher”; “Think nothing of it. As a teacher, doing at least this much should be the natural thing to do.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"wang-mei-yu.html\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“That concludes homeroom.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s the fifth day that Kushida-san, Wang-san, and Hasebe-san have been absent from school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ah, about that. Two of them are ostensibly still sick; they’ve continued to call in as such. However, they still haven’t been examined at the clinic as they should have. As for Hasebe, she’s consistently said that she would be…”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, about that. Two of them are ostensibly still sick; they’ve continued to call in as such. However, they still haven’t been examined at the clinic as they should have. As for Hasebe, she’s consistently said that she would be absent, but she hasn’t told me any details.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry about that. Especially for diligent students like Wang and Kushida, there are rules in place that allow for somewhat prolonged absences. Even with Hasebe, she’s not a problem student, so right now it’s not such a big deal. If they didn’t have good grades or had a track record of bad behavior, it would be a different story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. In addition, there might be healthy students who nonchalantly ditch school, but there also are students who will be down in the dumps for a week due to heartbreak. Distinguishing between the two is difficult. So, we have to make the decision by looking at their grades and how they have behaved in school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, the school isn’t fiendish. They aren’t plotting to force students to come to school and traumatize them mentally, you know. Anyhow, the three of those haven’t even been late to school before, and they had been taking their classes seriously. They’ve easily earned a reprieve.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That said, the time limit is close. If they continue being absent next week, the 100 class points you guys obtained after such desperation will, without mercy, disappear.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a minute, Horikita. You look like you still have something you want to say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you regretting your choice?”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want to give you an answer, but there’s nothing I can say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not that. It’s just that, at this stage, you can’t prove whether or not you were right. Sure, there were students who thought your decision was a bit despotic and self-serving. Those opinions are weighing on you, and you are beginning to feel that you may have been mistaken.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, is it really that important? Nobody is perfect from the beginning, no matter who they may be. We make mistakes on simple arithmetic, learn from it, and move on. I myself have lived a life full of mistakes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even when I took the same special exam, that was the case. I couldn’t even figure out whether I was right or wrong before time ran out. You, on the other hand, managed to produce a single answer. That’s something you did well! Nobody can score a 100 without gaining experience first. During that … special exam, you were recognized as a leader and given due authority. In addition, you were prepared to sacrifice someone to protect Kushida. From here on out is where you make everyone recognize that you made the right choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s fine for you to not aim for a 100 now. After all, your only two choices were to either logically cut off the lowest ranked person on the OAA, or to prioritize your promise and receive a handicap.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There will be times when you lose sight of your surroundings. There will also be times when you will doubt if your decision was correct once you cool down.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Until now, you’ve only had to make decisions that, in a positive sense, could be considered appropriate, but, in a negative sense, could also be considered just simple, right? Of course, that’s normal. After all, the uniqueness of this school is what made you seek out a new choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You fought within the rules the school set, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Were you set on protecting Kushida from the start, and the promise was just a lie in order to get assent?”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s the case, then there’s no problem. Sure, keeping your promise is important. However, sometimes, even adults have to go back on their word. I understand that your thinking changed, and you took that action because you realized it would be better if Kushida remained in the class. People are free to make fun of you, disrespect you, or ignore you now. Just as there are people who will follow you, there are also those who will not. Uniting a class of nearly 40 people is no easy task, even for Ryuuen, Sakayanagi, or Ichinose. Even while some students might ostensibly act as yes-men, there’s no telling what they are really thinking on the inside.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be afraid of failure. I’m not the kind of adult who won’t accept and won’t forgive a child’s mistakes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… I suppose so. But that means that you need to protect that choice you made until the very end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it weird that, after being cold for too long, I’ve now started behaving like a teacher?”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hm, I’m not so sure. During the incident with Kushida, he took drastic action. If he didn’t trust you, he probably would have just left you alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to trust and value him quite a bit more now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it was Hirata, then… no, I’m not sure when it comes to Kushida. If you took an upfront, good-natured, virtuous person to her, I can’t imagine her simply opening the door for him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, I can’t think of the right person for the job, but it might not be a bad idea to try looking for someone outside of your classmates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s definitely necessary to balance the pros and cons. Still, it doesn’t mean you absolutely can’t tell anyone about it. For instance, some of us teachers already know about Kushida’s past, and, out of those who don’t, there are probably teachers who would stay quiet if you consulted them. I don’t think it’s that much of a secret.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s about time I get going. It may be a bother, but let me say one last thing. What’s most important is what you want to do with Kushida. Think hard about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think nothing of it. As a teacher, doing at least this much should be the natural thing to do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> A teacher reborn — strict, heartfelt; threatens the loss of the 100 class points; gently advises; protects the corridor; “I don’t think it’s that much of a secret.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101–111, 172–175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her new-old student — the counsel that rebuilds her resolve.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The one she won&#x27;t convince herself; the idea of teachers as outside-the-class persuaders.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She thinks he&#x27;s observing Horikita and values her quite a bit; she&#x27;d never said that before.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Hasebe&#x27;s absence — never told any details; a special reprieve due to her good grades.<span class=\"pg\">p.102, 110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/b> Wang&#x27;s absence — &quot;diligent students like Wang and Kushida&quot; — a reprieve.<span class=\"pg\">p.102, 110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.1: The corridor — Sakura&#x27;s five thousand points<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.3: Monday homeroom — she keeps watch (AK POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p171-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  monday homeroom   she keeps watch  ak pov  monday   she enters with every seat except kushida s filled  the two absences get her half teasing warning instead of scolding  the homeroom confirms the return  then dismisses the class into the eruption  she nods once through the crack for ak s check   she is covering  every seat except kushida s was filled when she entered the classroom   looks like the two of you are feeling better  i suppose it was just a long summer cold  but take care of your health from now on   so kushida is absent today  i haven t heard from her either   the sports festival is just around the corner  i am expecting all of you to make great strides and participate well  she nods once through the crack at ak s poke check   watching the door is her task and the signal passes silently","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Monday homeroom — she keeps watch (AK POV)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.171–173<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Monday — she enters with every seat except Kushida&#x27;s filled; the two absences get her half-teasing warning instead of scolding; the homeroom confirms the return, then dismisses the class into the eruption; she nods once through the crack for AK&#x27;s check — she is covering.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Looks like the two of you are feeling better. I suppose it was just a long summer cold, but take care of your health from now on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So Kushida is absent today. I haven’t heard from her either─”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The Sports Festival is just around the corner. I am expecting all of you to make great strides and participate well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Every seat except Kushida&#x27;s was filled when she entered the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She nods once through the crack at AK&#x27;s poke-check — watching the door is her task and the signal passes silently.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p101-1\">← Before: Ch.3: The corridor talks; the long stare (Horikita&#x27;s POV)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p212-1\">→ After: Ch.4: Chabashira-sensei — to witness the alliance contract<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p212-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 4  chabashira sensei   to witness the alliance contract  i intend to have chabashira sensei and sakagami sensei get involved in this as well    horikita s line  the karaoke deal will be formalized with chabashira and sakagami as witnesses  stipulations for breach of contract will be included   naturally  there would be stipulations for breach of contract included in it  even ryuuen couldn t do anything if he were bound by unbreakable rules  the paperwork route is open   sakagami sensei is named in the same breath  nothing is signed on these pages  the alliance exists only as an agreement in the karaoke parlor  anchored references   quoted corpus verbatim where shown  see rows for pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p212-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: Chabashira-sensei — to witness the alliance contract<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.212–212<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Anchored references — quoted corpus verbatim where shown; see rows for pages.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “I intend to have Chabashira-sensei and Sakagami-sensei get involved in this as well.” — Horikita&#x27;s line; the karaoke deal will be formalized with Chabashira and Sakagami as witnesses; stipulations for breach of contract will be included; “Naturally, there would be stipulations for breach of contract included in it. Even Ryuuen couldn’t do anything if he were bound by unbreakable rules.”<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The paperwork route is open — Sakagami-sensei is named in the same breath; nothing is signed on these pages; the alliance exists only as an agreement in the karaoke parlor.<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Monday homeroom — she keeps watch (AK POV)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p336-1\">→ After: Short story: “Something That Can’t be Forgiven” (Chabashira POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p336-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hoshinomiya-chie kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae short story   something that can t be forgiven   chabashira pov  after homeroom with horikita   she is soon out of time    the most important thing is what you  horikita  wants to do with kushida  think carefully about this  she sends horikita off  walking back to the staff room  someone running behind her    don t run in the hallway  chie appears    sa e chan  yah ho    she warns her   chie heard the tail end    there was a huge risk of this leaking if chie heard about kushida   even the model student horikita has lots of worries     she s just a child  right  but that s not what i wanted to say     why have you gotten closer to your students now     there s nothing weird for a homeroom teacher  is it     that may be true     i won t acknowledge it  there is no way sae chan would ever act like a teacher      i know    her reply never reaches chie   we re soon out of time  just let me tell you one last thing  although it may look like i m meddling too much  the most important thing is what you  horikita  wants to do with kushida  think carefully about this   thank you  teacher  i ve decided what to do now   don t mind it  as your teacher  this is nothing  it s surely something to be expected after all   don t run in the hallway   sa e chan  yah ho   is that you  chie  how are you going to set an example if even you are running full ahead   bu ut  i saw you right ahead   stop with that bu ut  just call for me like normal   by the way  you were taking quite a long time talking with horikita san    so you even heard that   from when i heard her say thanks to you   looks like even the model student horikita has lots of worries   she s just a child  right  but that s not what i wanted to say   why have you gotten closer to your students now   there s nothing weird for a homeroom teacher  is it   it is  you are not that kind of a teacher  you have never been until now  have you   that may be true   i won t acknowledge it  there is no way sae chan would ever act like a teacher    i know  a teacher   she was not a teacher until now  she keeps her secrets  chie sees through her   may have been a lie    she does not refute it  chie   the teacher who tracks her   she does not acknowledge the change  her protege    even the model student horikita has lots of worries  the one horikita must bring back    what you  horikita  wants to do with kushida  short story  alternate retelling of the corridor scene from ch 3  built around chie s observation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p336-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Short story: “Something That Can’t be Forgiven” (Chabashira POV)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.336–338<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After homeroom with Horikita — she is soon out of time — “The most important thing is what you, Horikita, wants to do with Kushida. Think carefully about this.”; she sends Horikita off; walking back to the staff room; someone running behind her — “Don’t run in the hallway…”; Chie appears — “Sa~~~~e-chan. Yah-ho!” — she warns her — Chie heard the tail end — “There was a huge risk of this leaking If Chie heard about Kushida.”; “even the model student Horikita has lots of worries.” — “She’s just a child, right? But that’s not what I wanted to say.” — “Why have you gotten closer to your students now?” — “There’s nothing weird for a homeroom teacher, is it?” — “That may be true.” — “I won’t acknowledge it. There is no way Sae-chan would ever act like a teacher.” — “… I know.” — her reply never reaches Chie.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“We’re soon out of time. Just let me tell you one last thing, although it may look like I’m meddling too much. The most important thing is what you, Horikita, wants to do with Kushida. Think carefully about this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Thank you, teacher. I’ve decided what to do now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t mind it. As your teacher, this is nothing— it’s surely something to be expected after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t run in the hallway…”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sa~~~~e-chan. Yah-ho!”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that you, Chie? How are you going to set an example if even you are running full ahead?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Bu~ut, I saw you right ahead!”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop with that Bu~ut! Just call for me like normal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, you were taking quite a long time talking with Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… so you even heard that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From when I heard her say thanks to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like even the model student Horikita has lots of worries.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s just a child, right? But that’s not what I wanted to say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why have you gotten closer to your students now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing weird for a homeroom teacher, is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It is. You are not that kind of a teacher. You have never been until now, have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That may be true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.338<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t acknowledge it. There is no way Sae-chan would ever act like a teacher.”<span class=\"pg\">p.338<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “… I know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.338<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> A teacher — she was not a teacher until now; she keeps her secrets; Chie sees through her; “may have been a lie” — she does not refute it.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–338<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Chie — the teacher who tracks her — she does not acknowledge the change.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–338<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her protégé — “even the model student Horikita has lots of worries.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The one Horikita must bring back — “what you, Horikita, wants to do with Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Short story; alternate retelling of the corridor scene from Ch.3; built around Chie&#x27;s observation.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–338<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v6-p212-1\">← Before: Ch.4: Chabashira-sensei — to witness the alliance contract<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p7-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the festival briefing  the additional funds announcement monday  november 1st  chabashira opens homeroom with the festival review and the additional funds details  the students sit in serious  disciplined silence   i believe preparations are steadily progressing for the cultural festival  but i have some additional explanatory notes  first of all  i will once again display an overview of the festival as a review  so those who need to should check it    the explanation of the rules reappeared on the monitor   i would like to announce that the details of the  additional funds  mentioned in this overview explanation have been decided   first of all  the total amount of additional funds to be given to this class  and the breakdown of the funds    she operated her tablet and displayed the list  horikita 10 000  student council member bonus  sudo 10 000  club activity  onodera 10 000  club activity    the maximum  nine other students received hundreds to thousands  yosuke got 3 000  akito 100   i can t give you the breakdown  but sakayanagi s class a has 18 800 points  17 000 points for ryuen s class c  and ichinose s class d has 26 600 points in additional funds  in other words  this class has the most additional funds among the second year students   guests of honor will be people who are involved in the operation of this school and their families  but of course there will be a wide range of ages  from the elderly to toddlers and elementary school students  she said   it has also been decided that those who work at keyaki mall and convenience stores will also be invited as guests    a graph of guest ages by decade followed   the adults are guests of honor and they receive 10 000 points  minors receive 5 000 points  there are 283 adults and 202 minors  the total number of participants will be 485 in all  for a total sum of 3 840 000 points   i should also mention that the number of participants includes us teachers  homeroom teachers are restricted to use points in the grade for which they are responsible  but they are treated no differently than other guests   no  the guests can t spend more than the given points  the maximum amount is immovable    answering ike  without paying much attention  though she seemed to be enjoying such an unchanging ike   the primary method of payment is through a special cell phone app which the school will use to monitor sales in real time  keep in mind that the app will be disabled the moment the festival ends at 4 pm  you are free to set your own timing for the checkout  but we recommend that you receive payment before the products are served   if the sales are equal  they are treated as the same rank  if all 12 classes make equal sales  as horikita says  then all classes get 100 class points as first place   however  the total amount of sales can only be confirmed after the exam  and any manipulation of sales by third parties is not allowed  it is impossible for the classes to discuss and make a plan to combine sales before the festival  or to    make an arrangement to divide the sales equally after the festival is over  you know what this means  right   as maezono san said  if it is a normal fight  there is no need to be concerned about it  but it s not a bad thing to know if it s accepted as a rule or not    she answered horikita s tie question   that s all i have to say about the festival  next  i would like to announce the results of the second semester mid term exam that we recently conducted  this time  there are students who achieved results that surprised even me   however  given that chabashira sensei s expression wasn t dark or stiff  that seemed unlikely    the results pleased her  keisei first  perfect score  horikita second  3 points behind  sudo 11th  367 points  the surprise     students who achieved results that surprised even me  the additional funds and oaa motivations hang on her choices  chabashira watches her hand raise the tie question with genuine interest  the pocket money question   she answered without looking","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The festival briefing; the additional-funds announcement<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.7–13<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Monday, November 1st; Chabashira opens homeroom with the festival review and the additional-funds details; the students sit in serious, disciplined silence.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I believe preparations are steadily progressing for the cultural festival, but I have some additional explanatory notes. First of all, I will once again display an overview of the festival as a review, so those who need to…”<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I would like to announce that the details of the &#x27;additional funds&#x27; mentioned in this overview explanation have been decided.”<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“First of all, the total amount of additional funds to be given to this class, and the breakdown of the funds…” — she operated her tablet and displayed the list: Horikita 10,000 (student council member bonus), Sudō 10,000 (club…”<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe preparations are steadily progressing for the cultural festival, but I have some additional explanatory notes. First of all, I will once again display an overview of the festival as a review, so those who need to should check it.” — the explanation of the rules reappeared on the monitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First of all, the total amount of additional funds to be given to this class, and the breakdown of the funds…” — she operated her tablet and displayed the list: Horikita 10,000 (student council member bonus), Sudō 10,000 (club activity), Onodera 10,000 (club activity) — the maximum; nine other students received hundreds to thousands; Yōsuke got 3,000, Akito 100.<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can&#x27;t give you the breakdown, but Sakayanagi&#x27;s Class A has 18,800 points. 17,000 points for Ryūen&#x27;s Class C, and Ichinose&#x27;s Class D has 26,600 points in additional funds. In other words, this class has the most additional funds among the second-year students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Guests of honor will be people who are involved in the operation of this school and their families, but of course there will be a wide range of ages, from the elderly to toddlers and elementary school students,” she said. “It has also been decided that those who work at Keyaki Mall and convenience stores will also be invited as guests.” — a graph of guest ages by decade followed.<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The adults are guests of honor and they receive 10,000 points. Minors receive 5,000 points. There are 283 adults and 202 minors. The total number of participants will be 485 in all, for a total sum of 3,840,000 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should also mention that the number of participants includes us teachers. Homeroom teachers are restricted to use points in the grade for which they are responsible, but they are treated no differently than other guests.”<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. The guests can&#x27;t spend more than the given points. The maximum amount is immovable.” — answering Ike; without paying much attention, though she seemed to be enjoying such an unchanging Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The primary method of payment is through a special cell phone app which the school will use to monitor sales in real time. Keep in mind that the app will be disabled the moment the festival ends at 4 pm. You are free to set your own timing for the checkout, but we recommend that you receive payment before the products are served.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If the sales are equal, they are treated as the same rank. If all 12 classes make equal sales, as Horikita says, then all classes get 100 class points as first place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, the total amount of sales can only be confirmed after the exam, and any manipulation of sales by third parties is not allowed. It is impossible for the classes to discuss and make a plan to combine sales before the festival, or to …  make an arrangement to divide the sales equally after the festival is over. You know what this means, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.10–11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As Maezono-san said, if it is a normal fight, there is no need to be concerned about it. But it&#x27;s not a bad thing to know if it&#x27;s accepted as a rule or not.” — she answered Horikita&#x27;s tie question.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s all I have to say about the festival. Next, I would like to announce the results of the second semester mid-term exam that we recently conducted. This time, there are students who achieved results that surprised even me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “However, given that Chabashira-sensei&#x27;s expression wasn&#x27;t dark or stiff, that seemed unlikely.” — the results pleased her.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Keisei first (perfect score), Horikita second (3 points behind), Sudō 11th (367 points, the surprise) — “students who achieved results that surprised even me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The additional-funds and OAA motivations hang on her choices; Chabashira watches her hand raise the tie question with genuine interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.7–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The pocket-money question — she answered without looking.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p54-1\">→ After: Named in the staff-shift corridor gossip<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p54-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae named in the staff shift corridor gossip  after school  when chabashira sensei left the classroom  i took out my    ayanokoji s narration  she left the classroom   ayanokoji  you heard a little of what chabashira sensei said  what    mashima sensei s question   you haven t heard  not from chabashira sensei    ayanokoji s reply   what happened at the unanimous special exam    mashima sensei  the exam s effect on chabashira sensei is what the teachers were gossiping about  the narration shows the staff corridor knew   as i recall  mashima sensei and chabashira sensei were originally from the    they went to high school together  she was schoolmate to mashima sensei","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Named in the staff-shift corridor gossip<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.54, 57<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “After school, when Chabashira-sensei left the classroom, I took out my” — Ayanokōji&#x27;s narration; she left the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “Ayanokōji, you heard a little of what Chabashira-sensei said… What” — Mashima-sensei&#x27;s question.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “You haven&#x27;t heard? Not from Chabashira-sensei?” — Ayanokōji&#x27;s reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “What happened at the unanimous special exam?” — Mashima-sensei; the exam&#x27;s effect on Chabashira-sensei is what the teachers were gossiping about; the narration shows the staff corridor knew.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “As I recall, Mashima-sensei and Chabashira-sensei were originally from the” — they went to high school together; she was schoolmate to Mashima-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p7-1\">← Before: The festival briefing; the additional-funds announcement<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p153-1\">→ After: The 100,000-point hire; standing room only; 63 photos<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p153-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou wang-mei-yu sudou-ken chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the 100 000 point hire  standing room only  63 photos  3   it was getting close to 3 00 pm  he left the maid cafe to prepare for his final move  he called chabashira sensei  who would have been using her points for a non second year class on campus   sorry for calling you all the way here  chabashira sensei    ayanokoji   have you finished using your private points    ayanokoji   hmm  ah  there are 80 points left  i d say i ve used them up  what about it    chabashira sensei   in other words  you re free for the rest of the day    ayanokoji   yes  that s right  now all we have to do is wait for the end of the cultural festival  what the hell is this    chabashira sensei  she showed her confusion  not understanding why she was summoned here  the kimono cafe was just a backdrop  he left it up to chabashira sensei to see the momentum and interpret it as she saw fit   actually  i d like to ask chabashira sensei for her cooperation for the next hour or so    ayanokoji   no no no  wait  ayanokoji  cooperation  i don t understand what you re talking about    chabashira sensei  teachers were to contribute to the festival by spending points in the school  that was the only role they had been given today   we want chabashira sensei to be our maid in order to make sales at the maid cafe    ayanokoji   what    chabashira sensei  this may have been the dumbest strategy he had ever come up with in his life   did i not just tell you  i m just going to do what i can to win    ayanokoji   why should i be the maid  i m the homeroom teacher  i can t be obligated to one particular class    chabashira sensei   that s not true  the rule this time is that school teachers are to be treated as if they were guests of honor  homeroom teachers are not allowed to use points in their grade level  those are the only two rules that have been imposed  there is also no rule that only students may participate in the presentation  in extreme cases  they should be free to have guests of honor serve them  it would be unusual  but that problem could be resolved if the guest consents    ayanokoji  this was not a prohibited activity under the rules  it would be a clear violation if the person were to purchase goods from a convenience store  keyaki mall  or any other place other than the points of sale available at the festival  using personal expenses  however  in terms of  human resources  there was no need to apply for such a permit  and it was free   shall i explain it more clearly  assuming there was a student carrying a heavy load  they are dizzy  a guest passing by offered to help and carried the luggage on his shoulders to the desired location  is this a violation    ayanokoji   it s not a violation    chabashira sensei   exactly  other people can be substituted for the students  2nd year class a asks 2nd year class d for help  and class d readily agrees  would there be a problem if we loaned the students out    ayanokoji  the reasons for loaning them out were varied  whatever the reason  as long as it was within the rules  the school won t blame anyone for it  he saw a few students supporting other classes   i don t see the problem     it s the same thing  a teacher s willingness to cooperate isn t  in itself  a violation of the rules     no  it doesn t  it s still considered lending a hand for the class you re in     that s right  even if it is broadly allowed  you can t be sure that such an opinion won t be expressed   that s why clear rules need to be utilized and legitimate    ayanokoji   we will pay for any private points that would be incurred when renting teachers  i m sure the school is looking at that possibility in anticipation of this festival    ayanokoji   no way  no  but  i don t know if i m  enough to be considered    chabashira sensei  he d hit the bull s eye  she showed such an expression  chabashira sensei was also a teacher at this school  and in the past had been in charge of other classes  it was only natural that the school made various assumptions for a cultural festival that had never been held in the past  in principle  private points at this school were a powerful weapon  no wonder it could be used not only for routine shopping  but also to secure personnel if necessary   there is nothing in this school that cannot be bought with private points  is there a difference    ayanokoji  to deny this was to deny the school  and it was like admitting to being a disqualified teacher  in a panic  chabashira sensei began reading the rules about the festival on her cell phone   pay 100 000 private points for every hour students ask for a teacher s help    the backroom rule  the same thing that happened when private points were used to buy test scores   it seems that you are well prepared for the behind the scenes rules that only this schools has  that s the option    chabashira sensei   that s 100 000 points per hour  it s not a cheap deal  are you sure you want to do this    chabashira sensei   of course i m sure    ayanokoji  asking teachers to cooperate inherently doesn t help much  whether the teachers are made to cook or serve  if they hadn t practiced beforehand  it would be a waste of private points to have them on one s side for an hour or so  it was difficult for them to perform the job on the spot if they had to go out to the restaurant to serve the customers  but if they were used in a different way than usual  the school could get the effect it paid for   are you really  really sure    chabashira sensei   i m sorry  chabashira sensei  but now i m going to ask you to cooperate even if you don t want to  i don t have a lot of time to spare right now    ayanokoji  after 3 00 p m  they wouldn t be able to get a full hour s help  which would make them less efficient   well  wait  yes  why don t you ask chie  she does this kind of thing better  she d be ready to do it even for a rival class    chabashira sensei   i m sure she would  but what i m looking for now is not someone who can do this dexterously  but rather someone who is clumsy  because i believe that the more clumsy you are  or the more effective you are at the margins  the more    effective you will be    ayanokoji   i have no idea what your logic is    chabashira sensei  it must have been true that deep down she didn t like it and that she didn t understand  it was because she didn t understand that chabashira sensei functioned a certain  way  that could be appealable to a certain audience   there s no more time  please take care of it    ayanokoji  he forced her to accept his private points as he took his phone and paid chabashira sensei   we have a deal     that s not fair  ayanokoji  using the school rules     that s not cowardly  it s a really straightforward way to fight    the exchange   i have no idea how to act in a maid cafe  i don t know what s going to happen to me    chabashira sensei   that s fine  i don t expect anything from the teacher    ayanokoji  chabashira sensei staying inside the classroom in a maid outfit  that fact alone was enough to win   4   after pushing the reluctant chabashira sensei into the locker room  he pasted the text he had prepared on his cell phone and sent it to all his classmates at once as a bulk message  the purpose was to inform the students that chabashira sensei will be working as a maid for the last hour only  and to inform the students who were available that they were to go around the school advertising the event  as intended  the buzz spreaded swiftly through word of mouth  using teachers  this was a limited  oversized event that students would never be able to pull off  the air in the hallway was buzzing so much that it instantly turned into an uproar  chabashira sensei  dressed as a maid  rushed into the hallway with a red face   okay  here i am ayanokoji  hurry up and let me inside the classroom    chabashira sensei   we ve been waiting for you    ayanokoji  he can t keep showing her off for free  so he led her inside the classroom   so  what am i supposed to do here    chabashira sensei   you don t have to do anything  just stand still    ayanokoji   what    chabashira sensei   i told you  i don t want you to be dexterous  i m looking forward to working    with you    ayanokoji  she didn t talk to anyone  but simply stood shyly in the corner of the classroom  being clumsy  she wasn t able to do anything in particular and needed to stand without talking to anyone  this was the ultimate eroticism  they were going to have to make a major shift in their maid cafe policy from here on out  the biggest concern was the large number of visitors who couldn t fit in the classrooms  in order to forcefully solve this physical problem  they had to make the customers pay a reasonable price  the idea was to have a  standing room only  fee to accommodate over capacity customers  they added a rule that allowed immediate entry upon payment of 1 000 points to enter the classroom  the first guests waiting in line would be offered entry  and only those who responded that they would be willing to stand in line would be allowed to enter the room first  some of the visitors waiting in line at this point may complain  but they were willing to take that risk   standing room only     i ve never heard of that idea in a maid cafe    chabashira sensei  a standing room should be set up on the side of the room where desks couldn t be set up and in the space at the rear of the classroom  this would allow people to enter the room without desks and chairs  and 2 000 points for a photo shoot with chabashira sensei  this will be sold for more than double the price of a photo of one student  they hurriedly filled in the guests with the board at the entrance   amazing  would a customer pay that price     look behind you    kushida looked back and saw the customers who had paid their bill and accepted the standing room disappear one by one into the classroom  the current faculty and staff were intrigued by the sight  which they would not see again  although homeroom teachers of the same grade were restricted from spending their private points  the number of teachers who were still at the school and in charge of classes other than the second year was  of course  overwhelmingly large  the adults who worked at keyaki mall had a strong image of chabashira sensei as a hard nosed teacher  as they witnessed repeatedly in their daily lives  adults came in like a wave  the maid cafe queue was overflowing with more than 10 or 20 people in line  the long line was not decreasing  but rather gaining momentum   wow  that s a lot of people  ayanokoji kun    a stunned kushida pulled back at the hordes of adults pouring in   yeah  i guess so  to be honest  i didn t think it would be this big either    ayanokoji   how long have you been thinking about this crazy thing    kushida   about two weeks ago  i had it in mind as a hidden gem for the festival    ayanokoji   what would have happened if we had started earlier    kushida   certainly the lasting effect could have been two or three hours  but another problem arises  because if you have more time to spare  other classes can do similar imitations    ayanokoji   oh  i see  they have less than an hour left  so even if they wanted to imitate us  they couldn t    kushida   if we re going to put on a show  we only have this last hour where we can also put on a premiere    ayanokoji  the fact that kushida and the others had spread the word about the maid cafe in a positive light also helped   i see  no wonder i couldn t win    kushida   hmm    ayanokoji   i realized once again how great ayanokoji kun is  he s a nuisance to have as an enemy    kushida   your eyes aren t smiling  kushida    ayanokoji   i guess it s because i was half glad we were classmates and half pissed off    kushida  she said half and half  but he thought the latter was a higher percentage   don t push me  get in line here  please don t push    sudo and his team rushed to create a wall of people and tried to get them to form a line  but it was becoming a crowd as some adults sought to somehow look into the classroom  but this was business too  the inside was thoroughly concealed and the windows were locked  so the only way to forcefully see inside was to break a windowpane  of course  no adult would do such a thing  so they forced them to form a line  while this was going on  there was no end to the number of people who wanted to take pictures of chabashira sensei  both the  standing room only  customers  who had entered the store  and those who had already been in the store raised their hands one after the other and asked to be photographed   she might be the top individual sales person in the final hour  she hasn t even done anything    printed untagged  not assigned   i can t let any more people in  the second slot is filled up    mii chan s voice echoed like a scream  and we were informed that the spaces had been filled   that s it  huh  it s a shame that the number of customers hasn t decreased at all yet  and there s no sign of them leaving    kushida   not yet  the customers who are left now are in line because they have money  i m not going to let them leave    ayanokoji   maybe we need to carry the tables out or something  but i can t bring the tables with all the dishes and stuff  it would take a lot of work to carry them out    kushida  it was obvious that there was no longer any space in the classroom for guests   we can use this location to make the most out of the third slot    ayanokoji   a third space    kushida  he turned to all the customers in line and said   i m sorry  but the restaurant is full and no more rooms are available    ayanokoji  after announcing this to them  he got a series of looks from disgruntled adults   however  those of you who have at least one point on hand at this time may view the room from this location by paying the full amount of your point balance    ayanokoji  this location was the hallway where the lines were formed for the maid cafe  by opening the door  the obstruction was removed  and by opening the window  the classroom was pseudo extended   woah  you re using the hallway    kushida   yes    ayanokoji   but the full amount could be small  sure  but it might still be hundreds of points  you mean whoever has money and will pay it    kushida   no problem  i don t know if it s worth paying a lot of money  but there isn t    much time left  even if there were nearly 1 000 points left over  there would be a big question as to where and how they could be used    ayanokoji   oh  i see  i thought you were going to return the remaining points after the festival is over    kushida   they ve been notified to use them up as much as possible  they d rather spend all their points than to lose them here  it s not an exaggeration to say that 1 point or 10 000 points are worth the same to the adults who are given them    ayanokoji   please wait there while we go to the checkout in order    ayanokoji gave the order and sent a few people to collect the sales  he then lined up the adults in the hallway and directed them to a position where they could all see into the classroom   now all we need to do is open the curtains that we have been using to hide the classroom    doing so completed the third space  the curtains opened all at once and chabashira sensei was surprised to see them  for chabashira sensei  it was a kind of public execution  but since they paid the school for it  there was no need to feel bad   oh  oh  i see    a teacher who had just previously gossiped about chabashira sensei s transformation sounded impressed  thus  the public presentation of chabashira sensei continued until 4 00 p m  using this corridor  in the end  chabashira sensei took first place  surpassing kushida  with 63 desired pictures  the 100 000 point hire  the standing room only conversion  the 63 photos  the victory  the stunned kushida   he s a nuisance to have as an enemy  sudo and his team make the wall for the adults pouring in  mii chan s scream about the second slot filling","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The 100,000-point hire; standing room only; 63 photos<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.153–164<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">§3 — it was getting close to 3:00 pm; he left the maid café to prepare for his final move; he called Chabashira-sensei, who would have been using her points for a non-second year class on campus. §4 — after pushing the reluctant Chabashira-sensei into the locker room, he pasted the text he had prepared on his cell phone and sent it to all his classmates at once as a bulk message; the purpose was to inform the students that Chabashira-sensei will be working as a maid for the last hour only, and to inform the students who were available that they were to go around the school advertising the event. Chabashira-sensei, dressed as a maid, rushed into the hallway with a red face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"wang-mei-yu.html\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sorry for calling you all the way here, Chabashira-sensei.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Have you finished using your private points?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm? Ah, there are 80 points left. I&#x27;d say I&#x27;ve used them up. What about it?” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>95 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, you&#x27;re free for the rest of the day?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, that&#x27;s right. Now all we have to do is wait for the end of the cultural festival... What the hell is this?” — Chabashira-sensei; she showed her confusion, not understanding why she was summoned here.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The kimono café was just a backdrop; he left it up to Chabashira-sensei to see the momentum and interpret it as she saw fit.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually, I&#x27;d like to ask Chabashira-sensei for her cooperation for the next hour or so.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No no no, wait, Ayanokōji, cooperation? I don&#x27;t understand what you&#x27;re talking about.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Teachers were to contribute to the festival by spending points in the school; that was the only role they had been given today.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We want Chabashira-sensei to be our maid in order to make sales at the maid cafe.” — Ayanokōji; “What...?” — Chabashira-sensei; this may have been the dumbest strategy he had ever come up with in his life.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did I not just tell you? I&#x27;m just going to do what I can to win.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why should I be the maid!? I&#x27;m the homeroom teacher. I can&#x27;t be obligated to one particular class.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s not true. The rule this time is that school teachers are to be treated as if they were guests of honor. Homeroom teachers are not allowed to use points in their grade level. Those are the only two rules that have been imposed. There is also no rule that only students may participate in the presentation. In extreme cases, they should be free to have guests of honor serve them. It would be unusual, but that problem could be resolved if the guest consents.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> This was not a prohibited activity under the rules; it would be a clear violation if the person were to purchase goods from a convenience store, Keyaki Mall, or any other place other than the points of sale available at the festival, using personal expenses; however, in terms of “human resources,” there was no need to apply for such a permit, and it was free.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shall I explain it more clearly? Assuming there was a student carrying a heavy load, they are dizzy. A guest passing by offered to help and carried the luggage on his shoulders to the desired location. Is this a violation?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It&#x27;s not a violation…” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. Other people can be substituted for the students: 2nd year class A asks 2nd year class D for help, and class D readily agrees. Would there be a problem if we loaned the students out?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reasons for loaning them out were varied; whatever the reason, as long as it was within the rules, the school won&#x27;t blame anyone for it; he saw a few students supporting other classes; “I don&#x27;t see the problem.” — “It&#x27;s the same thing. A teacher&#x27;s willingness to cooperate isn&#x27;t, in itself, a violation of the rules.” — “No, it doesn&#x27;t. It&#x27;s still considered lending a hand for the class you&#x27;re in.” — “That&#x27;s right. Even if it is broadly allowed, you can&#x27;t be sure that such an opinion won&#x27;t be expressed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “That&#x27;s why clear rules need to be utilized and legitimate.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We will pay for any private points that would be incurred when renting teachers. I&#x27;m sure the school is looking at that possibility in anticipation of this festival.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No way, no, but... I don&#x27;t know if I&#x27;m... enough to be considered...” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He&#x27;d hit the bull&#x27;s-eye; she showed such an expression; Chabashira-sensei was also a teacher at this school, and in the past had been in charge of other classes; it was only natural that the school made various assumptions for a cultural festival that had never been held in the past.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> In principle, private points at this school were a powerful weapon; no wonder it could be used not only for routine shopping, but also to secure personnel if necessary.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is nothing in this school that cannot be bought with private points. Is there a difference?” — Ayanokōji; to deny this was to deny the school; and it was like admitting to being a disqualified teacher.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> In a panic, Chabashira-sensei began reading the rules about the festival on her cell phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Pay 100,000 private points for every hour students ask for a teacher&#x27;s help.” — the backroom rule, the same thing that happened when private points were used to buy test scores.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems that you are well prepared for the behind-the-scenes rules that only this schools has. That&#x27;s the option.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s 100,000 points per hour. It&#x27;s not a cheap deal. Are you sure you want to do this?” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I&#x27;m sure.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asking teachers to cooperate inherently doesn&#x27;t help much; whether the teachers are made to cook or serve, if they hadn&#x27;t practiced beforehand, it would be a waste of private points to have them on one&#x27;s side for an hour or so; it was difficult for them to perform the job on the spot if they had to go out to the restaurant to serve the customers; but if they were used in a different way than usual, the school could get the effect it paid for.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you really, really sure?” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m sorry, Chabashira-sensei, but now I&#x27;m going to ask you to cooperate even if you don&#x27;t want to. I don&#x27;t have a lot of time to spare right now.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After 3:00 p.m., they wouldn&#x27;t be able to get a full hour&#x27;s help, which would make them less efficient.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, wait. Yes, why don&#x27;t you ask Chie? She does this kind of thing better. She&#x27;d be ready to do it even for a rival class.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m sure she would. But what I&#x27;m looking for now is not someone who can do this dexterously, but rather someone who is clumsy. Because I believe that the more clumsy you are, or the more effective you are at the margins, the more …  effective you will be.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have no idea what your logic is.” — Chabashira-sensei; it must have been true that deep down she didn&#x27;t like it and that she didn&#x27;t understand; it was because she didn&#x27;t understand that Chabashira-sensei functioned a certain “way” that could be appealable to a certain audience.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There&#x27;s no more time. Please take care of it.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He forced her to accept his private points as he took his phone and paid Chabashira-sensei; “We have a deal.” — “That&#x27;s not fair, Ayanokōji, using the school rules.” — “That&#x27;s not cowardly, it&#x27;s a really straightforward way to fight.” — the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have no idea how to act in a maid cafe. I don&#x27;t know what&#x27;s going to happen to me.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s fine. I don&#x27;t expect anything from the teacher.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira-sensei staying inside the classroom in a maid outfit; that fact alone was enough to win.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> As intended, the buzz spreaded swiftly through word of mouth; using teachers, this was a limited, oversized event that students would never be able to pull off; the air in the hallway was buzzing so much that it instantly turned into an uproar.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, here I am Ayanokōji, hurry up and let me inside the classroom!” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We&#x27;ve been waiting for you.” — Ayanokōji; he can&#x27;t keep showing her off for free, so he led her inside the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, what am I supposed to do here?” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don&#x27;t have to do anything. Just stand still.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I told you, I don&#x27;t want you to be dexterous. I&#x27;m looking forward to working …  with you.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She didn&#x27;t talk to anyone, but simply stood shyly in the corner of the classroom; being clumsy, she wasn&#x27;t able to do anything in particular and needed to stand without talking to anyone; this was the ultimate eroticism.<span class=\"pg\">p.158–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> They were going to have to make a major shift in their maid cafe policy from here on out; the biggest concern was the large number of visitors who couldn&#x27;t fit in the classrooms; in order to forcefully solve this physical problem, they had to make the customers pay a reasonable price; the idea was to have a “standing room only” fee to accommodate over-capacity customers; they added a rule that allowed immediate entry upon payment of 1,000 points to enter the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The first guests waiting in line would be offered entry, and only those who responded that they would be willing to stand in line would be allowed to enter the room first; some of the visitors waiting in line at this point may complain, but they were willing to take that risk.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Standing room only … , I&#x27;ve never heard of that idea in a maid cafe.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A standing room should be set up on the side of the room where desks couldn&#x27;t be set up and in the space at the rear of the classroom; this would allow people to enter the room without desks and chairs; and 2,000 points for a photo shoot with Chabashira-sensei; this will be sold for more than double the price of a photo of one student.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> They hurriedly filled in the guests with the board at the entrance; “Amazing. Would a customer pay that price?” — “Look behind you.” — Kushida looked back and saw the customers who had paid their bill and accepted the standing room disappear one by one into the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The current faculty and staff were intrigued by the sight, which they would not see again; although homeroom teachers of the same grade were restricted from spending their private points, the number of teachers who were still at the school and in charge of classes other than the second year was, of course, overwhelmingly large; the adults who worked at Keyaki Mall had a strong image of Chabashira-sensei as a hard-nosed teacher, as they witnessed repeatedly in their daily lives; adults came in like a wave.<span class=\"pg\">p.159–160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The maid café queue was overflowing with more than 10 or 20 people in line; the long line was not decreasing, but rather gaining momentum.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wow, that&#x27;s a lot of people, Ayanokōji-kun.” — a stunned Kushida pulled back at the hordes of adults pouring in.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, I guess so. To be honest, I didn&#x27;t think it would be this big either.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How long have you been thinking about this crazy thing?” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “About two weeks ago. I had it in mind as a hidden gem for the festival.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What would have happened if we had started earlier...?” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Certainly the lasting effect could have been two or three hours. But another problem arises. Because if you have more time to spare, other classes can do similar imitations.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, I see. They have less than an hour left, so even if they wanted to imitate us, they couldn&#x27;t.” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “If we&#x27;re going to put on a show, we only have this last hour where we can also put on a premiere.” — Ayanokōji; the fact that Kushida and the others had spread the word about the maid café in a positive light also helped.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. No wonder I couldn&#x27;t win.” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I realized once again how great Ayanokōji-kun is. He&#x27;s a nuisance to have as an enemy.” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your eyes aren&#x27;t smiling, Kushida.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess it&#x27;s because I was half glad we were classmates and half pissed off.” — Kushida; she said half and half, but he thought the latter was a higher percentage.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Don&#x27;t push me! Get in line here! Please don&#x27;t push!” — Sudō and his team rushed to create a wall of people and tried to get them to form a line, but it was becoming a crowd as some adults sought to somehow look into the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> But this was business too; the inside was thoroughly concealed and the windows were locked, so the only way to forcefully see inside was to break a windowpane; of course, no adult would do such a thing, so they forced them to form a line.<span class=\"pg\">p.160–161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> While this was going on, there was no end to the number of people who wanted to take pictures of Chabashira-sensei; both the ‘standing-room-only’ customers, who had entered the store, and those who had already been in the store raised their hands one after the other and asked to be photographed.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “She might be the top individual sales person in the final hour. She hasn&#x27;t even done anything.” — printed untagged; not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can&#x27;t let any more people in! The second slot is filled up!” — Mii-chan&#x27;s voice echoed like a scream, and we were informed that the spaces had been filled.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s it, huh? It&#x27;s a shame that the number of customers hasn&#x27;t decreased at all yet, and there&#x27;s no sign of them leaving.” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not yet. The customers who are left now are in line because they have money. I&#x27;m not going to let them leave.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe we need to carry the tables out or something? But I can&#x27;t bring the tables with all the dishes and stuff. It would take a lot of work to carry them out.” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> It was obvious that there was no longer any space in the classroom for guests.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can use this location to make the most out of the third slot.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A third space?” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He turned to all the customers in line and said.<span class=\"pg\">p.161–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m sorry, but the restaurant is full and no more rooms are available.” — Ayanokōji; after announcing this to them, he got a series of looks from disgruntled adults.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, those of you who have at least one point on hand at this time may view the room from this location by paying the full amount of your point balance.” — Ayanokōji; this location was the hallway where the lines were formed for the maid café.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> By opening the door, the obstruction was removed, and by opening the window, the classroom was pseudo-extended.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Woah, you&#x27;re using the hallway?!” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But the full amount could be small, sure, but it might still be hundreds of points... you mean whoever has money and will pay it?” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No problem. I don&#x27;t know if it&#x27;s worth paying a lot of money, but there isn&#x27;t …  much time left. Even if there were nearly 1,000 points left over, there would be a big question as to where and how they could be used.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.162–163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, I see... I thought you were going to return the remaining points after the festival is over.” — Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “They&#x27;ve been notified to use them up as much as possible. They&#x27;d rather spend all their points than to lose them here. It&#x27;s not an exaggeration to say that 1 point or 10,000 points are worth the same to the adults who are given them.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Please wait there while we go to the checkout in order.” — Ayanokōji gave the order and sent a few people to collect the sales; he then lined up the adults in the hallway and directed them to a position where they could all see into the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Now all we need to do is open the curtains that we have been using to hide the classroom.” — doing so completed the third space; the curtains opened all at once and Chabashira-sensei was surprised to see them.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> For Chabashira-sensei, it was a kind of public execution, but since they paid the school for it, there was no need to feel bad; “Oh, oh, I see...” — a teacher who had just previously gossiped about Chabashira-sensei&#x27;s transformation sounded impressed; thus, the public presentation of Chabashira-sensei continued until 4:00 p.m., using this corridor.<span class=\"pg\">p.163–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> In the end, Chabashira-sensei took first place, surpassing Kushida, with 63 desired pictures.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The 100,000-point hire; the standing-room-only conversion; the 63 photos; the victory.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The stunned Kushida; &quot;He&#x27;s a nuisance to have as an enemy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.158–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudō and his team make the wall for the adults pouring in.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/b> Mii-chan&#x27;s scream about the second slot filling.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p54-1\">← Before: Named in the staff-shift corridor gossip<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p184-1\">→ After: The Epilogue: first place; the fallout<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p184-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou hasebe-haruka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the epilogue  first place  the fallout  epilogue   finally  4 00 pm arrived  and the cultural festival finally came to an end  the accounting application was forcibly shut down  the results could be checked via cell phone starting 6 pm two hours later  it was around 5 30 when all the customers left and all the classmates  except koenji  gathered at the maid cafe  chabashira sensei ran out of the classroom like a rabbit as soon as 4 o clock came  running around in that outfit would ve been conspicuous  but let s leave it at that   i guess chabashira sensei s cosplay really struck    printed untagged  not assigned   after finishing my conversation with tsubaki and utomiya    ayanokoji ran into an exhausted chabashira sensei on her way back to class   thanks for your hard work today  you were very active    ayanokoji   what s with the compliment    chabashira sensei was clearly angry as she turned her childlike glare on him without hiding it   did you really hate it so much that we made you wear a maid s uniform    ayanokoji asked knowingly  she shook her head and looked down   when i went back to the staff room  my pictures were on the desks of    teachers everywhere  that s not all  i wonder how many teachers i ve been accosted by in the short time i ve been there  how many stories about my maid s uniform  how many embarrassments i ve suffered  for the time being  i sincerely wish to be a shellfish    chabashira sensei  it must have been a really hard time for her  because she felt the pressure so intensely   that s not for me to know  it must be symbolic of the teacher s popularity    ayanokoji   i am definitely not popular  you ve gone the extra mile    chabashira sensei  if he really believed there was such a thing as no popularity  he was going to have a hard time in the future  there must ve been many adults who appreciated chabashira sensei as a member of the opposite sex  even if they hadn t surfaced until now   that s it  the class won first place  so that s good    chabashira sensei swallowed hard and held back  as if she thought there was no point in blaming him any more   not good at all  if anything  the top sales amount was a sure thing even if i didn t do anything    chabashira sensei   i see  well  first place looks better than second and third place  doesn t it    ayanokoji   that s not like you to say    chabashira sensei   even so  i didn t think you were cooperating with ryuen s class under the guise of being hostile to them    chabashira sensei   if one class fights alone  the maximum strength is about 40 people  but if two classes join hands  nearly twice that number of people will join hands though  not foolproof    ayanokoji  propaganda doesn t necessarily have to go hand in hand on the surface  if one gathers a lot of people together  albeit in different forms  one can make a big show without spending a lot of money   even the staff room was surprised  everyone thought it was a real showdown    chabashira sensei only mentioned the festival s success  but not yagami s withdrawal  even first year students who were not directly involved in the event should know about it as well as teachers  but none have spoken about it with him  who they think was uninvolved  as a teacher at this school  she was making the right decision   by the way  aren t you going home    chabashira sensei   i have horikita waiting in the classroom  are you still working overtime    ayanokoji   i m making the rounds of the school  there have been several reports of    forgotten items filed by guests    chabashira sensei  so even when the festival was over  the teachers were still busy cleaning up afterwards  when he returned to the classroom with chabashira sensei  horikita was lying on her desk with her upper body on top  chabashira sensei and he looked at each other and decided not to talk to her  he went closer to check and found that she seemed to be asleep  a strong breeze was coming in through the opened window  for a moment  he wondered if i should cover her with her uniform jacket  but decided against it   nn    she was talking in her sleep  it was a bit of a startling statement   no    she was talking in her sleep  horikita must ve been tired today  he closed the window quietly so she wouldn t catch a cold before heading back to the corridor   i m going to let her sleep a little longer    chabashira sensei   are you waiting for her to wake up    chabashira sensei   well  we did manage to get first place at the school festival  she deserves this much    ayanokoji   you can leave  i ll take over here    chabashira sensei   are you sure    ayanokoji   as the man behind the scenes  you deserve that much    chabashira sensei   then i ll take you up on your offer    ayanokoji   but ayanokoji  don t ever think of a plan to humiliate me again  okay    chabashira sensei   you still care    ayanokoji   this is a day i will never forget in my life    chabashira sensei   well  chabashira sensei  thank you for your efforts  someday that will be a good memory too    ayanokoji   don t get cocky  student    chabashira sensei  she sighed and leaned against the classroom door  well then  i m going home now  class points at the end of the november festival  class a led by sakayanagi  1201  class b led by horikita  966  class c led by ryuen  740  class d led by ichinose  675  the results  first place  2nd year b class  100 class points  class points at the end of the november festival  sakayanagi s class a 1 201  4th place finish  horikita s class b 966  1st place finish  ryuen s class c 740  2nd place finish  ichinose s class d 675  7th place finish  he watches over her through the festival  she sleeps at her desk  chabashira stands guard  she speaks about airi  she s the star of the sum up","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p184-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Epilogue: first place; the fallout<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.184–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">§Epilogue — finally, 4:00 PM arrived, and the cultural festival finally came to an end; the accounting application was forcibly shut down; the results could be checked via cell phone starting 6 PM two hours later; it was around 5:30 when all the customers left and all the classmates (except Kōenji) gathered at the maid café. “After finishing my conversation with Tsubaki and Utomiya,” — Ayanokōji ran into an exhausted Chabashira-sensei on her way back to class. When he returned to the classroom with Chabashira-sensei, Horikita was lying on her desk with her upper body on top; Chabashira-sensei and he looked at each other and decided not to talk to her; he went closer to check and found that she seemed to be asleep.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Thanks for your hard work today. You were very active.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What&#x27;s with the compliment?” — Chabashira-sensei was clearly angry as she turned her childlike glare on him without hiding it.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Did you really hate it so much that we made you wear a maid&#x27;s uniform?” — Ayanokōji asked knowingly; she shook her head and looked down.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>40 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira-sensei ran out of the classroom like a rabbit as soon as 4 o&#x27;clock came; running around in that outfit would&#x27;ve been conspicuous, but let&#x27;s leave it at that.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I guess Chabashira-sensei&#x27;s cosplay really struck!” — printed untagged; not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When I went back to the staff room, my pictures were on the desks of …  teachers everywhere. That&#x27;s not all. I wonder how many teachers I&#x27;ve been accosted by in the short time I&#x27;ve been there, how many stories about my maid&#x27;s uniform, how many embarrassments I&#x27;ve suffered. For the time being, I sincerely wish to be a shellfish.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> It must have been a really hard time for her, because she felt the pressure so intensely.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s not for me to know. It must be symbolic of the teacher&#x27;s popularity.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am definitely not popular. You&#x27;ve gone the extra mile.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> If he really believed there was such a thing as no popularity, he was going to have a hard time in the future; there must&#x27;ve been many adults who appreciated Chabashira-sensei as a member of the opposite sex, even if they hadn&#x27;t surfaced until now.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s it. The class won first place, so that&#x27;s good.” — Chabashira-sensei swallowed hard and held back, as if she thought there was no point in blaming him any more.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not good at all. If anything, the top sales amount was a sure thing even if I didn&#x27;t do anything.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, first place looks better than second and third place, doesn&#x27;t it?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s not like you to say.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I didn&#x27;t think you were cooperating with Ryūen&#x27;s class under the guise of being hostile to them.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If one class fights alone, the maximum strength is about 40 people. But if two classes join hands, nearly twice that number of people will join hands though, not foolproof.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Propaganda doesn&#x27;t necessarily have to go hand in hand on the surface; if one gathers a lot of people together, albeit in different forms, one can make a big show without spending a lot of money.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even the staff room was surprised. Everyone thought it was a real showdown.” — Chabashira-sensei only mentioned the festival&#x27;s success, but not Yagami&#x27;s withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Even first-year students who were not directly involved in the event should know about it as well as teachers, but none have spoken about it with him, who they think was uninvolved; as a teacher at this school, she was making the right decision.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, aren&#x27;t you going home?” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have Horikita waiting in the classroom. Are you still working overtime?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m making the rounds of the school. There have been several reports of …  forgotten items filed by guests.” — Chabashira-sensei; so even when the festival was over, the teachers were still busy cleaning up afterwards.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A strong breeze was coming in through the opened window; for a moment, he wondered if I should cover her with her uniform jacket, but decided against it.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Nn……” — she was talking in her sleep; it was a bit of a startling statement.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “No…” — she was talking in her sleep.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita must&#x27;ve been tired today; he closed the window quietly so she wouldn&#x27;t catch a cold before heading back to the corridor.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m going to let her sleep a little longer.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you waiting for her to wake up?” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, we did manage to get first place at the school festival. She deserves this much.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can leave. I&#x27;ll take over here.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you sure?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As the man behind the scenes, you deserve that much.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then I&#x27;ll take you up on your offer.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But Ayanokōji, don&#x27;t ever think of a plan to humiliate me again, okay?” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You still care?” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a day I will never forget in my life.” — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, Chabashira-sensei, thank you for your efforts. Someday that will be a good memory too.” — Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don&#x27;t get cocky, student.” — Chabashira-sensei; she sighed and leaned against the classroom door.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Well then, I&#x27;m going home now; class points at the end of the November festival: Class A led by Sakayanagi: 1201; Class B led by Horikita: 966; Class C led by Ryūen: 740; Class D led by Ichinose: 675.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The results: first place, 2nd year B class (+100 class points); class points at the end of the November festival: Sakayanagi&#x27;s Class A 1,201 (4th place finish), Horikita&#x27;s Class B 966 (1st place finish), Ryūen&#x27;s Class C 740 (2nd place finish), Ichinose&#x27;s Class D 675 (7th place finish).<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He watches over her through the festival; she sleeps at her desk; Chabashira stands guard.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She speaks about Airi.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She&#x27;s the star of the sum-up.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v7-p153-1\">← Before: The 100,000-point hire; standing room only; 63 photos<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p11-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira sae mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mentions on pages  p 13 18  p 20  p 23 24  p 46  p 49  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">chabashira-sae mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.11-208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions on pages: p.13-18, p.20, p.23-24, p.46, p.49.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p12-1\">→ After: Final exam results; the anonymous 0–37 evaluation task<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p12-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"hondou-ryoutaro horikita-suzune sudou-ken chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae final exam results  the anonymous 0 37 evaluation task final exam results are announced in homeroom  she knows this time last year was the paper shuffle  the rules were standardized this year  first place gains 50 class points  fourth loses 50  cutoff averages of 39 or less in all subjects mean expulsion   regarding this year s final exam results  i ll start with the lowest ranked student  she calls hondo last  53  then moves up the ranks  top 10  sudo  finally horikita and keisei  93 5  announces class a 1st  class b 2nd  25 pts  she then unveils the anonymous evaluation task  each student numbers every second year classmate 0 37 except themselves  on memory and feelings alone   no oaa  no internet  no speaking  the teachers will never see the lists  one hour  groups for the trip will be built from it   but there s one thing i want you to do before we discuss it   the numbers you re about to assign represent how you evaluate your fellow classmates from your point of view   you have one hour to finish  if you fail to finish within the time limit  you will not receive the full explanation for the school trip   seriously  there are a lot of girls i ve never spoken to  and i have no idea about their oaa or anything like that  so it s going to be random  is that okay  she deliberately agitates the students  it seemed as though she was trying to agitate the students  while calling results from the bottom up  she fields the trip briefing questions with mild teasing  she allowed the whole school trip to hinge on this one hour  she announces horikita s tie for first  she gives him the lowest rank  she names him 10th","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Final exam results; the anonymous 0–37 evaluation task<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.12–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Final exam results are announced in homeroom; she knows this time last year was the Paper Shuffle; the rules were standardized this year; first place gains 50 Class Points, fourth loses 50; cutoff averages of 39 or less in all subjects mean expulsion. She calls Hondō last (53), then moves up the ranks; top 10: Sudō; finally Horikita and Keisei (93.5); announces Class A 1st, Class B 2nd (+25 pts). She then unveils the anonymous evaluation task: each student numbers every second-year classmate 0–37 except themselves, on memory and feelings alone — no OAA, no internet, no speaking; the teachers will never see the lists; one hour; groups for the trip will be built from it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hondou-ryoutaro.html\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Regarding this year&#x27;s final exam results, I&#x27;ll start with the lowest-ranked student.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“But there&#x27;s one thing I want you to do before we discuss it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The numbers you&#x27;re about to assign represent how you evaluate your fellow classmates from your point of view.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have one hour to finish. If you fail to finish within the time limit, you will not receive the full explanation for the school trip.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Seriously, there are a lot of girls I&#x27;ve never spoken to, and I have no idea about their OAA or anything like that, so it&#x27;s going to be random, is that okay…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She deliberately agitates the students (&quot;It seemed as though she was trying to agitate the students&quot;) while calling results from the bottom up; she fields the trip-briefing questions with mild teasing; she allowed the whole school trip to hinge on this one hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She announces Horikita&#x27;s tie for first.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/b> She gives him the lowest rank.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> She names him 10th.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p11-1\">← Before: chabashira-sae mentioned in passing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p17-1\">→ After: Hokkaido wins; the trip&#x27;s rules and purpose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p17-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke hondou-ryoutaro chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae hokkaido wins  the trip s rules and purpose the class vote results are revealed  hokkaido  which received three of the class votes  is designated as the destination  ayanokoji  horikita and keisei had voted kyoto   as a result of each class s choice  hokkaido  which received three of the class votes  was designated as the school trip destination   rest assured  there will be no special exam to compete for class points  she frames the trip with sun tzu   if you know the enemy and know yourself  you will not be in danger in a hundred battles  that s the theme of this school trip   if you know the enemy and know yourself  you will not be in danger in a hundred battles  she lays out the stakes  the school s strict structure hinders friendships  the trip exists to remove those boundaries  mixed fixed groups  one boy  one girl per second year class  eight per group  two groups of six  fixed for five days  group behavior mandatory outside the ryokan  deprivation of freedom  if disrespected  cell phones allowed  cash exchange up to 10 000 yen private points   the most important thing for you is whether or not you graduate in class a   even in free activities  individuals are not allowed to do as they please   you made a good point  hirata  she answers hondo s special exam fear with a laugh  fields hirata s questions about group rotation  the whole trip is themed on breaking down inter class barriers   possibly a set piece for an exam to come  she fields his questions and defends the fixed group decision  superficial acquaintanceships  she teases his fear of a special exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hokkaido wins; the trip&#x27;s rules and purpose<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.17–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The class-vote results are revealed: Hokkaido, which received three of the class votes, is designated as the destination; Ayanokōji, Horikita and Keisei had voted Kyoto. She frames the trip with Sun Tzu: &quot;If you know the enemy and know yourself, you will not be in danger in a hundred battles. That&#x27;s the theme of this school trip.&quot; She lays out the stakes: the school&#x27;s strict structure hinders friendships; the trip exists to remove those boundaries; mixed fixed groups (one boy, one girl per second-year class), eight per group (two groups of six), fixed for five days, group behavior mandatory outside the ryokan (&quot;deprivation of freedom&quot; if disrespected), cell phones allowed, cash exchange up to 10,000 yen private points.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"hondou-ryoutaro.html\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“As a result of each class&#x27;s choice, Hokkaido, which received three of the class votes, was designated as the school trip destination.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Rest assured, there will be no special exam to compete for class points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you know the enemy and know yourself, you will not be in danger in a hundred battles.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The most important thing for you is whether or not you graduate in Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even in free activities, individuals are not allowed to do as they please.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You made a good point, Hirata.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She answers Hondō&#x27;s special-exam fear with a laugh; fields Hirata&#x27;s questions about group rotation; the whole trip is themed on breaking down inter-class barriers — possibly a set piece for an exam to come.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> She fields his questions and defends the fixed-group decision (&quot;superficial acquaintanceships&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.21–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/b> She teases his fear of a special exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p12-1\">← Before: Final exam results; the anonymous 0–37 evaluation task<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p46-1\">→ After: The bus assignments<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p46-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the bus assignments  chabashira sensei no  2   the class b bus   chabashira sensei was in charge of groups 6 through 10   the ski group teacher assignments","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The bus assignments<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.46, 49<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei No. 2&quot; (the Class B bus)<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei was in charge of groups 6 through 10&quot; (the ski-group teacher assignments)<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p17-1\">← Before: Hokkaido wins; the trip&#x27;s rules and purpose<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p153-1\">→ After: The second-floor Daifugō speech<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p153-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae the second floor daifugo speech two mid level teachers hogging the massage chairs  the room is tense  horikita and ayanokoji wander in  the banter escalates  chie turns on ayanokoji first  then on chabashira s class b  the daifugo analogy unfolds  the joker gets named  chie storms off drunk  horikita chides her about it later down the hall  the massage intensity is set to five  the machine screams  chabashira howls  ayanokoji s curiosity is to blame   nn  hya  nn  nn   of course not  there s a strength that suits each person   chie  stop it already   chabashira  under her breath   i don t know what you want to say  but you re not free to say whatever you re thinking   chabashira   chie  stop it already   it s not that i don t think about it  to be honest  the situation is too different from that of the class i taught three years ago   that s right  i would expect nothing less   well  i m going after chie  if i let her go like that  she might drink heavily until the sun rises   that s all for today  horikita  ex class b homeroom teacher  brought low but not bowed  the daifugo monologue is chabashira s own view filtered through chie s mouth   she d actually use the joker honestly and never say so  they bicker over stiff shoulders and old failures  she s the only one chie listens to  awkward confrontation about the class lineage  she takes the teaching role seriously  he malfunctions a massage chair for fun  she tries to cover him from chie s glare","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The second-floor Daifugō speech<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.153–159<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two mid-level teachers hogging the massage chairs; the room is tense; Horikita and Ayanokōji wander in; the banter escalates; Chie turns on Ayanokōji first, then on Chabashira&#x27;s Class B; the Daifugō analogy unfolds; the Joker gets named; Chie storms off drunk; Horikita chides her about it later down the hall. The massage intensity is set to five; the machine screams; Chabashira howls; Ayanokōji&#x27;s curiosity is to blame.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Nn, hya, nn, nn!”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Of course not! There&#x27;s a strength that suits each person!”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Chie. Stop it already.” (Chabashira, under her breath)<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t know what you want to say, but you&#x27;re not free to say whatever you&#x27;re thinking.” (Chabashira)<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Chie. Stop it already.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It&#x27;s not that I don&#x27;t think about it, to be honest. The situation is too different from that of the class I taught three years ago.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s right. I would expect nothing less...”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I&#x27;m going after Chie. If I let her go like that, she might drink heavily until the sun rises.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s all for today, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ex-Class-B homeroom teacher; brought low but not bowed; the Daifugō monologue is Chabashira&#x27;s own view filtered through Chie&#x27;s mouth — she&#x27;d actually use the joker honestly and never say so.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> They bicker over stiff shoulders and old failures; she&#x27;s the only one Chie listens to.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Awkward confrontation about the class lineage; she takes the teaching role seriously.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He malfunctions a massage chair for fun; she tries to cover him from Chie&#x27;s glare.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p46-1\">← Before: The bus assignments<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p202-1\">→ After: Short Story &quot;Confused and Enlightened&quot; (Chabashira POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p202-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae short story  confused and enlightened   chabashira pov  chie storms off after the drunk eruption  chabashira is rattled  the evening s fallout pleats into her own self recrimination about three years ago   i m going back to my room  bye   i m sorry for what happened earlier   you re a little concerned  aren t you  sensei   to be honest  it s impossible not to think about it  your class is so different from the one i took three years ago   i don t know if ayanokoji kun is a joker  however i can t deny that he is strong as a fellow classmate  but i don t plan to have any scruples about it   okay  i m going to go find chie  if i leave her alone she might drink until dawn  the professional weariness of a former homeroom teacher who mugged class b of three years ago and started over with this new cohort  the joker metaphor sits heavy  she aims   she will not hold his talent against her own duty  the ss keeps the original slanted quotation punctuation  straight quotes    trail offs    kept as printed  she will not surrender her ex colleague to the bottle  the two lost souls keep saving each other  horikita s composure vs chabashira s restraint   two leaders who respect each other s edges  the  joker  naming is hers to carry now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p202-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Short Story &quot;Confused and Enlightened&quot; (Chabashira POV)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.202–203<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chie storms off after the drunk eruption; Chabashira is rattled; the evening&#x27;s fallout pleats into her own self-recrimination about three years ago.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “I&#x27;m going back to my room! Bye!”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “I&#x27;m sorry for what happened earlier.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “You&#x27;re a little concerned, aren&#x27;t you, sensei?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, it&#x27;s impossible not to think about it. Your class is so different from the one I took three years ago.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t know if Ayanokoji-kun is a Joker, however I can&#x27;t deny that he is strong as a fellow classmate. But I don&#x27;t plan to have any scruples about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay... I&#x27;m going to go find Chie, if I leave her alone she might drink until dawn.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The professional weariness of a former homeroom teacher who mugged Class B of three years ago and started over with this new cohort; the joker metaphor sits heavy; she aims — she will not hold his talent against her own duty.<span class=\"pg\">p.202–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The SS keeps the original slanted quotation punctuation (straight quotes, &quot;~&quot; trail-offs) — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> She will not surrender her ex-colleague to the bottle; the two lost souls keep saving each other.<span class=\"pg\">p.202–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita&#x27;s composure vs Chabashira&#x27;s restraint — two leaders who respect each other&#x27;s edges.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The &quot;Joker&quot; naming is hers to carry now.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v8-p153-1\">← Before: The second-floor Daifugō speech<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v9-p10-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira announces the final special exam of the semester she arrives for homeroom and tells class 1 d that before winter break they must take the last special exam of the second semester   an academic one on one match with no expulsion but a swing of 50 class points   it should come as no surprise to you that you didn t have any warning  but before winter break  you ll have to take the last special exam of the second semester   i understand your concerns  but there s no need to panic so much  it isn t the most feared kind of special exam that will cause students to drop out  she lays out the rules   a cooperative written test of 100 questions solved one at a time  points scored inversely to oaa academic rating  time bonuses  and unanswerable questions for absences   and insists the class has a real chance to win  calm  matter of fact instructor who downplays panic and frames the exam as class b s genuine opportunity  she spoke like a mother watching over her children","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v9-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira announces the final special exam of the semester<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.10–15<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She arrives for homeroom and tells Class 1-D that before winter break they must take the last special exam of the second semester — an academic one-on-one match with no expulsion but a swing of 50 class points. She lays out the rules — a cooperative written test of 100 questions solved one at a time, points scored inversely to OAA academic rating, time bonuses, and unanswerable questions for absences — and insists the class has a real chance to win.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It should come as no surprise to you that you didn&#x27;t have any warning, but before winter break, you&#x27;ll have to take the last special exam of the second semester.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand your concerns, but there&#x27;s no need to panic so much. It isn&#x27;t the most feared kind of special exam that will cause students to drop out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm, matter-of-fact instructor who downplays panic and frames the exam as Class B&#x27;s genuine opportunity; she spoke like a mother watching over her children.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v9_5-p59-1","v":"y2v9.5","y":2,"o":26,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  teachers  christmas eve at the mall walks with hoshinomiya in casual clothes  ribs ayanokoji that he s alone on christmas  he says he misses his girlfriend  she and chie head to karaoke  ayanokoji thinks of mashima sensei choosing sides would be troublesome   i thought you d be lovey dovey with your girlfriend today and yesterday  did you get dumped   chie s the only one who wants to sing  i m just being dragged along  in her usual suit instead of casual clothes  not a fan of christmas solitude  constantly at odds but together  karaoke day out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v9_5-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Teachers&#x27; Christmas Eve at the mall<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.5 · p.59–60<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks with Hoshinomiya in casual clothes; ribs Ayanokōji that he&#x27;s alone on Christmas; he says he misses his girlfriend; she and Chie head to karaoke; Ayanokōji thinks of Mashima-sensei choosing sides would be troublesome.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I thought you&#x27;d be lovey-dovey with your girlfriend today and yesterday. Did you get dumped?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Chie&#x27;s the only one who wants to sing. I&#x27;m just being dragged along.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> In her usual suit instead of casual clothes; not a fan of Christmas solitude.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Constantly at odds but together; karaoke day out.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p12-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  third term opening speech morning homeroom  warns them the term will pass in a flash  announces first ever feb  student teacher discussion  about career and parent including path  parents already surveyed  ike bursts out they haven t heard of it  she hears the parents  voices  realizes her bedhead after touching her own hair  leaves quietly   the third term starts today  they say january comes and goes  february flies by  and march disappears  this period of time will pass by you in a flash  make sure you don t spend your days out of habit  and stay focused  he blurts out his surprise  says the february meeting may be necessary for him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Third-term opening speech<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.12–13<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning homeroom; warns them the term will pass in a flash; announces first-ever Feb &#x27;student-teacher discussion&#x27; about career and parent-including path; parents already surveyed; Ike bursts out they haven&#x27;t heard of it; she hears the parents&#x27; voices; realizes her bedhead after touching her own hair; leaves quietly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The third term starts today. They say January comes and goes, February flies by, and March disappears; this period of time will pass by you in a flash. Make sure you don&#x27;t spend your days out of habit, and stay focused.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He blurts out his surprise.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Says the February meeting may be necessary for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p12-2\">→ After: Ch.1: Homeroom, bedhead and the notice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p12-2","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  homeroom  bedhead and the notice third term homeroom  she greets the class  hand on the lectern  and announces the flash by third term  then a forgotten notice  the school s first  student teacher discussion  next month on careers and employment  parents  survey already completed   the third term starts today  they say january comes and goes  february flies by  and march disappears  this period of time will pass by you in a flash  make sure you don t spend your days out of habit  and stay focused   i forgot to mention one important notice  next month  we plan to have our first  student teacher discussion  at this school  it will be centered around discussions about your career and employment  interwoven with talks about your school life up till now  of course  we have already completed a survey with your parents   even though high school isn t compulsory education  we can t ignore the parents  words and allow students to decide their own paths  of course  there will be parent teacher conferences when the time comes   if you re curious about anything  it s okay to come and ask me directly  a little bedhead at the back of her head  probably woke late and hurried  for someone telling students to stay focused  her words read a little unconvincing  realized her own bed hair on the way out  one hand closed the door  the other patted the back of her head  the page prints a doubled period in the narration  head apparently  kept as printed  her talk of parent teacher conferences lands ominously for ayanokoji  his parent might come again    his interior beat  not hers","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p12-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Homeroom, bedhead and the notice<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.12–13<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Third-term homeroom; she greets the class, hand on the lectern, and announces the flash-by third term; then a forgotten notice: the school&#x27;s first ‘student-teacher discussion’ next month on careers and employment, parents&#x27; survey already completed.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The third term starts today. They say January comes and goes, February flies by, and March disappears; this period of time will pass by you in a flash. Make sure you don’t spend your days out of habit, and stay focused.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I forgot to mention one important notice. Next month, we plan to have our first ‘student-teacher discussion’ at this school. It will be centered around discussions about your career and employment, interwoven with talks about…”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Even though high school isn’t compulsory education, we can’t ignore the parents’ words and allow students to decide their own paths. Of course, there will be parent-teacher conferences when the time comes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I forgot to mention one important notice. Next month, we plan to have our first ‘student-teacher discussion’ at this school. It will be centered around discussions about your career and employment, interwoven with talks about your school life up till now. Of course, we have already completed a survey with your parents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re curious about anything, it’s okay to come and ask me directly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> A little bedhead at the back of her head; probably woke late and hurried; for someone telling students to stay focused, her words read a little unconvincing.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Realized her own bed hair on the way out; one hand closed the door, the other patted the back of her head.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page prints a doubled period in the narration (“head..Apparently”); kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her talk of parent-teacher conferences lands ominously for Ayanokōji (his parent might come again) — his interior beat, not hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Third-term opening speech<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p14-1\">→ After: Ch.1: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p14-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  passing mentions  locator cross check  passing mention   after chabashira sensei left the classroom  the class was engrossed in topics passing mention   the second drawer  maybe  as chabashira sensei said  this third term might pass by","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.14–30<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — After Chabashira-sensei left the classroom, the class was engrossed in topics<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — the second drawer. Maybe, as Chabashira-sensei said, this third term might pass by<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p12-2\">← Before: Ch.1: Homeroom, bedhead and the notice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p31-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Announcing Survival and Elimination<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p31-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  announcing survival and elimination morning homeroom  announces the exam  reports that the teacher side has been monitoring students all along  launches into the rules  warning that this exam is dangerous  second years only  the rotation shown on screen  she explains elimination rules  rewards excluding zero  protection mechanics  written rules for leaders  eliminated leaders can t be replaced  she disagrees with collusion logic in the written rules  closes with a vote refreshing vote  answers horikita s question  hands back to the class  friction appears immediately   survival and elimination  that sounds very dangerous   wow  e expulsion  seriously  i thought it was possible  but  blurts out the expected reaction first  responds to his prompt defense of horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p31-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Announcing Survival and Elimination<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.31–46<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning homeroom: announces the exam; reports that the teacher-side has been monitoring students all along; launches into the rules; warning that this exam is dangerous; second-years only; the rotation shown on screen. She explains elimination rules; rewards excluding zero; protection mechanics; written rules for leaders; eliminated leaders can&#x27;t be replaced; she disagrees with collusion logic in the written rules; closes with a vote-refreshing vote. Answers Horikita&#x27;s question; hands back to the class; friction appears immediately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Survival and Elimination? That sounds very dangerous...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Wow… E-expulsion, seriously… I thought it was possible, but…!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Blurts out the expected reaction first.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Responds to his prompt defense of Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p14-1\">← Before: Ch.1: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p31-2\">→ After: Ch.2: The announcement and the rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p31-2","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  the announcement and the rules thursday of the third term  she arrives stern faced as ever  her expression is always severe  she straightens herself  several students already sense something is different   good morning  today i want to talk about our first special exam of this third term   this special exam has slightly complicated rules   this special exam will only be conducted among second year students   in this special exam  there are diversified tasks based on categories prepared by the school  each class will choose a category  select a difficulty  and issue a task to the target class in a specific order   indeed  some areas might not be primarily related to a student s responsibilities  but those who are ignorant of the world are often eliminated when they step into society  in other words  even if you can t study  those who can follow the conversation are often treasured  this means that this time  your general knowledge as a human being will be tested   it seems there are some who find it hard to understand  so let me simplify it  basically  it has aspects similar to a quiz  the attacking class will present a quiz  and the defending class will solve it  it s as simple as that   be careful with your careless remarks  ike   the attacking class will select the difficulty level after choosing the category  the basic  first level is of average difficulty  the second and third levels   with higher difficulties can also be chosen  but to do so  you need to spend the points that you have acquired  for every point you spend  you can increase the difficulty level by one  the rule sentence runs across the page boundary  the extraction splits it there  kept as printed   the attacking side will nominate five people from the defending class and assign them tasks  you can keep selecting the same student  or you can change who you select  the same applies to categories   also  if a class with any eliminated students sinks to the bottom of the four classes  one of those eliminated students will be expelled   and the reward for this special exam is as follows   to answer the easier question first  even if you are eliminated  you just won t be nominated by the attacker afterward  you ll continue to wait in the same place as the other students and are free to participate in the conversation   as for a leader getting eliminated  the leader does not participate in any tasks to begin with  this means that they cannot be nominated by the attacker and therefore have no fear of being eliminated   correct  those who are chosen as leaders are effectively exempted from the risk of expulsion  whether they consider this a perk or not is up to the individuals   also  it s important to note that during this special exam  the use of mobile phones will be permitted at all times  except when the defensive side is solving a problem   the special exam will be conducted next friday  first of all  by the end of school next monday  find time  decide the leader through mutual discussion  and let me know  if you can t choose a leader  as you can probably guess  we will randomly select one   i understand everything  but it s going to be a tough fight  all i can say is   do your best not to place last  that s it  pages 39 42 print the reward table  1st  100  2nd 3rd  50  4th  100  extension on tie  all tie  100 each  and the bottom rank expulsion rule as displayed slides  not as her speech beyond the line  as follows","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p31-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: The announcement and the rules<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.31–42<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Thursday of the third term; she arrives stern-faced as ever; her expression is always severe; she straightens herself; several students already sense something is different.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Good morning. Today I want to talk about our first special exam of this third term.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This special exam has slightly complicated rules.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This special exam will only be conducted among second-year students.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this special exam, there are diversified tasks based on categories prepared by the school. Each class will choose a category, select a difficulty, and issue a task to the target class in a specific order.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Indeed, some areas might not be primarily related to a student’s responsibilities. But those who are ignorant of the world are often eliminated when they step into society. In other words, even if you can’t study, those who can follow the conversation are often treasured. This means that this time, your general knowledge as a human being will be tested.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems there are some who find it hard to understand, so let me simplify it. Basically, it has aspects similar to a quiz. The attacking class will present a quiz, and the defending class will solve it. It’s as simple as that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Be careful with your careless remarks, Ike.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The attacking class will select the difficulty level after choosing the category. The basic, first level is of average difficulty. The second and third levels”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “with higher difficulties can also be chosen, but to do so, you need to spend the points that you have acquired. For every point you spend, you can increase the difficulty level by one.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The rule sentence runs across the page boundary; the extraction splits it there; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The attacking side will nominate five people from the defending class and assign them tasks. You can keep selecting the same student, or you can change who you select. The same applies to categories.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also… if a class with any eliminated students sinks to the bottom of the four classes, one of those eliminated students will be expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And the reward for this special exam is as follows:”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To answer the easier question first, even if you are eliminated, you just won’t be nominated by the attacker afterward. You’ll continue to wait in the same place as the other students and are free to participate in the conversation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As for a leader getting eliminated, the leader does not participate in any tasks to begin with. This means that they cannot be nominated by the attacker and therefore have no fear of being eliminated.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Correct. Those who are chosen as leaders are effectively exempted from the risk of expulsion. Whether they consider this a perk or not is up to the individuals.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, it’s important to note that during this special exam, the use of mobile phones will be permitted at all times, except when the defensive side is solving a problem.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The special exam will be conducted next Friday. First of all, by the end of school next Monday, find time, decide the leader through mutual discussion, and let me know. If you can’t choose a leader, as you can probably guess, we will randomly select one.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand everything, but it’s going to be a tough fight. All I can say is—.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do your best not to place last. That’s it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Pages 39–42 print the reward table (1st +100; 2nd/3rd −50; 4th −100; extension on tie; all-tie −100 each) and the bottom-rank expulsion rule as displayed slides, not as her speech beyond the line &quot;as follows&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p31-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Announcing Survival and Elimination<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p50-1\">→ After: Ch.2: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p50-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  passing mentions  locator cross check  passing mention   including what they couldn t hear during chabashira sensei s explanation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.50–50<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — Including what they couldn&#x27;t hear during Chabashira-sensei&#x27;s explanation,<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p31-2\">← Before: Ch.2: The announcement and the rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p124-1\">→ After: Ch.6: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p124-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6  passing mentions  locator cross check  passing mention   without any absences  chabashira sensei left the classroom with words of","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.124–124<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — without any absences, Chabashira-sensei left the classroom with words of<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p50-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.7: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p191-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7  passing mentions  locator cross check  passing mention   chabashira sensei  passing mention   sakayanagi took her eyes off her and urged chabashira  the teacher in","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.191–197<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — Chabashira-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention — Sakayanagi took her eyes off her and urged Chabashira, the teacher in<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p124-1\">← Before: Ch.6: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p199-1\">→ After: Ch.7: The dismissal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p199-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7  the dismissal she is present at the dismissal   announces the exam is complete  says details including class a s expulsion will follow next week  she dismisses class for the day  she reveals nothing about class a s fate beyond the order of events  the dismissal feels surreal after the long exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: The dismissal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She is present at the dismissal — announces the exam is complete; says details including Class A’s expulsion will follow next week; she dismisses class for the day.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She reveals nothing about Class A’s fate beyond the order of events; the dismissal feels surreal after the long exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v10-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.7: passing mentions (locator cross-check)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p11-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  interviewing the oddball fifth and final day of the two person interviews  ayanokoji is called to the career counseling room last   you re finally here  have a seat   as a homeroom teacher  i can t help but be busy during this time  but i feel a little better knowing that the two person interviews will be over today  it was a good decision to leave the two oddballs for last   what  are you shocked to be treated on the same level as koenji   well  i don t have many opportunities to talk with each student  before we talk about your future plans  let s talk about your school life  if there s anything you want the school to improve  i d like to hear it   i don t think you re holding back   i don t know much about your past  i think it was wrong of me to pretend to know about it and try to leverage that  but now  as a homeroom teacher  i want to fully understand the abilities of the students i m in charge of  that s my duty   so tell me  if your parents want you to go on to higher education  can i assume that you have the ability to do so   yes  that s what i heard   that is  you re scheduled for the last slot  the father first told her a proxy would attend  then called to say he would come himself  he wants notice of any change to the whole class s schedule  she interviews him as homeroom teacher  he gives no complaints and no plans  she takes his word at face value","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Interviewing the oddball<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.11–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fifth and final day of the two-person interviews; Ayanokōji is called to the career counseling room last.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You&#x27;re finally here. Have a seat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“As a homeroom teacher, I can&#x27;t help but be busy during this time. But I feel a little better knowing that the two-person interviews will be over today. It was a good decision to leave the two oddballs for last.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What, are you shocked to be treated on the same level as Kōenji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I don&#x27;t have many opportunities to talk with each student. Before we talk about your future plans, let&#x27;s talk about your school life. If there&#x27;s anything you want the school to improve, I&#x27;d like to hear it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t think you&#x27;re holding back...”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t know much about your past. I think it was wrong of me to pretend to know about it and try to leverage that. But now, as a homeroom teacher, I want to fully understand the abilities of the students I&#x27;m in charge of. That&#x27;s my duty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So tell me, if your parents want you to go on to higher education, can I assume that you have the ability to do so?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, that&#x27;s what I heard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That is, you&#x27;re scheduled for the last slot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The father first told her a proxy would attend; then called to say he would come himself; he wants notice of any change to the whole class&#x27;s schedule.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She interviews him as homeroom teacher; he gives no complaints and no plans; she takes his word at face value.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p15-1\">→ After: Ch.1: The unpleasant question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p15-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  the unpleasant question the interview runs long  she presses about his future  he gives nothing   i m sorry  that might have been an unpleasant question  she sails past her own discomfort  the interview is done for today","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: The unpleasant question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.15<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The interview runs long; she presses about his future; he gives nothing.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I&#x27;m sorry. That might have been an unpleasant question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She sails past her own discomfort; the interview is done for today.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p11-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Interviewing the oddball<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p35-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Her briefing on the bus<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p35-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  her briefing on the bus 20 minutes into the highway ride  she takes the microphone and explains the camp to the whole bus before they even reach the mountains   i think it s about time to explain the details of the training camp  as i mentioned briefly at school  it has been decided to hold a three night  four day experiential learning exchange meeting for all years   let me remind you not to take the exchange meeting as a special exam  there will be no change in class points this time   it s unfortunate that ichihashi had to stay home due to illness  but it was a blessing in disguise   i think some of you may have already noticed  but even though it s for all years  this time  only five representatives from each class of the third years are participating  this is taking into account various circumstances   your main objective will be to interact with the first year students  but it s not like you can get along with everyone just from our vague instructions  as soon as you arrive at the camp  all years will be divided into 20 groups   this printout also includes some rewards you can get from the games and the conditions for obtaining them  you should read it carefully   oaa standards of balance are not taken into account at all  it wouldn t be strange if there was a drastic bias   but just because they re excellent doesn t mean they ll always win  especially in this case   i hope it s clear that there s no need to be too concerned about winning or losing this time   i hope you ll behave in a way that is not embarrassing to a senpai at the training camp   gather in your assigned groups  from now on  for the next three days  follow your leader s instructions  have discussions  and get along with everyone  absentees named in the list  second years ichihashi and ichinose  four first years  including ishigami  she runs the briefing  the routine turns to her exchange meeting rules","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Her briefing on the bus<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.35–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">20 minutes into the highway ride; she takes the microphone and explains the camp to the whole bus before they even reach the mountains.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I think it&#x27;s about time to explain the details of the training camp. As I mentioned briefly at school, it has been decided to hold a three-night, four-day experiential learning exchange meeting for all years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Let me remind you not to take the exchange meeting as a special exam. There will be no change in class points this time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It&#x27;s unfortunate that Ichihashi had to stay home due to illness, but it was a blessing in disguise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think some of you may have already noticed, but even though it&#x27;s for all years, this time, only five representatives from each class of the third-years are participating. This is taking into account various circumstances.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your main objective will be to interact with the first-year students, but it&#x27;s not like you can get along with everyone just from our vague instructions. As soon as you arrive at the camp, all years will be divided into 20 groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This printout also includes some rewards you can get from the games and the conditions for obtaining them. You should read it carefully.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “OAA standards of balance are not taken into account at all. It wouldn&#x27;t be strange if there was a drastic bias.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But just because they&#x27;re excellent doesn&#x27;t mean they&#x27;ll always win. Especially in this case.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hope it&#x27;s clear that there&#x27;s no need to be too concerned about winning or losing this time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hope you’ll behave in a way that is not embarrassing to a senpai at the training camp.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Gather in your assigned groups. From now on, for the next three days, follow your leader&#x27;s instructions, have discussions, and get along with everyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Absentees named in the list: second-years Ichihashi and Ichinose; four first-years, including Ishigami.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She runs the briefing; the routine turns to her exchange-meeting rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p15-1\">← Before: Ch.1: The unpleasant question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p214-1\">→ After: Short Story: The Student in Front of Me<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p214-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"narration spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae short story  the student in front of me chabashira s pov on the two person interviews  she remembers the two oddballs   koenji first  ayanokoji last   phew  koenji is such a troublesome student   his career aspiration was to be a free person  he didn t need human relationships  his only concerns were about improving his own body  and so on   if i submit this  who knows what the higher ups will say   the last one left was ayanokoji  who could be equally as troublesome as koenji   honestly  i couldn t imagine what kind of one on one meeting it would be   you re finally here  have a seat   as a homeroom teacher  i can t help but be busy during this time  but i feel a little better knowing that the two person interviews will be over today  it was a good decision to leave the two oddballs for last   two oddballs  you say   do you think koenji is more of an oddball  well  i can understand why you d think that  but to me  there s not much difference  you re quite the oddball yourself   one thing was for certain  he didn t want to be compared to koenji   well  i don t have many opportunities to talk with each student  before we talk about your future plans  let s talk about your school life  if there s anything you want the school to improve  i d like to hear it   i don t have anything in particular  as an individual  i m satisfied   i see  do you have any trouble in your relationships with friends  or anything you want to consult about   i don t   he was definitely an oddball  unlike koenji  he was concise and efficient  but like koenji  he lacked substance   chabashira sensei  you ve changed quite a bit too   i felt as if ayanokoji was interviewing me  which was strange   i don t think i ve changed  but i might ve become more honest than before   the student in front of me is a whole generation younger than me  yet  why does he sometimes seem like someone who s lived as long or even longer than me  it took courage for me to accept this feeling   a teacher s gaze upon the children in the class must always be equal   ayanokoji would casually cross that boundary  there were times when i felt like i wanted him to know my weaknesses   though  this was originally the feeling that we wanted students to have toward their teachers    anyway  if there s anything you re concerned about in your school life  don t hesitate to tell me   i cleared my throat to dispel unnecessary thoughts   the person in front of me now was an important student  nothing more  nothing less   i d like to know whether you re hoping to go on to higher education or get a job  if you ve made up your mind  please tell me   i decided to move the conversation forward to distract myself from that strange feeling  she interviews him as homeroom teacher  he crosses the teacher student boundary casually  she distracts herself with the meeting mechanics  the other oddball  the two troublemakers for last","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p214-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Short Story: The Student in Front of Me<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.214–217<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira&#x27;s POV on the two-person interviews; she remembers the two oddballs — Kōenji first, Ayanokōji last.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Phew... Kōenji is such a troublesome student.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If I submit this, who knows what the higher-ups will say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You&#x27;re finally here. Have a seat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “His career aspiration was to be a free person, he didn&#x27;t need human relationships, his only concerns were about improving his own body, and so on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “The last one left was Ayanokōji, who could be equally as troublesome as Kōenji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Honestly, I couldn&#x27;t imagine what kind of one-on-one meeting it would be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As a homeroom teacher, I can&#x27;t help but be busy during this time. But I feel a little better knowing that the two-person interviews will be over today. It was a good decision to leave the two oddballs for last.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Two oddballs, you say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think Kōenji is more of an oddball? Well, I can understand why you&#x27;d think that, but to me, there&#x27;s not much difference. You&#x27;re quite the oddball yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “One thing was for certain, he didn&#x27;t want to be compared to Kōenji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I don&#x27;t have many opportunities to talk with each student. Before we talk about your future plans, let&#x27;s talk about your school life. If there&#x27;s anything you want the school to improve, I&#x27;d like to hear it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t have anything in particular. As an individual, I&#x27;m satisfied.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Do you have any trouble in your relationships with friends, or anything you want to consult about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “He was definitely an oddball. Unlike Kōenji, he was concise and efficient, but like Kōenji, he lacked substance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Chabashira-sensei, you&#x27;ve changed quite a bit too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I felt as if Ayanokōji was interviewing me, which was strange.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t think I&#x27;ve changed. But I might&#x27;ve become more honest than before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “The student in front of me is a whole generation younger than me. Yet, why does he sometimes seem like someone who&#x27;s lived as long or even longer than me? It took courage for me to accept this feeling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “A teacher&#x27;s gaze upon the children in the class must always be equal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Ayanokōji would casually cross that boundary. There were times when I felt like I wanted him to know my weaknesses.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “Though, this was originally the feeling that we wanted students to have toward their teachers.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “... Anyway. If there&#x27;s anything you&#x27;re concerned about in your school life, don&#x27;t hesitate to tell me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I cleared my throat to dispel unnecessary thoughts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “The person in front of me now was an important student. Nothing more, nothing less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;d like to know whether you&#x27;re hoping to go on to higher education or get a job. If you&#x27;ve made up your mind, please tell me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> “I decided to move the conversation forward to distract myself from that strange feeling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She interviews him as homeroom teacher; he crosses the teacher-student boundary casually; she distracts herself with the meeting mechanics.<span class=\"pg\">p.214–217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The other oddball; the two troublemakers for last.<span class=\"pg\">p.214–215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v11-p35-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Her briefing on the bus<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p10-1","v":"y2v12","y":2,"o":31,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae prologue  named in hoshinomiya s monologue hoshinomiya chie s printed monologue names  sae chan  as her best friend and rival   chabashira sae   and states her motive for becoming a teacher  to eliminate all hope from sae s dream of graduating a class a  chabashira does not appear  she is named by the monologist  the  defective goods  history the class carries is the trail hoshinomiya still resents","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Prologue: named in Hoshinomiya&#x27;s monologue<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12 · p.10–11<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hoshinomiya Chie&#x27;s printed monologue names &quot;Sae-chan&quot; as her best friend and rival — Chabashira Sae — and states her motive for becoming a teacher: to eliminate all hope from Sae&#x27;s dream of graduating a Class A.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira does not appear; she is named by the monologist. The &quot;defective goods&quot; history the class carries is the trail Hoshinomiya still resents.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p12-1\">→ After: Ch.1: Announcing the special exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p12-1","v":"y2v12","y":2,"o":31,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  announcing the special exam thursday  the second week of march  the morning greetings are sparse  she appears with a calm demeanor and  before announcing the exam  prefaces it with a personal story  her eighth year at advanced nurturing high school  six years leading two classes  never moving up from class d   i will now announce the end of year special exam and its contents  but before that  i would like to share a little personal story   this is my eighth year as a teacher at the advanced nurturing high school  she reflects aloud that she once believed a fair teacher must stay distant  the class s own students made her realize such detachment is also escapism  she shows the rankings  class a 1098  class b 983  class c 730  class d 654  and notes that this class dispelled the  defective goods  image   however  no one calls you defective goods anymore   however  i don t want you to become complacent  the monitor reveals the setup  special building  a vs c and b vs d  three representatives per class  vanguard 5 lives  middle guard 7  general 10  at least one representative from each gender  substitutes allowed  deadline sunday  even the teachers weren t told the details  it likely isn t physical  most of the rules will be disclosed only on the day  end of year special exam  three representatives per class  vanguard 5 lives  middle guard 7 lives  general 10 lives  at least one representative from each gender  knockout format  winner takes all  no draws   that s right  but as i ve just told you  i can t tell you anything beyond what i ve explained   and as for the crucial reward  the winning class will earn 200 points  horikita stands and floats  a battle through conversation  as a possibility  chabashira answers only that it is quite possible  without confirming","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Announcing the special exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12 · p.12–19<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Thursday, the second week of March; the morning greetings are sparse; she appears with a calm demeanor and, before announcing the exam, prefaces it with a personal story: her eighth year at Advanced Nurturing High School, six years leading two classes, never moving up from Class D. She reflects aloud that she once believed a fair teacher must stay distant; the class&#x27;s own students made her realize such detachment is also escapism; she shows the rankings (Class A 1098, Class B 983, Class C 730, Class D 654) and notes that this class dispelled the &quot;defective goods&quot; image. The monitor reveals the setup: special building; A vs C and B vs D; three representatives per class (vanguard 5 lives, middle guard 7, general 10); at least one representative from each gender; substitutes allowed; deadline Sunday; even the teachers weren&#x27;t told the details; it likely isn&#x27;t physical; most of the rules will be disclosed only on the day.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I will now announce the end-of-year special exam and its contents. But before that, I would like to share a little personal story.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This is my eighth year as a teacher at the Advanced Nurturing High School.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;However, no one calls you defective goods anymore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, I don&#x27;t want you to become complacent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> End-of-year special exam: three representatives per class (vanguard 5 lives, middle guard 7 lives, general 10 lives); at least one representative from each gender; knockout format; winner takes all, no draws.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s right. But as I&#x27;ve just told you, I can&#x27;t tell you anything beyond what I&#x27;ve explained.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;And as for the crucial reward, the winning class will earn 200 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita stands and floats &quot;a battle through conversation&quot; as a possibility; Chabashira answers only that it is quite possible, without confirming.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p10-1\">← Before: Prologue: named in Hoshinomiya&#x27;s monologue<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p29-1\">→ After: Mentioned in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p29-1","v":"y2v12","y":2,"o":31,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae mentioned in passing named in passing    even chabashira sensei doesn t know the details of the exam   horikita  named in passing    as chabashira sensei had mentioned  physical abilities were not necessary  and the academic abilities needed were proven to be minimal   mashima s explanation aftermath  passing mention only  neither appearance is a scene presence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12 · p.29, 78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in passing — “Even Chabashira-sensei doesn&#x27;t know the details of the exam” (Horikita). Named in passing — “as Chabashira-sensei had mentioned, physical abilities were not necessary, and the academic abilities needed were proven to be minimal” (Mashima&#x27;s explanation aftermath).<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only; neither appearance is a scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.29, 78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Announcing the special exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.3: Enters with Mashima<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p67-1","v":"y2v12","y":2,"o":31,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  enters with mashima as the representatives get restless waiting  there is movement in the room   mashima sensei and chabashira sensei appear together  as if announcing the start of the special exam   you better quiet down now  is printed with no speaker tag  it is unattributable on these pages  see this volume s attribution gaps","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Enters with Mashima<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12 · p.67–68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As the representatives get restless waiting, there is movement in the room — Mashima-sensei and Chabashira-sensei appear together, as if announcing the start of the special exam.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> &quot;You better quiet down now&quot; is printed with no speaker tag; it is unattributable on these pages (see this volume&#x27;s attribution gaps).<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12-p29-1\">← Before: Mentioned in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p11-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 1  the class debrief after the special exam chabashira tells the representatives what can be shared and leaves them to discuss the exam s details   of course  it s up to you to decide what should be done  we re going to depart soon  but you should discuss and resolve any concerns   yes  that s the plan  even the representatives don t know in detail what kind of battles were fought individually  we believe it s necessary to share information  back in the classroom  chabashira announces the end of year special exam was won  class 2 b gains significant class points  promotion to class a near certain   but maezono was expelled   the end of year special exam ended in your victory   half correct  half incorrect  indeed  maezono is processing her expulsion in the staff room  but if you can come up with the necessary private points right here  it s possible to avoid it   no  i wonder  at least not right away  she s only just been told about her expulsion and she s severely shaken  until that settles  it will be difficult   there are many things you might be curious about  but i m not allowed to speak on the details  if you have questions  it would be good to discuss them later  that s all from me  chabashira observes the student led discussion in silence  then cuts it off once koenji has left   koenji isn t here  so maybe we should just disband for now  the class points printed after the exam  horikita s class a 1233  sakayanagi s class b 1093  ryuen s class c 1040 1090  ichinose s class d 714  p 22  with sakayanagi s expulsion  her class would drop 300 points to 793  p 23  she observes objectively as he explains the expulsion to the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: The class debrief after the special exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.11–22<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira tells the representatives what can be shared and leaves them to discuss the exam&#x27;s details. Back in the classroom, Chabashira announces the end-of-year special exam was won; Class 2-B gains significant class points, promotion to Class A near-certain — but Maezono was expelled. Chabashira observes the student-led discussion in silence, then cuts it off once Kōenji has left.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Of course. It’s up to you to decide what should be done. We’re going to depart soon, but you should discuss and resolve any concerns.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes, that’s the plan. Even the representatives don’t know in detail what kind of battles were fought individually. We believe it’s necessary to share information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The end-of-year special exam ended in your victory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Half correct, half incorrect. Indeed, Maezono is processing her expulsion in the staff room, but if you can come up with the necessary private points right here, it’s possible to avoid it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No... I wonder. At least not right away. She’s only just been told about her expulsion and she’s severely shaken. Until that settles, it will be difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are many things you might be curious about, but I’m not allowed to speak on the details. If you have questions, it would be good to discuss them later. That’s all from me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kōenji isn’t here, so maybe we should just disband for now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The class points printed after the exam: Horikita&#x27;s class A 1233, Sakayanagi&#x27;s class B 1093, Ryūen&#x27;s class C 1040–1090, Ichinose&#x27;s class D 714 (p.22). With Sakayanagi&#x27;s expulsion, her class would drop 300 points to 793 (p.23).<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She observes objectively as he explains the expulsion to the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.4: The Keyaki Mall gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p63-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakagami mashima-tomonari hoshinomiya-chie chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 4  the keyaki mall gathering ayanokoji asks to meet her at keyaki mall at 11 00  she arrives early and spots him at 10 50  uneasy about meeting a student there   you re quite early   you haven t really kept me waiting  there s still some time before our appointment  no need to worry   i never thought i d be meeting a student at keyaki mall   of course not   ayanokoji  you speak too lightly   an apology is not enough  isn t it   horikita  and hirata too  is the situation much worse than i imagined   is that so  i thought you were being put on the spot because of that incident   then that s good   how students fight within the rules is up to them  i m pleased that the class won and how it s likely to move up to class a   it s certainly not pleasant  but as a teacher  getting too involved in student or class issues often leads to trouble  i ve learned the hard way from trying to use you before  i d rather not repeat that   well  i m not sure if i should call it a blessing in disguise  but thanks to that  i was able to wake myself up too  it s because you re a student who doesn t show any mercy  even when going up against teachers  that i was able to do so   i m not good at considering others  intentions  it looks like one person has arrived   hmm  sakagami sensei   mashima sensei  i haven t been informed of the details by ayanokoji either  but perhaps it isn t too late now to hear what he has to say   chie  no  hoshinomiya sensei   so it was just an excuse to talk with you  ayanokoji kun   don t tell me you intend to doubt a student   well  yes  she agrees to confront hoshinomiya  he tells her he will change hoshinomiya s mind by the end of spring break  sakagami insists on impartial evidence before acting  mashima scolds ayanokoji  then stays for the confrontation  the unanimous vote special exam grudge between them resurfaces","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: The Keyaki Mall gathering<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.63–69<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji asks to meet her at Keyaki Mall at 11:00; she arrives early and spots him at 10:50, uneasy about meeting a student there.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakagami.html\">Sakagami<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re quite early.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You haven’t really kept me waiting. There’s still some time before our appointment; no need to worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I never thought I’d be meeting a student at Keyaki Mall.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course not.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokōji. You speak too lightly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “An apology is not enough, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita... and Hirata too? Is the situation much worse than I imagined?”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? I thought you were being put on the spot because of that incident...”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “...Then that’s good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How students fight within the rules is up to them. I’m pleased that the class won and how it’s likely to move up to Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “...It’s certainly not pleasant, but as a teacher, getting too involved in student or class issues often leads to trouble. I’ve learned the hard way from trying to use you before. I’d rather not repeat that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m not sure if I should call it a blessing in disguise, but thanks to that, I was able to wake myself up too... It’s because you’re a student who doesn’t show any mercy, even when going up against teachers, that I was able to do so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not good at considering others’ intentions. It looks like one person has arrived.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm…? Sakagami-sensei...?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Mashima-sensei, I haven’t been informed of the details by Ayanokōji either, but perhaps it isn’t too late now to hear what he has to say—”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “...Chie, no, Hoshinomiya-sensei?”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So it was just an excuse to talk with you, Ayanokōji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t tell me you intend to doubt a student?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “...Well... yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She agrees to confront Hoshinomiya; he tells her he will change Hoshinomiya&#x27;s mind by the end of spring break.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakagami<\/b> Sakagami insists on impartial evidence before acting.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Mashima scolds Ayanokōji, then stays for the confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The unanimous-vote special exam grudge between them resurfaces.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p11-1\">← Before: Ch.1: The class debrief after the special exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p70-1\">→ After: Ch.4: Mashima&#x27;s room; Hoshinomiya&#x27;s grudge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p70-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie mashima-tomonari sakagami chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 4  mashima s room  hoshinomiya s grudge the three teachers confront hoshinomiya sensei  the discussion moves to mashima sensei s room in the teachers  dormitory   you know what this is about  chie   using students  no  teachers deviating from the rules to win an exam is not something to overlook   it s not just about using ayanokoji for misconduct  we can t just watch as you continue to engage in it  chie   i m not joking  i m seriously worried   it can t be helped that you hate me  but now we aren t students we re teachers  is it wrong to aim for class a for the sake of the students   there s no way i can do that  teachers holding back their students  progress   to think to that extent  you  no  i suppose it s natural  i can t make any excuses   give her time   i m sorry i couldn t be of more help  even though you confided in me   i couldn t solve it immediately  but i deeply appreciate that you had the courage to tell me   that is  ah  yes  but   you will change  what are you talking about   you are  who are you really  her grudge  hoshinomiya vows she will never let chabashira graduate her class from class a  mashima proposes giving hoshinomiya time to think over spring break  sakagami threatens escalation if she acts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p70-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: Mashima&#x27;s room; Hoshinomiya&#x27;s grudge<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.70–76<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The three teachers confront Hoshinomiya-sensei; the discussion moves to Mashima-sensei&#x27;s room in the teachers&#x27; dormitory.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"sakagami.html\">Sakagami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You know what this is about, Chie.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Using students... No, teachers deviating from the rules to win an exam is not something to overlook.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s not just about using Ayanokōji for misconduct. We can’t just watch as you continue to engage in it, Chie.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not joking. I’m seriously worried.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “...It can’t be helped that you hate me. But now we aren’t students—we’re teachers. Is it wrong to aim for Class A for the sake of the students?”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no way I can do that. Teachers holding back their students’ progress—”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To think to that extent, you… No, I suppose it’s natural… I can’t make any excuses.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “...Give her time...?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry I couldn’t be of more help, even though you confided in me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I couldn’t solve it immediately, but I deeply appreciate that you had the courage to tell me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That is… Ah, yes, but—”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You will change...? What are you talking about—”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You are—! Who are you really...”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Her grudge: Hoshinomiya vows she will never let Chabashira graduate her class from Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Mashima proposes giving Hoshinomiya time to think over spring break.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakagami<\/b> Sakagami threatens escalation if she acts.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y2v12_5-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.4: The Keyaki Mall gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p16-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira announces the transfer  ends the homeroom with a warning arrives pale with unfocused  lifeless eyes and does not respond to hirata or kikuchi  after a long silence she murmurs that she is fine   i m fine   there s something i need to tell all of you  this morning no  just a little while ago a certain student used their private points to exercise a certain right  or so it seems   the student who s absent from the classroom right now  ayanokouji  he s the one who exercised that right   class  transfer   i understand that what i m saying is hard to grasp  however  it s the truth   take out your phone and display the class oaa   ayanokouji has been transferred from this class to class c as of today  asked whether an illegal transfer could be canceled  the answer   that an illegal transfer could be canceled but the fraud committer would face severe punishment and  the arrows would also point at ayanokouji    is not speaker tagged in the translation  on subject matter it reads as chabashira s  but the attribution is not printed   y yes  that s right   let s end the homeroom period here  however  i ask that you don t take action against ayanokouji for the sake of blaming or criticizing him  currently  he hasn t done anything against the rules   that s right  avoid unnecessary contact with ayanokouji  and make sure not to get into trouble with other classes  if anything happens  make sure to go through me or the school  okay  uncharacteristically shattered   keeps glancing at her tablet and cannot give a straight explanation  students later realize how much they did not know about his standing in the class  delivers the news of his transfer  instructs the class not to blame or contact him  for rules and safety reasons  first to ask after her  he then echoes her warning about avoiding unnecessary contact  she signals to end the homeroom  chabashira agrees aloud  the print run leaves these pages without prose  blank","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira announces the transfer; ends the homeroom with a warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.16–28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives pale with unfocused, lifeless eyes and does not respond to Hirata or Kikuchi; after a long silence she murmurs that she is fine.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There&#x27;s something I need to tell all of you. This morning—no, just a little while ago—a certain student used their Private Points to exercise a certain right… or so it seems.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The student who&#x27;s absent from the classroom right now… Ayanokouji. He&#x27;s the one who exercised that right.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…Class… transfer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand that what I&#x27;m saying is hard to grasp. However… it&#x27;s the truth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Take out your phone and display the class OAA.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji has been transferred from this class to Class C as of today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asked whether an illegal transfer could be canceled, the answer — that an illegal transfer could be canceled but the fraud-committer would face severe punishment and &quot;the arrows would also point at Ayanokouji&quot; — is not speaker-tagged in the translation; on subject matter it reads as Chabashira&#x27;s, but the attribution is not printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…Y-Yes, that&#x27;s right.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s end the homeroom period here. However, I ask that you don&#x27;t take action against Ayanokouji for the sake of blaming or criticizing him. Currently, he hasn&#x27;t done anything against the rules.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s right. Avoid unnecessary contact with Ayanokouji, and make sure not to get into trouble with other classes. If anything happens, make sure to go through me or the school, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Uncharacteristically shattered — keeps glancing at her tablet and cannot give a straight explanation; students later realize how much they did not know about his standing in the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Delivers the news of his transfer; instructs the class not to blame or contact him, for rules and safety reasons.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> First to ask after her; he then echoes her warning about avoiding unnecessary contact.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She signals to end the homeroom; Chabashira agrees aloud.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The print run leaves these pages without prose (blank).<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p87-1\">→ After: Chabashira tails Ayanokōji; asks whether the transfer was on her account<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p87-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae chabashira tails ayanokoji  asks whether the transfer was on her account appears at the mall and pulls ayanokoji aside  she admits her colleagues had noticed him and that hoshinomiya s issue is resolved   come with me for a moment   i wanted to talk to you  as your homeroom teacher  no  as your former homeroom teacher  i thought it might be inappropriate to carelessly make contact  but i couldn t help wanting to check something   you noticed   that doesn t matter  what i want to hear about is the class transfer  the transfer matter  what were you thinking when you decided to transfer without telling anyone   isn t there something inconvenient  something that forced you to transfer   is it really because of me  because i was troubled with chie s problem  did you sacrifice yourself to solve it   what s the reason then  why do something so meaningless   it doesn t seem like you re simply being considerate   yes   understood  i see  sorry for taking your time  quietly relieved yet still chasing answers   stays calm in the open but visibly cannot accept losing him without knowing why  ayanokoji notes she might still share the talk with others  tails him from the dorm  he tells her the transfer was not on her account and that it was decided even before hoshinomiya s issue surfaced  her trouble is what chabashira feared had cost them ayanokoji  ayanokoji rates her tailing skills as on par with morishita s    and to put it nicely  they weren t good","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira tails Ayanokōji; asks whether the transfer was on her account<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.87–89<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears at the mall and pulls Ayanokōji aside; she admits her colleagues had noticed him and that Hoshinomiya&#x27;s issue is resolved.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Come with me for a moment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;…I wanted to talk to you. As your homeroom teacher… no, as your former homeroom teacher, I thought it might be inappropriate to carelessly make contact, but I couldn&#x27;t help wanting to check something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;…You noticed?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That doesn&#x27;t matter. What I want to hear about is the class transfer… the transfer matter. What were you thinking when you decided to transfer without telling anyone…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Isn&#x27;t there something inconvenient… something that forced you to transfer?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is it really because of me? Because I was troubled with Chie&#x27;s problem… Did you sacrifice yourself to solve it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What&#x27;s the reason then? Why do something so meaningless…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It doesn&#x27;t seem like you&#x27;re simply being considerate…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yes…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Understood. I see… sorry for taking your time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Quietly relieved yet still chasing answers — stays calm in the open but visibly cannot accept losing him without knowing why; Ayanokōji notes she might still share the talk with others.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Tails him from the dorm; he tells her the transfer was not on her account and that it was decided even before Hoshinomiya&#x27;s issue surfaced.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Her trouble is what Chabashira feared had cost them Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji rates her tailing skills as on par with Morishita&#x27;s — &quot;and to put it nicely, they weren&#x27;t good.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y3v1-p16-1\">← Before: Chabashira announces the transfer; ends the homeroom with a warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
